00:27:29,198 --> 00:27:33,956
但在之前，我们只是简单地把生成的节点都加到前沿里。这次我们要稍微聪明一点。
But before we just always added the resulting nodes to the frontier. We're going to be a little clever about it this time.

310
00:27:34,256 --> 00:27:42,148
只有当这些节点不在前沿中，且也不在已探索集合中时，我们才会把它们添加到前沿。
We're only going to add the nodes to the frontier if they aren't already in the frontier, and if they aren't already in the explored set.

311
00:27:42,862 --> 00:27:51,556
所以我们会同时检查前沿和已探索集合，确保该节点没在其中两个里，只要它不在，我们就把它加到前沿中，
So we'll check both the frontier and the explored set, make sure that the node isn't already in one of those two, and so long as it isn't, then we'll go ahead and add it to the frontier,

312
00:27:51,856 --> 00:27:52,740
否则就不加。
but not otherwise.

313
00:27:53,582 --> 00:27:59,204
这种改进后的方法最终能确保我们不会在两个节点之间来回跳跃。
And so that revised approach is ultimately what's going to help make sure that we don't go back and forth between two nodes.

314
00:28:00,430 --> 00:28:06,564
现在，我到目前为止略过的一个重点是这一步：从前沿中移除一个节点。
Now, the one point that I've kind of glossed over here so far is this step here, removing a node from the frontier.

315
00:28:06,766 --> 00:28:10,276
之前我只是随意选择，比如就随便拿出一个节点，到此结束。
Before I just chose arbitrarily, like let's just remove a node and that's it.

316
00:28:10,702 --> 00:28:17,316
但事实证明，我们如何决定构建前沿的结构、如何添加以及如何移除节点，其实非常重要。
But it turns out it's actually quite important how we decide to structure our frontier, how we add and how we remove our nodes.

317
00:28:17,806 --> 00:28:23,044
前沿是一个数据结构，我们需要决定按照什么顺序来移除元素。
The frontier is a data structure, and we need to make a choice about in what order are we going to be removing elements.

318
00:28:24,046 --> 00:28:28,772
而最简单的用于添加和移除元素的其中一种数据结构就是所谓的“栈”。
And one of the simplest data structures for adding and removing elements is something called a stack.

319
00:28:29,166 --> 00:28:40,484
栈是一种后进先出的数据结构，这意味着我最后添加到前沿的东西，将是第一个从前沿中被移除的东西。
And a stack is a data structure that is a last in, first out data type, which means the last thing that I add to the frontier is going to be the first thing that I remove from the frontier.

320
00:28:40,814 --> 00:28:46,884
所以在这种情况下，进入栈或前沿的最近的一个东西，就是我正在探索的那个节点。
So the most recent thing to go into the stack or the frontier in this case is going to be the node that I explore.

321
00:28:47,694 --> 00:28:55,236
那么让我们看看如果把这种基于栈的方法应用到类似这个问题时会发生什么：寻找从 A 到 E 的路径。
So let's see what happens if I apply this stack-based approach to something like this problem: finding a path from A to E.

322
00:28:55,854 --> 00:28:56,576
会发生什么呢？
What's going to happen?

323
00:28:56,782 --> 00:29:00,548
嗯，同样地，我们从 A 开始，然后说，好，让我们先看看 A。
Well, again, we'll start with A, and we'll say, all right, let's go ahead and look at A first.

324
00:29:00,910 --> 00:29:04,736
然后注意这次，我们将 A 添加到了已探索集合中。
And then notice this time, we've added A to the explored set.

325
00:29:05,006 --> 00:29:06,404
A 现在是我们已经探索过的内容。
A is something we've now explored.

326
00:29:06,576 --> 00:29:08,548
我们有这个数据结构来记录这些信息。
We have this data structure that's keeping track.

327
00:29:09,294 --> 00:29:11,396
然后我们说，从 A 出发，我们可以到达 B。
We then say from A, we can get to B.

328
00:29:12,014 --> 00:29:18,016
好的，那么从 B 开始，我们可以做什么？嗯，从 B 出发，我们可以探索 B 并到达 C 和 D。
And all right, from B, what can we do? Well, from B, we can explore B and get to both C and D.

329
00:29:18,222 --> 00:29:20,100
所以我们添加了 C，然后是 D。
So we added C and then D.

330
00:29:20,718 --> 00:29:26,148
所以现在，当我们探索一个节点时，我们将把前沿视为一个栈，即后进先出。
So now, when we explore a node, we're going to treat the frontier as a stack, last in, first out.

331
00:29:26,510 --> 00:29:29,696
D 是最后进入的，所以我们先去探索它
D was the last one to come in, so we'll go ahead and explore that

332
00:29:29,696 --> 00:29:32,256
接下来，我们问：从 D 可以到达哪里？
next and say, all right, where can we get to from D?

333
00:29:32,430 --> 00:29:33,316
嗯，我们可以到达 F。
Well, we can get to F.

334
00:29:34,158 --> 00:29:36,580
好的，那我们就去探索它，把 F 放入前沿。
And so, all right, we'll explore it, put F into the frontier.

335
00:29:37,166 --> 00:29:42,084
现在，因为前沿是一个栈，F 是栈中最新加入的元素。
And now, because the frontier is a stack, F is the most recent thing that's gone in the stack.

336
00:29:42,542 --> 00:29:43,908
所以 F 是我们接下来要探索的。
So F is what we'll explore next.

337
00:29:44,016 --> 00:29:47,044
我们去探索 F 并问：从 F 可以到达哪里？
We'll explore F and say, all right, where can we get to from F?

338
00:29:47,598 --> 00:29:50,116
嗯，我们无处可去，所以没有任何东西被添加到前沿。
Well, we can't get anywhere, so nothing gets added to the frontier.

339
00:29:50,798 --> 00:29:53,508
那么现在，新加入的前沿中最新的是什么？
So now what was the new most recent thing added to the frontier?

340
00:29:53,838 --> 00:29:56,068
嗯，现在是 C，它是前沿中剩下的唯一一个元素。
Well, it's now C, the only thing left in the frontier.

341
00:29:56,462 --> 00:30:04,868
我们去探索它，从中我们可以看到，从 C 可以到达 E，所以 E 进入前沿，然后我们说：好，看看 E，而 E 现在就是解
We'll explore that, from which we can see, all right, from C we can get to E, so E goes into the frontier, and then we say, all right, let's look at E, and E is now the solution,

342
00:30:05,070 --> 00:30:06,788
现在我们解决了这个问题。
and now we've solved the problem.

343
00:30:07,662 --> 00:30:13,380
所以当我们把前沿当作一个栈，即后进先出的数据结构时，这就是我们得到的结果。
So when we treat the frontier like a stack, a last in, first out data structure, that's the result we get.

344
00:30:13,646 --> 00:30:16,100
我们从 A 到 B 再到 D 最后到 F，
We go from A to B to D to F,

345
00:30:16,814 --> 00:30:23,216
然后我们有点回溯，向下走到 C 然后是 E。直观理解这个算法的工作原理非常重要。
and then we sort of backed up and went down to C and then E. And it's important to get a visual sense for how this algorithm is working.

346
00:30:23,376 --> 00:30:33,284
可以说，我们在搜索树中深入探索了很久，一直到最底部直到撞上死胡同。然后我们实际上是回溯并探索了之前没尝试过的另一条路线。
We went very deep in this search tree, so to speak, all the way until the bottom, where we hit a dead end. And then we effectively backed up and explored this other route that we didn't try before.

347
00:30:33,678 --> 00:30:42,020
这种在搜索树中深入探索的思路，也就是当我们使用栈时算法最终运作的方式，我们将这个版本的算法称为
And it's this going very deep in the search tree idea, this way the algorithm ends up working when we use a stack, that we call this version of the algorithm

348
00:30:42,350 --> 00:30:43,776
深度优先搜索。
depth first search.

349
00:30:44,206 --> 00:30:49,776
深度优先搜索是一种我们总是探索前沿中最深节点的搜索算法。
Depth first search is the search algorithm where we always explore the deepest node in the frontier.

350
00:30:49,998 --> 00:30:56,452
我们在搜索树中不断深入，如果遇到死胡同，我们就回溯并尝试别的东西。
We keep going deeper and deeper through our search tree, and then if we hit a dead end, we back up and we try something else instead.

351
00:30:57,710 --> 00:31:01,252
但深度优先搜索只是我们可以使用的几种搜索选项之一。
But depth for search is just one of the possible search options that we could use.

352
00:31:01,742 --> 00:31:08,676
事实证明，还有另一种叫广度优先搜索的算法，它的行为与深度优先搜索非常相似，只有一个区别。
It turns out that there's another algorithm called breadth first search, which behaves very similarly to depth for search, with one difference.

353
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:18,532
不同于深度优先搜索总是探索搜索树中最深的节点，广度优先搜索总是去探索前沿中最浅的节点。
Instead of always exploring the deepest node in the search tree, the way the depth for search does, breadth for search is always going to explore the shallowest node in the frontier.

354
00:31:19,310 --> 00:31:20,000
那这意味着什么呢？
So what does that mean?

355
00:31:20,238 --> 00:31:28,800
嗯，这意味着它不使用深度优先搜索或 DFS 所用的栈（即最新加入到前沿的元素是下一个要探索的）。
Well, it means that instead of using a stack, which depth for search or DFS used, where the most recent item added to the frontier is the one we'll explore.

356
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:40,640
在广度优先搜索或 BFS 中，我们改用队列。队列是一种先入先出的数据类型，意味着我们最先添加到前沿的东西就是第一个
next, in breadth for search, or BFS, we'll instead use a queue, where a queue is a first in, first out data type, where the very first thing we add to the frontier is the first one.

357
00:31:40,640 --> 00:31:48,132
我们要探索的。它们实际上形成了一个排队或队列，你越早进入前沿，就越早被探索。
we'll explore, and they effectively form a line or a queue, where the earlier you arrive in the frontier, the earlier you get explored.

358
00:31:49,198 --> 00:31:53,060
那么对于同一个问题，即寻找从 A 到 E 的路径，这意味着什么呢？
So what would that mean for the same exact problem, finding a path from A to E?

359
00:31:53,902 --> 00:31:55,524
嗯，我们还是从 A 开始。
Well, we start with A, same as before.

360
00:31:56,334 --> 00:31:59,200
然后我们继续探索 A 并问：从 A 可以到达哪里？
Then we'll go ahead and have explored A and say, where can we get to from A?

361
00:31:59,374 --> 00:32:01,760
嗯，从 A 出发我们可以到达 B，和之前一样。
Well, from A we can get to B, same as before.

362
00:32:02,094 --> 00:32:06,404
从 B 出发，同样如前所述，我们可以到达 C 和 D，所以 C 和 D 被添加到前沿中。
From B, same as before, we can get to C and D, so C and D get added to the frontier.

363
00:32:06,958 --> 00:32:11,908
不过这次我们先将 C 添加到前沿，而不是 D，所以我们会先探索 C。
This time though, we added C to the frontier before D, so we'll explore C first.

364
00:32:12,718 --> 00:32:13,828
于是 C 被探索了。
So C gets explored.

365
00:32:14,318 --> 00:32:15,908
那么从 C 出发，我们可以去哪？
And from C, where can we get to?

366
00:32:16,174 --> 00:32:17,092
嗯，我们可以到达 E。
Well, we can get to E.

367
00:32:17,518 --> 00:32:23,556
所以 E 被添加到前沿，但因为 D 在 E 之前被探索了，所以我们接下来会查看 D。
So E gets added to the frontier, but because D was explored before E, we'll look at D next.

368
00:32:24,302 --> 00:32:27,268
于是我们去探索 D 并思考：从 D 出发能到哪？我们可以到达 F。
So we'll explore D and say, where can we get to from D? We can get to F.

369
00:32:27,758 --> 00:32:30,788
直到那时我们才会说，好，现在我们可以到达 E 了。
And only then will we say, all right, now we can get to E.

370
00:32:31,598 --> 00:32:39,440
这就是广度优先搜索或 BFS 的做法：我们从这里开始，查看了 C 和 D，然后才去查看 E。
And so what breadth for search or BFS did is we started here, we looked at both C and D, and then we looked at E.

371
00:32:39,630 --> 00:32:48,160
实际上，我们是先看距离初始状态为 1 的点，再看距离为 2 的点，最后才看距离为 3 的点。
Effectively, we're looking at things one away from the initial state, then two away from the initial state, and only then things that are three away from the initial state.

372
00:32:48,366 --> 00:32:56,100
这与深度优先搜索不同，后者会一直深入到搜索树的可能最深处直到遇到死胡同，然后最终不得不回溯。
Unlike depth for search, which just went as deep as possible into the search tree until it hit a dead end, and then ultimately had to back up.

373
00:32:56,846 --> 00:33:01,668
所以现在我们有了两种可以用来尝试解决问题的不同搜索算法。
So these now are two different search algorithms that we could apply in order to try and solve a problem.

374
00:33:01,934 --> 00:33:07,492
让我们看看这些算法在实际操作中，比如在解迷宫时是如何运作的。
And let's take a look at how these would actually work in practice with something like maze solving, for example.

375
00:33:07,822 --> 00:33:09,200
这是一个迷宫的例子。
So here's an example of a maze.

376
00:33:09,360 --> 00:33:12,388
这些空白格子代表智能体可以移动的地方。
These empty cells represent places where our agent can move.

377
00:33:12,590 --> 00:33:16,880
这些深灰色的格子代表墙壁，智能体无法穿过。
These darkened gray cells represent walls that the agent can't pass through.

378
00:33:17,040 --> 00:33:26,532
最终，我们的智能体，也就是我们的 AI，将尝试通过一系列动作从位置 A 到达位置 B，这些动作包括向左、
And ultimately, our agent, our AI, is going to try to find a way to get from position A to position B via some sequence of actions, where those actions are left,

379
00:33:26,880 --> 00:33:28,132
向右、向上和向下。
right, up, and down.

380
00:33:28,942 --> 00:33:30,916
在这种情况下，深度优先搜索会怎么做？
What will depth first search do in this case?

381
00:33:31,406 --> 00:33:33,732
嗯，深度优先搜索只会遵循一条路径。
Well, depth first search will just follow one path.

382
00:33:34,222 --> 00:33:39,920
如果它到达一个有多个不同选择的岔路口，在这种情况下，深度优先搜索只会选择其中一个。
If it reaches a fork in the road where it has multiple different options, depth first search is just in this case going to choose one.

383
00:33:40,174 --> 00:33:41,252
它并没有真正的偏好。
It hasn't a real preference.

384
00:33:41,614 --> 00:33:44,548
但它会一直沿着这条路径走，直到撞上死胡
But it's going to keep following one until it hits a dead

385
00:33:45,230 --> 00:33:54,212
头。当它遇到死胡同时，深度优先搜索实际上会回到上一个决策点，并尝试另一条路径，彻底探索完这条路径。
end. And when it hits a dead end, depth first search effectively goes back to the last decision point and tries the other path, fully exhausting this entire path.

386
00:33:54,478 --> 00:33:58,468
当它意识到目标不在这里时，它会将注意力转向这条路径。
And when it realizes that, okay, the goal is not here, then it turns its attention to this path.

387
00:33:58,734 --> 00:34:00,240
它会尽可能深入下去。
It goes as deep as possible.

388
00:34:00,590 --> 00:34:04,228
当它撞到死胡同时，它会回溯，然后尝试这条其他的路径。
When it hits a dead end, it backs up and then tries this other path.

389
00:34:05,070 --> 00:34:10,724
在某一条特定的路径上一直深入探索，直到发现那是死胡同时，它就会回溯
Keeps going as deep as possible down one particular path, and when it realizes that that's a dead end, then it'll back up

390
00:34:11,406 --> 00:34:13,636
并最终找到通往目标的路。
and then ultimately find its way to the goal.

391
00:34:14,094 --> 00:34:20,560
也许你运气好，或者之前做出了不同的选择，但本质上深度优先搜索就是这样运行的。
And maybe you got lucky and maybe you made a different choice earlier on, but ultimately this is how depth first search is going to work.

392
00:34:20,686 --> 00:34:26,467
它会一直沿着路径走直到遇到死胡同，一旦遇到死胡同，它就会回退并寻找不同的路径。
It's going to keep following until it hits a dead end, and when it hits a dead end, it backs up and looks for a different solution.

393
00:34:26,989 --> 00:34:30,880
那么你可能会问一个合理的问题：这个算法总是有效的吗？
And so one thing you might reasonably ask is, is this algorithm always going to work?

394
00:34:31,040 --> 00:34:34,788
它真的总能找到从初始状态到目标状态的路径吗？
Will it always actually find a way to get from the initial state to the goal?

395
00:34:35,150 --> 00:34:44,547
事实是，只要我们的迷宫是有限的，只要可移动的空间数量是有限的，那么深度优先搜索就一定能找到解。
And it turns out that as long as our maze is finite, as long as there are only finitely many spaces where we can travel, then yes, depth first search is going to find a solution.

396
00:34:44,813 --> 00:34:46,947
因为它最终会遍历所有的路径。
Because eventually it'll just explore everything.

397
00:34:47,246 --> 00:34:54,000
如果迷宫是无限的，且状态空间也是无限的（这在某些特定类型的问题中确实存在），情况就会略有不同。
If the maze happens to be infinite and there's an infinite state space, which does exist in certain types of problems, then it's a slightly different story.

398
00:34:54,254 --> 00:34:58,084
但只要我们的迷宫格数有限，我们就一定能找到解。
But as long as our maze has finitely many squares, we're going to find a solution.

399
00:34:59,214 --> 00:35:02,820
然而，我们接下来要问的下一个问题是：它能找到一个好的解吗？
The next question, though, that we want to ask is: is it going to be a good solution?

400
00:35:03,022 --> 00:35:05,156
它能找到最优解吗？
Is it the optimal solution that we can find?

401
00:35:05,710 --> 00:35:07,908
答案是：不一定。
And the answer there is not necessarily.

402
00:35:08,206 --> 00:35:09,792
让我们来看一个例子。
And let's take a look at an example of that.

403
00:35:10,032 --> 00:35:14,436
在这个迷宫中，我们再次尝试从 A 点找到 B 点。
In this maze, for example, we're again trying to find our way from A to B.

404
00:35:14,862 --> 00:35:17,392
你会注意到这里有多个可能的解。
And you notice here there are multiple possible solutions.

405
00:35:17,552 --> 00:35:21,828
我们可以走这条路，也可以向上走，从而从 A 到达 B。
We could go this way or we could go up in order to make our way from A to B.

406
00:35:22,222 --> 00:35:25,892
如果我们运气好，深度优先搜索会选择这条路径并到达 B。
Now, if we're lucky, depth first search will choose this way and get to B.

407
00:35:26,126 --> 00:35:31,312
但并没有理由规定深度优先搜索必须在“向上”和“向右”之间做出特定选择。
But there's no reason necessarily why depth first search would choose between going up or going to the right.

408
00:35:31,438 --> 00:35:35,620
这是一个随机的决策点，因为这两个选项都会被添加到前沿中。
It's sort of an arbitrary decision point because both are going to be added to the frontier.

409
00:35:36,366 --> 00:35:43,140
最终，如果我们运气不好，深度优先搜索可能会先选择探索这条路径，因为此时这只是一个随机选择。
And ultimately, if we get unlucky, depth first search might choose to explore this path first, because it's just a random choice at this point.

410
00:35:43,406 --> 00:35:50,992
它会不断探索、探索、再探索，并最终找到这个目标——也就是这条路径，而实际上还有更好的路径。
It'll explore, explore, explore, and it'll eventually find the goal, this particular path, when in actuality there was a better path.

411
00:35:51,072 --> 00:35:59,332
如果我们将解的成本衡量为所需步数，那么原本存在一个更优的解，需要的步数更少。
There was a more optimal solution that used fewer steps, assuming we're measuring the cost of a solution based on the number of steps that we need to take.

412
00:35:59,854 --> 00:36:06,468
所以，深度优先搜索在运气不好的情况下，可能无法找到最优解，即使存在更好的解。
So, depth first search, if we're unlucky, might end up not finding the best solution when a better solution is available.

