01:17:07,024 --> 01:17:16,064
嗯，每当我们试图把人类关于玩游戏、赢和输这些概念转换给计算机时，我们希望用计算机能理解的术语来表达。
Well, anytime we try and translate this human concept of playing a game, winning and losing, to a computer, we want to translate it in terms that the computer can understand.

874
01:17:16,302 --> 01:17:19,300
而最终，计算机其实只理解数字。
And ultimately, the computer really just understands numbers.

875
01:17:19,822 --> 01:17:26,464
所以我们需要一种方法，把网格上的井字棋游戏转换成数值，变成计算机能理解的东西。
And so we want some way of translating a game of X's and O's on a grid to something numerical, something the computer can understand.

876
01:17:26,624 --> 01:17:33,764
电脑通常不理解赢或输的概念，但它理解更大和更小的概念。
The computer doesn't normally understand notions of win or lose, but it does understand the concept of bigger and smaller.

877
01:17:34,510 --> 01:17:42,948
所以我们可能会采取的做法是，把井字棋可能出现的每种情况都拿出来，并给每一种情况分配一个数值或效用
And so what we might do is we might take each of the possible ways that a tic-tac-toe game can unfold and assign a value or a utility

