So for example, I might want to calculate what is the probability that if I roll two dice, a red die and a blue die, what is the likelihood that A is a six or B is a six,

2829
04:21:10,222 --> 04:21:11,108
也就是其中任何一个成立的概率。
like one or the other.

2830
04:21:11,534 --> 04:21:20,512
你可能会想到的、但不是正确做法的方法是：好吧，红骰子出 6 的概率是 1/6，
And what you might imagine you could do, and the wrong way to approach it, would be just to say, all right, well, A comes up as a six with the red die comes up as a six with probability one

2831
04:21:21,518 --> 04:21:23,364
蓝骰子也是一样，也是 1/6。
The same for the blue die, it's also one over six.

2832
04:21:23,662 --> 04:21:26,596
把它们相加得到 2/6，也就是 1/3。
Add them together and you get two over six, otherwise known as one third.

2833
04:21:26,990 --> 04:21:35,396
呃，但这存在重复计算的问题，因为我们把 A 和 B 同时成立的情况——也就是红骰子和蓝骰子都出 6 的情况——
Uh but this suffers from a problem of overcounting, that we've double counted the case where both a and b, both the red die and the blue die,

2834
04:21:35,632 --> 04:21:39,072
重复计算了两次。
both come up as a six rule. And I've counted that instance twice.

2835
04:21:39,470 --> 04:21:47,472
为了解决这个问题，计算 A 或 B 的概率的实际表达式是使用我们所谓的“容斥原理”。
So to resolve this, the actual expression for calculating the probability of A or B uses what we call the inclusion-exclusion formula.

2836
04:21:47,726 --> 04:21:56,032
所以我取 A 的概率，加上 B 的概率，这部分和之前一样，但接着我需要减去那些被重复计算的情况。
So I take the probability of A, add it to the probability of B, that's all same as before, but then I need to exclude the cases that I've double counted.

2837
04:21:56,112 --> 04:21:57,380
所以我要从中减去
So I subtract from that

2838
04:21:58,062 --> 04:22:00,672
A 和 B 同时成立的概率。
the probability of A and B.

2839
04:22:01,198 --> 04:22:03,072
这样我就能得到 A 或 B 的结果。
And that gets me the result for A or B.

2840
04:22:03,152 --> 04:22:06,752
我考虑所有 A 为真的情况，以及所有 B 为真的情况。
I consider all the cases where A is true and all the cases where B is true.

2841
04:22:06,958 --> 04:22:15,792
如果你把这想象成一个韦恩图，其中一部分是 A 为真，另一部分是 B 为真，我只需要减去中间的部分，来消除那些在两个独立表达式中都被计入的重复项。
And if you imagine this is like a Venn diagram of cases where A is true, cases where B is true, I just need to subtract out the middle to get rid of the cases that I have overcounted by double

2842
04:22:15,872 --> 04:22:19,620
它们在两个单独的表达式里都被计算了一次。
counting them inside of both of these individual expressions.

2843
04:22:20,992 --> 04:22:25,028
另一个非常有用的规则是叫做“边缘化”的规则。
one other rule that's going to be quite helpful is a rule called marginalization.

2844
04:22:25,422 --> 04:22:33,348
所谓边缘化，就是回答这样一个问题：如何利用我可能掌握的其他变量（比如 B）来计算 A 的概率。
So marginalization is answering the question of how do I figure out the probability of A using some other variable that I might have access to, like B.

2845
04:22:33,582 --> 04:22:42,192
即使我不了解关于它的额外信息，我也知道 B 这个事件可以有两种可能的状态：要么 B 发生，要么 B 不发生，
Even if I don't know additional information about it, I know that B, some event, can have two possible states, either B happens or B doesn't happen,

2846
04:22:42,446 --> 04:22:44,036
假设它是一个布尔值，即真或假。
assuming it's a Boolean, true or false.

2847
04:22:44,686 --> 04:22:50,592
那么这意味着，为了让我能够计算 A 的概率，只有两种情况。
And well, what that means is that for me to be able to calculate the probability of A, there are only two cases.

2848
04:22:50,752 --> 04:22:55,472
要么 A 发生且 B 也发生，或者 A 发生但 B 不发生。
Either A happens and B happens, or A happens and B doesn't happen.

2849
04:22:55,552 --> 04:23:00,804
而这两者是互斥的，意味着它们不能同时发生；要么 B 发生，要么 B 不发生。
And those are two disjoint, meaning they can't both happen together, either B happens or B doesn't happen.

2850
04:23:01,134 --> 04:23:02,980
它们是互斥的或独立的两种情况。
They're disjoint or separate cases.

2851
04:23:03,246 --> 04:23:07,712
这样我就能通过把这两个情况相加，来计算出 A 的概率。
And so I can figure out the probability of A just by adding up those two cases.

2852
04:23:07,886 --> 04:23:16,068
A 为真的概率等于「A 与 B 为真」的概率加上「A 为真且 B 不为真」的概率。
The probability that A is true is the probability that A and B is true, plus the probability that A is true and B isn't true.

2853
04:23:16,462 --> 04:23:23,364
所以通过边缘化，我考虑了可能发生的两种情况。要么 B 发生，要么 B 不发生。
So by marginalizing, I've looked at the two possible cases that might take place. Either B happens or B doesn't happen.

2854
04:23:23,726 --> 04:23:26,992
而在这两种情况下，我都去查看 A 发生的概率是多少。
And in either of those cases, I look at what's the probability that A happens.

2855
04:23:27,214 --> 04:23:31,524
如果把它们相加，我就能得到 A 发生的整体概率。
And if I add those together, well then I get the probability that A happens as a whole.

2856
04:23:32,366 --> 04:23:33,552
所以来看看这个规则。
So take a look at that rule.

2857
04:23:33,632 --> 04:23:41,860
无论 B 是什么或者它与 A 有什么关系，只要我知道这些联合分布，我就能算出 A 的总概率。
It doesn't matter what B is or how it's related to A, so long as I know these joint distributions, I can figure out the overall probability of A.

2858
04:23:42,062 --> 04:23:51,072
如果我有一个联合分布，比如 A 和 B 的联合分布，这种方法就很有用，可以用来计算某些无条件概率，比如 A 的概率。
And this can be a useful way if I have a joint distribution, like the joint distribution of A and B, to just figure out some unconditional probability, like the probability of A,

2859
