乘以没有轨道维护的概率
rain multiplied by the probability of no track maintenance.

3038
04:41:30,574 --> 04:41:39,396
在已知有小雨的情况下，再乘以在已知有小雨且无轨道维护的情况下，列车延误的概率，因为列车是准点还是延误
given light rain multiplied by the probability of a delayed train given light rain and no track maintenance, because whether the train is on time or delayed

3039
04:41:39,760 --> 04:41:42,560
取决于这两个变量中的任何一个。
is dependent upon both of these other two variables.

3040
04:41:42,766 --> 04:41:48,228
因此，我有两项证据进入到这个条件概率的计算中。
And so I have two pieces of evidence that go into the calculation of that conditional probability.

3041
04:41:48,462 --> 04:41:58,400
而这三个值中的每一个，都只是我可以从我的贝叶斯网络中编码的各个独立概率分布中查到的数值。
And each of these three values is just a value that I can look up by looking at one of these individual probability distributions that is encoded into my Bayesian

3042
04:41:58,560 --> 04:41:59,200
网络。
network.

3043
04:41:59,726 --> 04:42:09,316
如果我想要所有四个变量的联合概率，比如“小雨、无轨道维护、列车延误且错过预约”的概率，
And if I wanted a joint probability over all four of the variables, something like the probability of light rain and no track maintenance and a delayed train and I miss my appointment,

3044
04:42:09,742 --> 04:42:14,240
那么这就意味着要乘以四个不同的值，每个值来自这些独立节点中的一个。
well that's going to be multiplying four different values, one from each of these individual nodes.

3045
04:42:14,478 --> 04:42:22,340
它将是小雨的概率，接着是已知有小雨时无轨道维护的概率，然后是已知有小雨且无轨道维护时列车延误的概率。
It's going to be the probability of light rain, then of no track maintenance given light rain, then of a delayed train given light rain and no track maintenance.

3046
04:42:22,670 --> 04:42:31,840
最后，对于这里的这个节点，即我是否能赶上预约，它并不依赖于这两个变量，而是取决于我知道列车是否准点。
And then finally, for this node here, for whether I make it to my appointment or not, it's not dependent upon these two variables given that I know whether or not the train is on time.

3047
04:42:31,920 --> 04:42:39,760
我只需要关心在已知列车延误的情况下，我错过列车或错过预约的条件概率。
I only need to care about the conditional probability that I miss my train, or that I miss my appointment, given that the train happens to be delayed.

3048
04:42:39,840 --> 04:42:47,908
因此，这里用四个概率来表示，每一个概率都位于这些节点各自的概率分布中，
And so that's represented here by four probabilities, each of which is located inside of one of these probability distributions for each of the nodes,

3049
04:42:48,320 --> 04:42:49,988
全部相乘。
all multiplied together.

3050
04:42:50,734 --> 04:42:58,948
因此，我可以取这样一个变量，通过将贝叶斯网络中的一系列独立概率相乘来计算出联合概率。
And so I can take a variable like that and figure out what the joint probability is by multiplying a whole bunch of these individual probabilities from the Bayesian network.

3051
04:42:59,630 --> 04:43:07,908
但当然，就像上次一样，我们真正想做的是获取新的信息，在这里，这也是我们希望在贝叶斯网络中实现的目标。
But of course, just as with last time, where what I really wanted to do was to be able to get new pieces of information, here too, this is what we're going to want to do with our Bayesian network.

3052
04:43:08,240 --> 04:43:11,204
在知识的语境下，我们讨论过推理问题。
In the context of knowledge, we talked about the problem of inference.

3053
04:43:11,440 --> 04:43:19,440
给定我已知为真的事物，我能否推断出关于世界其他事实的结论，而这些事实我也知道是真实的？
Given things that I know to be true, can I draw conclusions, make deductions about other facts about the world that I also know to be true?

3054
04:43:19,854 --> 04:43:23,652
而我们现在要做的是将同样的理念应用到概率上。
And what we're going to do now is apply the same sort of idea to probability.

3055
04:43:23,840 --> 04:43:31,780
利用我掌握的一些信息，无论是某些证据还是某些概率，我是否能确定其他变量的结论，
Using information about which I have some knowledge, whether some evidence or some probabilities, can I figure out not other variables for certain,

3056
04:43:32,014 --> 04:43:36,640
或者说，我是否能计算出其他变量取特定值的概率？
but can I figure out the probabilities of other variables taking on particular values?

3057
04:43:36,800 --> 04:43:44,640
因此，我们在这里引入了在概率设定下的推理问题，即在变量不一定确定为真，
And so here we introduce the problem of inference in a probabilistic setting, in a case where variables might not necessarily be true for sure,

3058
04:43:44,910 --> 04:43:49,380
而是以某种概率取不同值的随机变量的情况。
but they might be random variables that take on different values with some probability.

3059
04:43:50,158 --> 04:43:53,700
那么，我们如何正式定义这个推理问题究竟是什么？
So how do we formally define what exactly this inference problem actually is?

3060
04:43:54,126 --> 04:43:56,548
嗯，推理问题包含几个部分。
Well, the inference problem has a couple of parts to it.

3061
04:43:56,974 --> 04:44:01,280
我们有一些查询，也就是一些我们想要计算概率分布的变量 x。
We have some query, some variable x that we want to compute the distribution for.

3062
04:44:01,440 --> 04:44:06,276
也许我想知道错过列车的概率，或者我想知道
Maybe I want the probability that I miss my train, or I want the probability that

3063
04:44:07,200 --> 04:44:10,400
是否存在轨道维护，这是我想要获取信息的内容。
there is track maintenance, something that I want information about.

3064
04:44:11,150 --> 04:44:13,088
然后我还有一些证据变量。
And then I have some evidence variables.

3065
04:44:13,168 --> 04:44:19,652
可能只有一项证据，也可能是多项证据，但我已经观测到了某些事件相关的特定变量。
Maybe it's just one piece of evidence, maybe it's multiple pieces of evidence, but I've observed certain variables for some sort of event.

3066
04:44:20,238 --> 04:44:23,332
例如，我可能观察到正在下雨。
So for example, I might have observed that it is raining.

3067
04:44:23,488 --> 04:44:24,528
这就是我拥有的证据。
This is evidence that I have.

3068
04:44:24,688 --> 04:44:33,540
我知道是小雨，或者我知道是大雨，这些都是我拥有的证据，利用这些证据，我想知道列车延误的概率是多少，
I know that there is light rain, or I know that there is heavy rain, and that is evidence I have, and using that evidence, I want to know what is the probability that my train is delayed,

3069
04:44:33,728 --> 04:44:34,244
举个例子。
for example.

3070
04:44:34,894 --> 04:44:37,968
这就是我基于这些证据可能提出的查询。
And that is a query that I might want to ask based on this evidence.

3071
04:44:38,126 --> 04:44:43,844
所以我有查询、某些变量，以及在我的 Bayesian network 中观测到的其他变量作为证据。
So I have a query, some variable, evidence, which are some other variables that I have observed inside of my Bayesian network.

3072
04:44:44,206 --> 04:44:46,848
当然，这还留下了一些隐藏变量。
And of course, that does leave some hidden variables.

3073
04:44:47,088 --> 04:44:47,428
为什么？
Why?

3074
04:44:47,728 --> 04:44:51,780
这些是既不是证据变量也不是查询变量的变量。
These are variables that are not evidence variables and not query variables.

3075
04:44:52,206 --> 04:45:01,956
你可以想象一下，在我知道是否下雨，并想知道列车是否会延误的情况下，隐藏变量，也就是我无法获取的信息，
So you might imagine in the case where I know whether or not it's raining, and I want to know whether my train is going to be delayed or not, the hidden variable, the thing I don't have access to,

3076
04:45:02,158 --> 04:45:04,196
是类似“轨道上是否有维护”这样的内容。
is something like is there maintenance on the track?

3077
04:45:04,494 --> 04:45:06,756
或者比如，“我是否能按时到达预约地点”？
Or am I going to make or not make my appointment, for example?

3078
04:45:06,928 --> 04:45:09,008
这些是我无法获取的变量。
These are variables that I don't have access to.

3079
04:45:09,088 --> 04:45:14,340
它们是隐藏的，因为它们不是我观察到的内容，也不是我正在询问的查询。
They're hidden, because they're not things I observed, and they're also not the query, the thing that I'm asking.

3080
04:45:14,702 --> 04:45:22,528
所以最终我们要计算的是：给定我观察到的事件 e，我想知道 x 的概率分布。
And so ultimately what we want to calculate is I want to know the probability distribution of x given e, the event that I observe.

3081
04:45:22,608 --> 04:45:31,968
也就是说，既然我观察到了一些事件，比如我看到在下雨，我想知道列车这个随机变量在所有可能取值上的分布。它是准时的吗？
So given that I observe some event, I observe that it is raining, I would like to know what is the distribution over the possible values of the train random variable. Is it on time?

3082
04:45:32,302 --> 04:45:32,848
它是延误的吗？
Is it delayed?

3083
04:45:33,070 --> 04:45:34,916
它到场的可能性是多少？
What's the likelihood it's going to be there?

3084
04:45:35,342 --> 04:45:41,888
结果发现，我们只需利用之前见过的许多概率规则就能完成这个计算。
And it turns out we can do this calculation just using a lot of the probability rules that we've already seen in action.

3085
04:45:42,030 --> 04:45:46,608
最终，我们将从较高层次、抽象的层面来审视这些数学原理，
And ultimately, we're going to take a look at the math at a little bit of a high level, at an abstract level,

3086
04:45:46,798 --> 04:45:52,128
但最终我们可以让计算机和现有的编程库来帮我们完成一部分数学计算。
but ultimately we can allow computers and programming libraries that already exist to begin to do some of this math for us.

3087
04:45:52,238 --> 04:45:56,868
不过，了解这个推理过程发生时到底发生了什么，还是很有必要的。
But it's good to get a general sense for what's actually happening when this inference process takes place.

3088
04:45:57,582 --> 04:46:06,788
举个例子，假设我想计算在某些证据下、即已知有小雨的情况下，预约这个随机变量的概率分布，
Let's imagine, for example, that I want to compute the probability distribution of the appointment random variable given some evidence, given that I know that there was light rain

3089
04:46:07,168 --> 04:46:08,452
并且没有轨道维护。
and no track maintenance.

3090
04:46:08,942 --> 04:46:12,164
这就是我的证据，就是这两个我观测到数值的变量。
So there's my evidence, these two variables that I observe the values of.

3091
04:46:12,448 --> 04:46:18,148
我观察到降雨的数值，我知道有小雨，并且我知道今天没有轨道维护。
I observe the value of rain, I know there's light rain, and I know that there is no track maintenance going on today.

3092
04:46:18,446 --> 04:46:22,368
而我关心的、也就是我的查询内容，是这个随机变量：预约。
And what I care about knowing, my query, is this random variable, appointment.

3093
04:46:22,528 --> 04:46:31,300
我想知道这个随机变量“预约”的分布，比如在给定这些证据的情况下，我能按时参加预约的概率是多少，或者错过预约的概率是多少。
I want to know the distribution of this random variable appointment, like what is the chance that I'm able to attend my appointment, what is the chance that I miss my appointment given this evidence.

3094
04:46:31,950 --> 04:46:36,676
而隐藏变量，也就是我无法获取信息的部分，是这个变量：列车。
And the hidden variable, the information that I don't have access to, is this variable train.

3095
04:46:36,848 --> 04:46:43,652
这是不属于我所见证据的信息，不是我观察到的内容，但它也不是我要求的查询项。
This is information that is not part of the evidence that I see, not something that I observe, but it is also not the query that I'm asking for.

3096
04:46:44,526 --> 04:46:52,516
那么这个推理过程看起来会是什么样呢？如果你还记得我们定义条件概率并进行相关计算时的情况，
And so what might this inference procedure look like? Well, if you recall back from when we were defining conditional probability and doing math with conditional probabilities,

3097
04:46:52,878 --> 04:46:58,212
我们知道条件概率与联合概率成比例。
we know that a conditional probability is proportional to the joint probability.

3098
04:46:58,638 --> 04:47:07,248
我们通过回顾这一点来记住：给定 b 的概率只是某个常数因子 alpha 乘以 a 和 b 的概率。
And we remember this by recalling that the probability of a given b is just some constant factor alpha multiplied by the probability of a and b.

3099
04:47:07,502 --> 04:47:16,288
这个常数因子 alpha 实际上就是除以 b 的概率，但重要的是它只是一个常数乘以联合分布，
That constant factor alpha turns out to be like dividing over the probability of b, but the important thing is that it's just some constant multiplied by the joint distribution,

3100
04:47:16,494 --> 04:47:19,012
也就是所有这些个体事件同时发生的概率。
the probability that all of these individual things happen.

3101
04:47:19,630 --> 04:47:28,928
所以在这种情况下，我可以把“给定小雨且无轨道维护”的预约随机变量的概率，说成是成比例的。
So in this case, I can take the probability of the appointment random variable given light rain and no track maintenance, and say that is just going to be proportional.

3102
04:47:29,198 --> 04:47:37,092
即某个常数 alpha 乘以联合概率，也就是特定预约随机变量值、小雨、
some constant alpha, multiplied by the joint probability, the probability of a particular value for the appointment, random variable and light rain,

3103
04:47:37,568 --> 04:47:39,488
以及无轨道维护的联合概率。
and no track maintenance.

3104
04:47:39,982 --> 04:47:46,884
好，那么当我真正关心的是了解……
Well, all right, how do I calculate this probability of appointment and light rain and no track maintenance when what I really care about is knowing like

3105
04:47:47,088 --> 04:47:55,328
我需要这四个值中的全部，才能计算出涵盖所有内容的联合分布，因为特定的预约取决于列车的状态。
I need all four of these values to be able to calculate a joint distribution across everything, because in a particular appointment depends upon the value of train.

3106
04:47:56,014 --> 04:47:59,652
为了做到这一点，这里我可以开始使用边缘化技巧。
Well, in order to do that, here I can begin to use that marginalization trick.

3107
04:48:00,000 --> 04:48:05,156
即：获取“预约、小雨、无轨道维护”任何一种配置只有两种可能的方法。
That there are only two ways I can get any configuration of an appointment, light rain, and no track maintenance.

3108
04:48:05,520 --> 04:48:13,760
要么是这种特定的变量组合发生且列车准点，要么是这种特定的变量组合发生且列车延误。
Either this particular setting of variables happens and the train is on time, or this particular setting of variables happens and the train is delayed.

3109
04:48:13,920 --> 04:48:16,880
这是我需要考虑的两种可能情况。
Those are two possible cases that I would want to consider.

3110
04:48:17,134 --> 04:48:26,468
如果把这两种情况相加，那么我就能通过把隐藏变量（如果有多个的话）的所有可能性全部相加来得到结果。
And if I add those two cases up, well then I get the result just by adding up all of the possibilities for the hidden variable, or variables if there are multiple.

3111
04:48:26,640 --> 04:48:35,076
但因为这里只有一个隐藏变量“列车”，我只需要遍历该隐藏变量所有可能的值并累加它们的概率。
But since there's only one hidden variable here, train, all I need to do is iterate over all the possible values for that hidden variable train and add up their probabilities.

3112
04:48:36,046 --> 04:48:46,560
所以这里的概率表达式变成了：预约、小雨、无维护且列车准点的概率分布，以及
So this probability expression here becomes probability distribution over appointment, light, no rain, and train is on time, and the probability distribution over the appointment,

3113
04:48:46,720 --> 04:48:51,040
例如：预约、小雨、无维护且列车延误的概率分布。
light rain, no track maintenance, and that the train is delayed, for example.

3114
04:48:51,246 --> 04:48:54,916
所以我把“列车”的两个可能值都取出来，然后将它们相加。
So I take both of the possible values for train, go ahead and add them up.

3115
04:48:55,246 --> 04:49:02,916
这些只是我们之前见过的联合概率，只需向上寻找父节点、再向上……计算出那些概率并相乘即可。
These are just joint probabilities that we saw earlier how to calculate just by going parent, parent, parent, parent, and calculating those probabilities and multiplying them together,

3116
04:49:03,246 --> 04:49:08,740
最后你还需要对它们进行归一化，从宏观上来说，是为了确保所有项相加等于 1。
and then you'll need to normalize them at the end, speaking at a high level to make sure that everything adds up to the number one.

3117
04:49:09,486 --> 04:49:16,080
这种被称为“枚举推理”的过程中的公式看起来有点复杂，但最终它长这样。
So the formula for how you do this in a process known as inference by enumeration looks a little bit complicated, but ultimately it looks like this.

3118
04:49:16,206 --> 04:49:19,840
现在让我们试着理清这些符号到底代表什么意思。
And let's now try to distill what it is that all of these symbols actually mean.

3119
04:49:20,014 --> 04:49:20,720
从这里开始。
Let's start here.

3120
04:49:21,006 --> 04:49:27,204
我关心的内容是：在给定某些证据的情况下，我的查询变量 x 的概率。
What I care about knowing is the probability of x, my query variable, given some sort of evidence.

3121
04:49:27,982 --> 04:49:29,840
关于条件概率，我了解到了什么？
What do I know about conditional probabilities?

3122
04:49:30,030 --> 04:49:34,320
嗯，条件概率与联合概率成正比。
Well, a conditional probability is proportional to the joint probability.

3123
04:49:34,670 --> 04:49:40,740
也就是说，它是某个常数（归一化常数）乘以这个关于 x 和证据的联合概率。
So it's some alpha, some normalizing constant, multiplied by this joint probability of x and evidence.

3124
04:49:41,454 --> 04:49:42,640
那我该如何计算它呢？
And how do I calculate that?

3125
04:49:42,926 --> 04:49:49,840
为了做到这一点，我将对所有隐藏变量进行边缘化，即对那些我无法直接观测到数值的所有变量进行处理。
Well, to do that, I'm going to marginalize over all of the hidden variables, all the variables that I don't directly observe the values for.

3126
04:49:50,000 --> 04:49:55,280
基本上就是遍历所有可能发生的情况，然后把它们全部加起来。
I'm basically going to iterate over all of the possibilities that it could happen and just sum them all up.

3127
04:49:55,534 --> 04:50:02,884
因此我可以将其转换为对所有 y 的求和，y 涵盖了所有可能的隐藏变量及其可能取到的值，
And so I can translate this into a sum over all y, which ranges over all the possible hidden variables and the values that they could take on,

3128
04:50:03,822 --> 04:50:07,556
并把所有这些可能的个体概率累加起来。
and adds up all of those possible individual probabilities.

3129
04:50:07,918 --> 04:50:11,652
这将允许我执行这种“枚举推理”的过程。
And that is going to allow me to do this process of inference by enumeration.

3130
04:50:12,206 --> 04:50:19,440
当然，如果人类非得自己去计算所有的数学公式，那确实挺麻烦的，但事实证明，这正是计算机和 AI 能提供极大帮助的地方。
Now ultimately it's pretty annoying if we as humans have to do all of this math for ourselves, but turns out this is where computers and AI can be particularly helpful,

3131
04:50:19,520 --> 04:50:26,820
我们可以编写程序让计算机理解贝叶斯网络，从而能够理解这些推理过程并完成这些计算。
that we can program a computer to understand a Bayesian network, to be able to understand these inference procedures, and to be able to do these calculations.

3132
04:50:27,150 --> 04:50:31,556
利用你在这里看到的这些信息，你自己就可以从头开始实现一个贝叶斯网络。
And using the information you've seen here, you could implement a Bayesian network from scratch yourself.

3133
04:50:31,758 --> 04:50:38,160
但事实是，有很多库（尤其是用 Python 编写的）可以让我们更轻松地进行这种概率推理。
but turns out there are a lot of libraries, especially written in Python, that allow us to make it easier to do this sort of probabilistic inference,

3134
04:50:38,414 --> 04:50:44,240
这些库能让我们处理贝叶斯网络并进行此类计算，这样你就没必要去理解所有底层的数学原理了。
to be able to take a Bayesian network and do these sorts of calculations, so that you don't need to know and understand all of the underlying math.

3135
04:50:44,462 --> 04:50:46,500
不过，对其工作原理有一个大致的了解还是很有帮助的。
Though it's helpful to have a general sense for how it works.

