3762
05:51:19,712 --> 05:51:26,832
即使你允许自己移动到其中一个邻居，也不清楚最终会选择哪一个，而且你也可能卡在这里。
And even if you allowed yourself to move to one of the neighbors, it wouldn't be clear which neighbor you would ultimately move to, and you could get stuck here as well.

3763
05:51:27,246 --> 05:51:28,352
这里还有一个。
And there's another one over here.

3764
05:51:28,590 --> 05:51:34,992
这个被称为“肩部”。它并不是真正的局部最大值，因为仍有地方可以更高；也不是局部最小值，因为我们还可以更低。
This one is called a shoulder. It's not really a local maximum because there's still places where we can go higher, not a local minimum because we can go lower.

3765
05:51:35,246 --> 05:51:42,592
所以我们仍然可以取得进展，但它仍然是一个平坦区域，如果你使用局部搜索算法，可能会在这里迷失方向，
So we can still make progress, but it's still this flat area where if you have a local search algorithm, there's potential to get lost here,

3766
05:51:42,798 --> 05:51:47,780
根据我们是想最大化还是最小化，可能无法做出向上或向下的进展，
unable to make some upward or downward progress depending on whether we're trying to maximize or minimize,

3767
05:51:48,014 --> 05:51:54,180
因此还有另一种可能，就是我们找到的解可能并不是真正的最优解。
and therefore another potential for us to be able to find a solution that might not actually be the optimal solution.

3768
05:51:54,926 --> 05:52:00,164
正是因为这种可能性，即爬山算法不一定总能带给我们最优结果的风险，
And so, because of this potential, the potential that hill climbing has to not always find us the optimal result,

3769
05:52:00,464 --> 05:52:08,452
事实证明，有许多不同种类和变体的爬山算法，可以根据具体情况更好地解决问题。
it turns out there are a number of different varieties and variations on the hill climbing algorithm that help to solve the problem better depending on the context.

3770
05:52:08,544 --> 05:52:12,864
并且根据问题的特定类型，其中一些变体可能比其他的更适用。
And depending on the specific type of problem, some of these variants might be more applicable than others.

3771
05:52:13,198 --> 05:52:18,820
到目前为止我们看的是一种通常被称为“最速上升爬山算法”的版本，
What we've taken a look at so far is a version of hill climbing generally called steepest ascent hill climbing,

3772
05:52:19,246 --> 05:52:27,104
其中最速上升爬山算法的思路是：在我们要最大化的情况下选择数值最高的邻居，或者在我们要最小化的情况下选择数值最低的邻居。
where the idea of steepest ascent hill climbing is we are going to choose the highest valued neighbor in the case where we're trying to maximize or the lowest valued neighbor

3773
05:52:27,278 --> 05:52:28,624
在我们需要最小化的情况下。
in cases where we're trying to minimize.

3774
05:52:28,784 --> 05:52:35,584
但总的来说，如果我有五个邻居且它们都比我当前的状态更好，我会选择这五个中最好的那个。
But generally speaking, if I have five neighbors and they're all better than my current state, I will pick the best one of those five.

3775
05:52:35,950 --> 05:52:41,828
现在，有时这可能会运行得很好。这是一种贪婪策略，即试图在任何特定时间步采取最好的操作。
Now, sometimes that might work pretty well. It's sort of a greedy approach of trying to take the best operation at any particular time step.

3776
05:52:42,254 --> 05:52:43,264
但它并不总是奏效。
But it might not always work.

3777
05:52:43,344 --> 05:52:51,812
有些情况下，我可能想选择一个比我好一点、但不是最好的选项，因为这在后续可能会带来更好的结果。
There might be cases where actually I want to choose an option that is slightly better than me, but maybe not the best one, because that later on might lead to a better outcome ultimately.

3778
05:52:52,078 --> 05:52:55,780
所以我们还可以考虑这种基础爬山算法的其他变体。
So there are other variants that we might consider of this basic hill climbing algorithm.

3779
05:52:56,430 --> 05:52:58,244
其中一种被称为“随机爬山算法”。
One is known as stochastic hill climbing.

3780
05:52:58,510 --> 05:53:02,064
在这种情况下，我们从所有数值更高的邻居中随机选择一个。
And in this case, we choose randomly from all of our higher value neighbors.

3781
05:53:02,222 --> 05:53:08,932
如果我处于当前状态，且有五个邻居都比我好，而不是像最陡上升爬山算法那样只选择最好的一个，
So if I'm at my current state and there are five neighbors that are all better than I am, rather than choosing the best one, as steep as descent would do,

3782
05:53:09,230 --> 05:53:15,844
随机爬山算法会从这些更好的邻居中随机选一个，它认为只要更好就是好，而且可能有向前进展的潜力，
stochastic will just choose randomly from one of them, thinking that if it's better, then it's better, and maybe there's a potential to make forward progress,

3783
05:53:16,078 --> 05:53:19,584
即使它不是我能选择的所有选项中局部最好的那个。
even if it is not locally the best option I could possibly

3784
05:53:19,584 --> 05:53:26,864
首选爬山算法则是只选择它遇到的第一个高价值邻居，遵循类似的逻辑。
choose. First choice hill climbing ends up just choosing the very first highest valued neighbor that it follows, behaving on a similar idea.

3785
05:53:27,054 --> 05:53:32,704
与其考虑所有的邻居，我们只要找到一个比当前状态更好的邻居，就直接移动到那里。
Rather than consider all of the neighbors, as soon as we find a neighbor that is better than our current state, we'll go ahead and move there.

3786
05:53:33,006 --> 05:53:39,556
这样可能有一些效率上的提升，并且有可能找到其他策略无法找到的解。
So maybe some efficiency improvements there, and maybe has the potential to find a solution that the other strategies weren't able to find.

3787
05:53:39,886 --> 05:53:43,620
尽管有这些变体，我们仍然面临同样的潜在风险。
And with all of these variants, we still suffer from the same potential risk.

3788
05:53:43,824 --> 05:53:47,620
就是我们可能会陷入局部最小值或局部最大值。
This risk that we might end up at a local minimum or a local maximum.

3789
05:53:48,078 --> 05:53:51,556
我们可以通过多次重复这个过程来降低这种风险。
And we can reduce that risk by repeating the process multiple times.

3790
05:53:52,078 --> 05:53:59,396
爬山算法的一个变体是随机重启爬山，其核心思想是进行多次爬山操作。
So one variant of hill climbing is random restart hill climbing, where the general idea is we'll conduct hill climbing multiple times.

3791
05:53:59,822 --> 05:54:05,744
例如，如果我们应用最陡上升爬山算法，我们会从一个随机状态开始，尝试解决问题，
If we apply steepest ascent hill climbing, for example, we'll start at some random state, try and figure out how to solve the problem,

3792
05:54:05,824 --> 05:54:11,584
找出我们到达的局部最大值或最小值，然后随机重启并再次尝试。
and figure out what is the local maximum or local minimum we get to, and then we'll just randomly restart and try again.

3793
05:54:11,744 --> 05:54:19,744
选择一个新的初始配置，找出局部的最大值或最小值，重复若干次，在完成多次尝试后，
Choose a new starting configuration, try and figure out what the local maximum or minimum is, and do this some number of times, and then after we've done it some number of times,

3794
05:54:19,918 --> 05:54:22,788
我们可以从所有尝试过的结果中选出最好的那个。
we can pick the best one out of all of the ones that we've taken a look at.

3795
05:54:23,310 --> 05:54:25,956
所以我们还有另一个可用的选项。
So there's another option we have access to as well.

3796
05:54:26,542 --> 05:54:32,932
虽然我之前说过局部搜索通常只跟踪一个节点并移动到它的邻居之一，
And then, although I said that generally local search will usually just keep track of a single node and then move to one of its neighbors,

3797
05:54:33,166 --> 05:54:41,184
但爬山算法中有一种被称为局部束搜索的变体，它不是只记录一个当前最好的状态，而是追踪 K 个。
there are variants of hill climbing that are known as local beam searches, where rather than keep track of just one current best state, we're keeping track of K.

3798
05:54:41,646 --> 05:54:50,704
即高价值邻居。与其从一个随机初始配置开始，我可能会从三个、四个或五个开始，随机生成所有邻居，然后挑选
Highest valued neighbors, such that rather than starting at one random initial configuration, I might start with three or four or five, randomly generate all the neighbors, and then pick

3799
05:54:50,944 --> 05:54:56,164
找到的所有邻居中最好的三个、四个或五个，并不断重复这个过程。
the three or four or five best of all of the neighbors that I find, and continually repeat this process.

3800
05:54:56,494 --> 05:55:06,148
其核心思想是现在我有更多的选项可以考虑，有更多种方法可以引导自己走向特定问题可能存在的最优解。
With the idea being that now I have more options that I'm considering, more ways that I could potentially navigate myself to the optimal solution that might exist for a particular problem.

