传统的爬山算法只会选取当前状态，查看两个相邻状态，并始终选择那个能增加状态值的。
our traditional hill climbing algorithms would just take the state and look at the two neighbor ones and always pick the one that is going to increase the value of the state.

3904
06:04:55,950 --> 06:05:00,740
但如果我们想有机会找到全局最大值，我们就不能总是做“好”的移动。
But if we want some chance of being able to find the global maximum, we can't always make good moves.

3905
06:05:01,518 --> 06:05:05,956
我们有时必须做出一些“坏”的移动，允许自己向一个
We have to sometimes make bad moves and allow ourselves to make a move in a direction

3906
06:05:06,638 --> 06:05:12,516
目前看起来会让情况变差的方向移动，这样以后我们才能找到路径向上到达
that actually seems for now to make our situation worse, such that later we can find our way up to

3907
06:05:13,198 --> 06:05:15,968
那个全局最大值，从而解决这个问题。
that global maximum in terms of trying to solve that problem.

3908
06:05:16,238 --> 06:05:23,780
当然，一旦我们到达这个全局最大值，在进行了大量的搜索之后，我们可能就不想再移动到比当前状态更差的状态了。
Of course, once we get up to this global maximum, once we've done a whole lot of the searching, then we probably don't want to be moving to states that are worse than our current state.

3909
06:05:24,046 --> 06:05:29,888
这就是“退火”这一隐喻开始发挥作用的地方，即我们希望初期进行更多随机移动，
And so this is where this metaphor for annealing starts to come in, where we want to start making more random moves,

3910
06:05:30,062 --> 06:05:35,172
并随着时间的推移，根据特定的温度计划来减少这些随机移动。
and over time start to make fewer of those random moves based on a particular temperature schedule.

3911
06:05:36,174 --> 06:05:37,892
所以基本的轮廓大概是这样的。
So the basic outline looks something like this.

3912
06:05:38,208 --> 06:05:42,148
在模拟退火的早期，我们处于高温度状态。
Early on in simulated annealing, we have a higher temperature state.

3913
06:05:42,478 --> 06:05:48,928
所谓高温度状态，是指我们更有可能接受那些比当前状态更差的邻居。
And what we mean by a higher temperature state is that we are more likely to accept neighbors that are worse than our current state.

3914
06:05:49,134 --> 06:05:56,708
也就是说，我们可能会查看邻居，如果某个邻居比当前状态差，尤其是没差多少，只是稍微差一点点的话，
That we might look at our neighbors, and if one of our neighbors is worse than the current state, especially if it's not all that much worse, if it's pretty close but just slightly worse,

3915
06:05:57,168 --> 06:06:01,252
那么我们就更有可能接受它，并直接移动到那个邻居。
then we might be more likely to accept that and go ahead and move to that neighbor anyways.

3916
06:06:02,062 --> 06:06:11,968
但随后在运行模拟退火的过程中，我们会降低温度；在较低的温度下，我们不太可能接受比当前状态更差的邻居。
But later on, as we run simulated annealing, we're going to decrease that temperature, and at a lower temperature, we're going to be less likely to accept neighbors that are worse than our current

3917
06:06:11,968 --> 06:06:16,740
现在为了将其正式化并写成一点伪代码，这个算法可能长这样。
state. Now to formalize this and put a little bit of pseudocode to it, here is what that algorithm might look like.

3918
06:06:17,008 --> 06:06:22,608
我们有一个名为“模拟退火”的函数，它接收我们要解决的问题作为输入，还有可能包含
We have a function called simulated annealing that takes as input the problem we're trying to solve, and also potentially

3919
06:06:22,830 --> 06:06:29,088
我们希望运行模拟退火过程的最大次数，即我们要尝试寻找多少个不同的邻居。
some maximum number of times that we might want to run the simulated annealing process, how many different neighbors we're going to try and look for.

3920
06:06:29,262 --> 06:06:31,940
这个数值将根据你试图解决的问题而变化。
And that value is going to vary based on the problem you're trying to solve.

3921
06:06:33,166 --> 06:06:36,868
我们再次从一个当前状态开始，它等于问题的初始状态。
We'll again start with some current state that will be equal to the initial state of the problem.

3922
06:06:37,328 --> 06:06:42,436
但现在我们需要重复这个过程，直到达到最大次数。
But now we need to repeat this process over and over for max number of times.

3923
06:06:42,734 --> 06:06:47,620
重复某些过程若干次，其中我们首先要计算一个温度。
Repeat some process some number of times, where we're first going to calculate a temperature.

3924
06:06:48,046 --> 06:06:57,168
这个温度函数接收从 1 开始到 max 的当前时间 t，然后给出一个我们可以用于计算的温度。
And this temperature function takes the current time t starting at one, going all the way up to max, and then gives us some temperature that we can use in our computation.

3925
06:06:57,328 --> 06:07:02,688
这里的思路是：这个温度在早期会更高，而在后期会更低。
Where the idea is that this temperature is going to be higher early on and it's going to be lower later on.

3926
06:07:02,862 --> 06:07:05,408
这种温度函数通常有几种实现方式。
So there are a number of ways this temperature function could often work.

3927
06:07:05,614 --> 06:07:10,608
最简单的一种方法就是将其设为剩余时间的比例。
One of the simplest ways is just to say it is like the proportion of time that we still have remaining.

3928
06:07:10,768 --> 06:07:13,888
在 max 个时间单位中，我们还剩下多少时间？
Out of max units of time, how much time do we have remaining?

3929
06:07:14,048 --> 06:07:21,668
你一开始拥有大量的剩余时间，随着时间的推移，由于剩下的时间越来越少，温度也会随之下降。
You start off with a lot of that time remaining, and as time goes on, the temperature is going to decrease because you have less and less of that remaining time still available to you.

3930
06:07:22,382 --> 06:07:28,048
因此，我们计算当前时间的温度，然后选择一个当前状态的随机邻居。
So we calculate a temperature for the current time, and then we pick a random neighbor of the current state.

3931
06:07:28,208 --> 06:07:33,248
我们不再是去挑选可能最好的邻居，或者选择几个较好的邻居。
No longer are we going to be picking the best neighbor that we possibly can, or just one of the better neighbors that we can.

3932
06:07:33,422 --> 06:07:34,688
我们要选择一个随机的邻居。
We're going to pick a random neighbor.

3933
06:07:34,798 --> 06:07:37,248
它可能更好，也可能更差，但我们会计算出那个结果。
It might be better, it might be worse, but we're going to calculate that.

3934
06:07:37,328 --> 06:07:44,612
我们要计算 delta E，在这种情况下 E 代表能量，也就是这个邻居比当前状态好多少。
We're going to calculate delta E, E for energy in this case, which is just how much better is the neighbor than the current state.

3935
06:07:45,230 --> 06:07:49,060
所以如果 delta E 是正数，意味着那个邻居比我们的当前状态更好。
So if delta E is positive, that means the neighbor is better than our current state.

3936
06:07:49,358 --> 06:07:53,540
如果 delta E 是负数，那意味着那个邻居比我们的当前状态更差。
If delta E is negative, that means the neighbor is worse than our current state.

3937
06:07:54,094 --> 06:07:55,888
那么我们可以设置这样一个条件。
And so we can then have a condition that looks like this.

3938
06:07:56,078 --> 06:08:01,540
如果 delta E 大于零，这意味着邻居状态比我们当前的更好。
If delta E is greater than zero, that means the neighbor state is better than our current state.

3939
06:08:01,870 --> 06:08:06,448
如果出现这种情况，我们就直接把当前状态更新为那个邻居。
And if ever that situation arises, we'll just go ahead and update current to be that neighbor.

3940
06:08:06,608 --> 06:08:12,676
就像之前一样，因为邻居比当前状态好，就把我们的位置移动到那个邻居，我们接受这个变化。
Same as before, move where we are currently to be the neighbor, because the neighbor is better than our current state. We'll go ahead and accept that.

3941
06:08:13,230 --> 06:08:20,688
但现在的区别是，以前我们绝不接受让情况变差的移动，而现在我们有时会想要这样做
But now the difference is that whereas before we never ever wanted to take a move that made our situation worse, now we sometimes want to

3942
06:08:21,168 --> 06:08:23,648
去进行一个实际上会让情况变差的移动。
make a move that is actually going to make our situation worse.

3943
06:08:23,918 --> 06:08:31,968
因为有时候我们需要从局部最小值或局部最大值中脱离出来，从而提高稍后能找到全局最小值或全局
Because sometimes we're going to need to dislodge ourselves from a local minimum or local maximum to increase the probability that we're able to find the global minimum or the global

3944
06:08:31,968 --> 06:08:33,220
最大值的概率。
maximum a little bit later.

3945
06:08:34,062 --> 06:08:39,140
那我们该怎么做呢？我们如何决定有时接受一些可能更差的状态？
And so how do we do that? How do we decide to sometimes accept some state that might actually be worse?

3946
06:08:39,470 --> 06:08:45,700
嗯，我们将以一定的概率接受较差的状态，而这个概率需要基于几个因素。
Well, we're going to accept a worse state with some probability, and that probability needs to be based on a couple of factors.

3947
06:08:45,966 --> 06:08:52,740
它部分取决于温度，如果温度较高，我们就更有可能移动到更差的邻居。
It needs to be based in part on the temperature, where if the temperature is higher, we're more likely to move to a worse neighbor.

3948
06:08:52,910 --> 06:08:56,164
如果温度较低，我们就较少去移动到更差的邻居。
And if the temperature is lower, we're less likely to move to a worse neighbor.

3949
06:08:56,686 --> 06:08:59,972
但它在某种程度上也应该基于 delta E。
But it also to some degree should be based on delta e.

3950
06:09:00,526 --> 06:09:08,900
如果邻居比当前状态差很多，那么我们选择它的概率应该低于邻居只比当前状态稍微差一点的情况。
If the neighbor is much worse than the current state, we probably want to be less likely to choose that than if the neighbor is just a little bit worse than the current state.

3951
06:09:09,678 --> 06:09:19,088
同样，计算这个值有几种方法，但结果发现最流行的一种是计算 e 的 delta E 除以 t 次方，其中 e 是一个常数。
So again, there are a couple of ways you could calculate this, but it turns out one of the most popular is just to calculate e to the power of delta e over t, where e is just a constant.

3952
06:09:19,374 --> 06:09:22,724
这里的 delta E 除以 t 是基于 delta E 和 t 计算的。
Delta e over t are based on delta e and t here.

3953
06:09:22,928 --> 06:09:30,948
我们计算出这个值，它会是一个介于 0 到 1 之间的数值，这就是我们决定“好，让我们移动到那个邻居”的概率。
We calculate that value, and that'll be some value between 0 and 1, and that is the probability with which we should just say, all right, let's go ahead and move to that neighbor.

3954
06:09:31,182 --> 06:09:37,860
而且事实证明，如果你对这个值进行数学推导，当 delta E 使得邻居并不比当前状态差多少时，
And it turns out that if you do the math for this value, when delta e is such that the neighbor is not that much worse than the current state,

3955
06:09:38,048 --> 06:09:40,804
我们更有可能去移动到那个状态。
that's going to be more likely that we're going to go ahead and move to that state.

3956
06:09:41,006 --> 06:09:46,180
同样地，当温度较低时，我们也更不容易移动到那个邻居状态。
And likewise, when the temperature is lower, we're going to be less likely to move to that neighboring state as well.

3957
06:09:47,054 --> 06:09:49,904
这就是模拟退火的大致全貌。
So now this is the big picture for simulated annealing.

3958
06:09:49,984 --> 06:09:56,676
这个过程是把问题拿出来并生成随机邻居，如果它比我们当前状态更好，就会始终移动到那个邻居。
This process of taking the problem and going ahead and generating random neighbors will always move to a neighbor if it's better than our current state.

3959
06:09:56,974 --> 06:10:04,260
但即使邻居比当前状态差，我们有时也会移动过去，这取决于它差多少，以及基于当前的温度。
But even if the neighbor is worse than our current state, we'll sometimes move there, depending on how much worse it is, and also based on the temperature.

3960
06:10:04,654 --> 06:10:12,624
因此，这个整个过程的希望和目标是，当我们开始尝试寻找通往全局最大值或全局最小值的路径时，
And as a result, the hope, the goal of this whole process is that as we begin to try and find our way to the local the global maximum or the global minimum,

3961
06:10:12,784 --> 06:10:21,572
这样我们就能从局部最大值或局部最小值中脱困，从而最终找到状态空间中最好的部分。
we can dislodge ourselves if we ever get stuck at a local maximum or local minimum in order to eventually make our way to exploring the part of the state space that is going to be the best.

3962
06:10:22,030 --> 06:10:31,044
随着温度降低，我们最终会稳定在目前找到的最佳方案附近，而不会在结果上产生太多变动。
And then as the temperature decreases, eventually we settle there without moving around too much from what we've found to be the globally best thing that we can do thus far.

3963
06:10:31,438 --> 06:10:37,188
最后，我们只需返回当前的任何状态，这就是该算法的结论。
So at the very end, we just return whatever the current state happens to be, and that is the conclusion of this algorithm.

3964
06:10:37,584 --> 06:10:39,620
我们已经能够找出解决方案了。
We've been able to figure out what the solution is.

3965
06:10:40,462 --> 06:10:43,824
这类算法有很多不同的应用场景。
And these types of algorithms have a lot of different applications.

3966
06:10:43,984 --> 06:10:50,304
只要你能把一个问题转化为可以探索特定配置，并询问：
Anytime you can take a problem and formulate it as something where you can explore a particular configuration and then ask,

3967
06:10:50,542 --> 06:10:59,428
“邻居中是否有比当前配置更好的？”并且有一种衡量方法，那么这些爬山算法或模拟退火算法就适用。
are any of the neighbors better than this current configuration and have some way of measuring that, then there's an applicable case for these hill climbing, simulated annealing types of algorithms.

3968
06:10:59,822 --> 06:11:06,276
比如在设施选址类问题中，比如当你试图规划城市并确定医院应该建在哪里时，
So sometimes it can be for facility location type problems, like for when you're trying to plan a city and figure out where the hospitals should be,

3969
06:11:06,478 --> 06:11:08,452
但肯定还有其他的应用场景。
but there are definitely other applications as well.

3970
06:11:08,686 --> 06:11:12,944
计算机科学中最著名的问题之一是旅行商问题。
And one of the most famous problems in computer science is the traveling salesman problem.

3971
06:11:13,230 --> 06:11:15,876
旅行商问题通常被表述如下：
Traveling salesman problem generally is formulated like this.

3972
06:11:16,206 --> 06:11:18,852
我这里有一堆由这些点表示的城市。
I have a whole bunch of cities here indicated by these dots.

3973
06:11:19,342 --> 06:11:25,316
我想找一条经过所有城市并回到起点的一条路线。
And what I'd like to do is find some route that takes me through all of the cities and ends up back where I started.

3974
06:11:25,614 --> 06:11:31,428
也就是从这里出发，经过所有这些城市，最后回到我最初开始的地方。
So some route that starts here, goes through all these cities and ends up back where I originally started.

3975
06:11:32,014 --> 06:11:39,744
我可能想最小化我必须行驶的总距离，或者走完这条完整路径的总成本。
And what I might like to do is minimize the total distance that I have to travel or the total cost of taking this entire path.

3976
06:11:40,014 --> 06:11:48,304
你可以想象这是一个非常实用的问题，比如当快递公司试图把货物送到很多不同的房子时。
And you can imagine this is a problem that's very applicable in situations like when delivery companies are trying to deliver things to a whole bunch of different houses.

3977
06:11:48,464 --> 06:11:57,504
他们需要计算如何从仓库到达所有这些不同的房子并返回，同时尽可能减少时间、距离和能耗。
They want to figure out how do I get from the warehouse to all these various different houses and get back again, all using as minimal time and distance and energy as possible.

3978
06:11:57,838 --> 06:12:00,064
所以你可能想尝试解决这类
So you might want to try to solve these sorts of

3979
06:12:00,064 --> 06:12:09,184
问题。但事实证明，解决这类特定问题在计算上非常困难。要找出确切答案是一个非常耗费计算资源的任务。
problems. But it turns out that solving this particular kind of problem is very computationally difficult. It is a very computationally expensive task to be able to figure it out.

3980
06:12:09,344 --> 06:12:17,092
这属于所谓的 NP-complete 问题类别，即目前还没有已知的高效方法来解决这类问题。
This falls under the category of what are known as NP-complete problems, problems that there is no known efficient way to try and solve these sorts of problems.

3981
06:12:17,422 --> 06:12:27,824
因此我们最终要做的是寻找一些近似方案，或者用一些方法去寻找一个好的解，即使我们无法找到可能存在的全局最优解，
And so what we ultimately have to do is come up with some approximation, some ways of trying to find a good solution, even if we're not going to find the globally best solution that we possibly can,

3982
06:12:27,984 --> 06:12:30,660
至少在可行或可接受的时间内是找不到的。
at least not in a feasible or tractable amount of time.

3983
06:12:31,246 --> 06:12:39,424
所以我们可以把旅行商问题拿出来，尝试用局部搜索来表述它，并提出一个问题：好，我可以选择一个状态，
And so what we could do is take the traveling salesman problem and try to formulate it using local search and ask a question, like, all right, I can pick some state,

3984
06:12:39,584 --> 06:12:45,700
一种配置，即连接所有这些节点的一条路线，我可以衡量这个状态的成本，计算出距离是多少，
some configuration, some route between all of these nodes, and I can measure the cost of that state, figure out what the distance is,

3985
06:12:46,030 --> 06:12:49,124
然后我现在想尽可能地最小化这个成本。
and I might now want to try to minimize that cost as much as possible.

3986
06:12:49,902 --> 06:12:53,860
那么现在唯一的问题是，这个状态的“邻居”意味着什么？
And then the only question now is, what does it mean to have a neighbor of this state?

3987
06:12:54,094 --> 06:13:01,380
这意味着采取这条特定路线，并有一个与之接近但略有不同的邻近路线，从而可能产生不同的总距离。
What does it mean to take this particular route and have some neighboring route that is close to it but slightly different such that it might have a different total distance?

3988
06:13:01,774 --> 06:13:06,660
对于旅行商配置的“邻居”定义有很多种。
And there are a number of different definitions for what a neighbor of a traveling salesman configuration might look like.

3989
06:13:06,990 --> 06:13:15,012
其中一种方法就是说：如果我们选择两个节点之间的边并有效地交换它们，这就是一个邻居。
But one way is just to say, a neighbor is what happens if we pick two of these edges between nodes and switch them

3990
06:13:15,278 --> 06:13:15,748
有效地。
effectively.

3991
06:13:16,384 --> 06:13:22,372
例如，我可能会选择这里的这两条边，就是这两条恰好交叉的边，这个节点到这里，那个节点到那里，
So for example, I might pick these two edges here, these two that just happen to cross, this node goes here, this node goes there,

3992
06:13:23,150 --> 06:13:24,484
然后把它们交换一下。
and go ahead and switch them.

3993
06:13:24,846 --> 06:13:33,504
这个过程通常看起来是：从图中移除这两条边，把这个节点连接到它原本没连接的那个节点上。
And what that process will generally look like is removing both of these edges from the graph, taking this node and connecting it to the node it wasn't connected to.

3994
06:13:33,646 --> 06:13:35,588
也就是说，改到这里来连接。
So connecting it up here instead.

3995
06:13:36,014 --> 06:13:42,660
我们需要把这些原本朝这个方向的箭头反转过来，变成向另一个方向，然后填补最后剩下的空白，
We'll need to take these arrows that were originally going this way and reverse them, so move them going the other way, and then just fill in that last remaining blank,

3996
06:13:42,894 --> 06:13:44,900
换成一个指向那个方向的箭头。
add an arrow that goes in that direction instead.

3997
06:13:45,294 --> 06:13:54,784
所以通过选取两条边并交换它们，我就能考虑到这个特定配置的一个可能邻居，而且看起来这个邻居实际上更好一些。
So by taking two edges and just switching them, I have been able to consider one possible neighbor of this particular configuration, and it looks like this neighbor is actually better.

3998
06:13:54,864 --> 06:14:01,744
看起来这条路径在经过所有城市时，比当前状态所走的距离更短。
It looks like this probably travels a shorter distance in order to get through all the cities through this route than the current state did.

