4117
06:25:32,368 --> 06:25:40,164
我们需要确定这些变量分别应该取什么值，但这些变量受到特定约束的限制，这些约束将限制
and we need to figure out what values each of those variables should take on, but those variables are subject to particular constraints that are going to limit

4118
06:25:40,288 --> 06:25:42,628
这些变量实际可以取到的值。
what values those variables can actually take on.

4119
06:25:43,342 --> 06:25:46,116
所以让我们来看一个现实世界的例子。
So let's take a look at a real world example, for example.

4120
06:25:46,448 --> 06:25:48,048
我们来看看考试安排。
let's look at exam scheduling.

4121
06:25:48,238 --> 06:25:51,008
这里我有四个学生，学生一、二、三和四。
That I have four students here, students one, two, three, and four.

4122
06:25:51,408 --> 06:25:53,648
他们中的每一个都在选修一些不同的课程。
each of them is taking some number of different classes.

4123
06:25:53,998 --> 06:25:56,004
这里的课程将用字母来表示。
Classes here are going to be represented by letters.

4124
06:25:56,462 --> 06:26:03,652
所以学生一选修了课程 A、B 和 C，学生二选修了课程 B、D 和 E，以此类推。
so student one is enrolled in courses A, B, and C, student two is enrolled in courses B, D, and E, so on and so forth.

4125
06:26:04,302 --> 06:26:12,528
现在，假设某所大学正试图为所有这些课程安排考试，但周一、
And now, say university, for example, is trying to schedule exams for all of these courses, but there are only three exam slots on Monday,

4126
06:26:12,608 --> 06:26:16,612
周二和周三只有三个考试时段，而我们必须为每一门课程安排一场考试。
Tuesday, and Wednesday, and we have to schedule an exam for each of these courses.

4127
06:26:17,294 --> 06:26:25,008
但现在面临的约束是，在安排考试时，我们不希望任何人需要在同一天参加两场考试。
But the constraint now, the constraint we have to deal with with the scheduling, is that we don't want anyone to have to take two exams on the same day.

4128
06:26:25,134 --> 06:26:28,292
我们希望尽可能减少甚至消除这种情况。
We would like to try and minimize that or eliminate it if at all possible.

4129
06:26:29,454 --> 06:26:37,408
那么，我们如何开始表达这个想法？我们该如何构建它，让带有 AI 算法的计算机能够尝试解决这个问题？
So, how do we begin to represent this idea? How do we structure this in a way that a computer with an AI algorithm can begin to try and solve the problem?

4130
06:26:37,774 --> 06:26:45,316
好，我们特别来看看这些可能选修的课程，并将每门课程表示为图中的一个节点。
Well, let's in particular just look at these classes that we might take and represent each of the courses as some node inside of a graph.

4131
06:26:45,870 --> 06:26:53,156
我们要做的就是：如果两个节点之间存在约束，就在这个图中在它们之间建立一条边。
And what we'll do is we'll create an edge between two nodes in this graph if there is a constraint between those two nodes.

4132
06:26:54,286 --> 06:26:55,088
这代表什么意思呢？
So what does this mean?

4133
06:26:55,406 --> 06:26:59,488
我们可以从学生一开始，他选修了课程 A、B 和 C。
Well, we can start with student one, who's enrolled in courses A, B, and C.

4134
06:26:59,822 --> 06:27:08,804
这意味着 A 和 B 不能同时考试，A 和 C 不能同时考试，B 和 C 也不能同时考试。
What that means is that A and B can't have an exam at the same time, A and C can't have an exam at the same time, and B and C also can't have an exam at the same time.

4135
06:27:09,102 --> 06:27:12,048
我可以在这个图中通过绘制边来表示这一点。
And I can represent that in this graph by just drawing edges.

4136
06:27:12,208 --> 06:27:16,548
在 A 和 B 之间画一条边，B 和 C 之间画一条，然后 C 和 A 之间也画一条。
One edge between A and B, one between B and C, and then one between C and A.

4137
06:27:16,782 --> 06:27:25,636
这现在编码了这些节点之间存在约束的这一想法，具体来说，这个约束恰好是这两个值不能相等，
And that encodes now the idea that between those nodes there is a constraint, and in particular, the constraint happens to be that these two can't be equal to each other,

4138
06:27:25,742 --> 06:27:30,052
当然，根据你试图解决问题的类型，还有其他可能存在的约束类型。
though there are other types of constraints that are possible, depending on the type of problem that you're trying to solve.

4139
06:27:31,182 --> 06:27:33,712
然后我们可以对其他每个学生做同样的操作。
And then we can do the same thing for each of the other students.

4140
06:27:33,838 --> 06:27:40,912
对于选修了课程 B、D 和 E 的学生二来说，这意味着 B、D 和 E 这些节点也都需要互相连接的边。
So for student two, who's enrolled in courses B, D, and E, well that means B, D, and E, those all need to have edges that connect each other as well.

4141
06:27:41,294 --> 06:27:48,324
学生三选修了课程 C、E 和 F。所以我们继续把 C、E 和 F 连接起来，在它们之间画上边。
Student three is enrolled in courses C, E, and F. So we'll go ahead and take C, E, and F and connect those by drawing edges between them too.

4142
06:27:48,590 --> 06:27:57,312
最后，学生四选修了课程 E、F 和 G。我们可以通过在 E、F 和 G 之间画线来表示这一点，尽管 E 和 F 之间已经有一条边了。
And then finally, student four is enrolled in courses E, F, and G, and we can represent that by drawing edges between E, F, and G, although E and F already had an edge between them.

4143
06:27:57,472 --> 06:28:05,060
我们不需要再画一条，因为这个约束只是在编码一个概念：课程 E 和课程 F 不能在同一天考试。
We don't need another one, because this constraint is just encoding the idea that course E and course F cannot have an exam on the same day.

4144
06:28:05,678 --> 06:28:08,900
这就是我们所谓的约束图。
So this then is what we might call the constraint graph.

4145
06:28:09,326 --> 06:28:16,804
从某种意义上说，它是所有变量以及这些可能变量之间约束的一种图形表示。
It is some graphical representation of all of my variables, so to speak, and the constraints between those possible variables.

4146
06:28:16,992 --> 06:28:23,312
在这种情况下，每一个约束都代表一个不等式约束，即 b 和 d 之间的边
Where in this particular case, each of the constraints represents an inequality constraint, that an edge between b and d

4147
06:28:23,534 --> 06:28:29,540
意味着变量 b 所取的任何值都不能是变量 d 所取的值。
means whatever value the variable b takes on cannot be the value that the variable d takes on as well.

4148
06:28:30,286 --> 06:28:33,312
那么，什么是约束满足问题呢？
So what then actually is a constraint satisfaction problem?

4149
06:28:33,710 --> 06:28:39,140
嗯，约束满足问题就是一组变量，从 x1 一直到 xn，
Well, a constraint satisfaction problem is just some set of variables, x1 all the way through xn,

4150
06:28:39,886 --> 06:28:44,832
以及为每个变量设定的定义域。也就是说，每个变量都需要取某些值。
some set of domains for each of those variables. So every variable needs to take on some values.

4151
06:28:45,102 --> 06:28:48,964
也许每个变量都有相同的定义域，但也可能每个变量的定义域略有不同。
Maybe every variable has the same domain, but maybe each variable has a slightly different domain.

4152
06:28:49,582 --> 06:28:55,428
然后还有一组约束，我们称之为 C，即施加在这些变量上的某些约束。
And then there's a set of constraints, and we'll just call a set c that is some constraints that are placed upon these variables.

4153
06:28:55,632 --> 06:28:57,712
比如 x1 不等于 x2。
Like x1 is not equal to x2.

4154
06:28:57,998 --> 06:29:06,180
但它们也可以是其他形式，例如如果这些变量在定义域中取数值，那么可能是 x1 等于 x2 加 1。
But they could be of other forms too, like maybe x1 equals x2 plus one if these variables are taking on numerical values in their domain, for example.

4155
06:29:06,432 --> 06:29:09,632
约束的类型将根据问题的
The types of constraints are going to vary based on the types of

4156
06:29:09,632 --> 06:29:18,628
类型而变化。而且在任何涉及受特定约束限制的变量的情况下，约束满足都会出现。
problems. And constraint satisfaction shows up all over the place as well in any situation where we have variables that are subject to particular constraints.

4157
06:29:19,214 --> 06:29:26,112
例如一个流行的游戏是数独，这是一个九乘九的网格，你需要填入数字到每个单元格中，但你希望
So one popular game is Sudoku, for example, this nine by nine grid where you need to fill in numbers into each of these cells, but you want to

4158
06:29:27,152 --> 06:29:33,604
确保任何一行、任何一列或任何三乘三的方格内都没有重复的数字。
make sure there's never a duplicate number in any row or in any column or in any grid of three by three cells, for example.

4159
06:29:34,126 --> 06:29:37,380
那么这作为约束满足问题会是什么样子的？
So what might this look like as a constraint satisfaction problem?

4160
06:29:37,838 --> 06:29:41,632
嗯，我的变量是谜题中所有空白的格子。
Well, my variables are all of the empty squares in the puzzle.

4161
06:29:41,934 --> 06:29:49,956
这里所表示的就像是一个 x 和 y 坐标，即所有我需要填入数值、且目前不知道该填什么值的格子。
So represented here is just like an x, comma, y coordinate, for example, as all of the squares where I need to plug in a value, where I don't know what value it should take on.

4162
06:29:50,606 --> 06:29:51,492
定义域
The domain

4163
06:29:52,142 --> 06:29:59,684
就是从 1 到 9 的所有数字，即我可以填入这些单元格中的任何值。所以这就是每个变量的定义域。
is just going to be all of the numbers from one through nine, any value that I could fill in to one of these cells. So that is going to be the domain for each of these variables.

4164
06:30:00,174 --> 06:30:08,032
然后约束的形式就像是：这个格子不能等于那个格子，不能等于这个格子，也就是说所有这些都需要不同，例如
And then the constraints are going to be of the form like this cell can't be equal to this cell, can't be equal to this cell, can't be all of these need to be different, for example,

4165
06:30:08,270 --> 06:30:12,388
同样的规则也适用于所有的行、列以及三乘三的方格。
and same for all of the rows and the columns and the three by three squares as well.

4166
06:30:12,686 --> 06:30:17,028
因此，这些约束将强制执行哪些值是允许的。
So those constraints are going to enforce what values are actually allowed.

4167
06:30:17,902 --> 06:30:25,252
我们可以在这个考试排程问题中用同样的概念来表述，其中变量是我们拥有的不同课程，从 a 到 g。
And we can formulate the same idea in the case of this exam scheduling problem, where the variables we have are the different courses, a up through G.

4168
06:30:25,806 --> 06:30:30,084
这些变量各自的定义域将是周一、周二和周三。
The domain for each of these variables is going to be Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday.

4169
06:30:30,192 --> 06:30:37,060
这些是每个变量可以取到的可能值，在这种情况下，它们仅代表该课程考试的时间。
Those are the possible values each of the variables can take on, that in this case just represent when is the exam for that class.

4170
06:30:38,062 --> 06:30:48,004
然后约束的形式如下：a 不等于 B，A 不等于 C，意味着 A 和 B 不能在同一天考试，A 和 C 也不能在同一天考试。
And then the constraints are of this form: a is not equal to B, A is not equal to C, meaning A and B can't have an exam on the same day, A and C can't have an exam on the same day,

4171
06:30:48,192 --> 06:30:54,512
或者更正式点说，这两个变量在它们的定义域内不能取相同的值。
or more formally, these two variables cannot take on the same value within their domain.

4172
06:30:56,078 --> 06:31:02,660
这就是约束满足问题的表述方式，我们可以开始用它来尝试解决这个问题。
So that then is this formulation of a constraint satisfaction problem that we can begin to use to try and solve this problem.

4173
06:31:03,086 --> 06:31:05,152
而且约束可以有多种不同的形式。
And constraints can come in a number of different forms.

4174
06:31:05,392 --> 06:31:09,952
有硬约束，即为了得到正确解必须满足的约束。
There are hard constraints, which are constraints that must be satisfied for a correct solution.

4175
06:31:10,254 --> 06:31:17,232
就像在 Sudoku 谜题中，处于同一行中的这两个单元格不能取相同的值。
So something like in the Sudoku puzzle, you cannot have this cell and this cell that are in the same row take on the same value.

4176
06:31:17,312 --> 06:31:18,500
这就是一个硬约束。
That is a hard constraint.

4177
06:31:18,926 --> 06:31:27,472
但问题也可以有软约束，这类约束是表达某种偏好，比如 A 和 B 可能不能在同一天考试，
But problems can also have soft constraints, where these are constraints that express some notion of preference, that maybe A and B can't have an exam on the same day,

4178
06:31:27,792 --> 06:31:32,032
但可能有人更倾向于让 A 的考试在 B 的考试之前。
but maybe someone has a preference that A's exam is earlier than B's exam.

4179
06:31:32,142 --> 06:31:37,312
并不一定非要用某种表达方式来说明某个解比另一个解更好。
It doesn't need to be the case with some expression that some solution is better than another solution.

4180
06:31:37,422 --> 06:31:42,788
在这种情况下，你可以把问题建模为试图最大化人们的偏好。
And in that case, you might formulate the problem as trying to optimize for maximizing people's preferences.

4181
06:31:42,992 --> 06:31:46,116
你希望尽可能满足人们的偏好。
You want people's preferences to be satisfied as much as possible.

4182
06:31:46,830 --> 06:31:54,032
不过在目前的情况下，我们主要处理硬约束，即为了获得正确解而必须满足的约束。
In this case, though, we'll mostly just deal with hard constraints, constraints that must be met in order to have a correct solution to the problem.

4183
06:31:54,318 --> 06:32:02,244
所以我们要找出这些变量到特定值的某种赋值，从而最终为问题提供一个解
So we want to figure out some assignment of these variables to their particular values that is ultimately going to give us a solution to the problem

4184
06:32:02,352 --> 06:32:08,324
通过给每个课程分配一个日期，使得不同课程之间没有任何冲突。
by allowing us to assign some day to each of the classes such that we don't have any conflicts between classes.

4185
06:32:09,198 --> 06:32:15,556
事实证明，我们可以将约束满足问题中的约束分为几个不同的类别。
So it turns out that we can classify the constraints in a constraint satisfaction problem into a number of different categories.

4186
06:32:16,160 --> 06:32:25,892
第一个类别可能是最简单的约束类型，被称为一元约束，即只涉及单个变量的约束。
The first of those categories are perhaps the simplest of the types of constraints, which are known as unary constraints, where a unary constraint is a constraint that just involves a single variable.

4187
06:32:26,222 --> 06:32:33,280
例如，一元约束可能类似于 A 不等于周一，意味着课程 A 不能在周一考试。
For example, a unary constraint might be something like A does not equal Monday, meaning course A cannot have its exam on Monday.

4188
06:32:33,422 --> 06:32:41,360
如果由于某种原因该课程的老师周一没空，你的问题中可能会有一个这样的约束，即只包含单个变量 A 的约束，
If for some reason the instructor for the course isn't available on Monday, you might have a constraint in your problem that looks like this, something that just has a single variable A in it,

4189
06:32:41,614 --> 06:32:50,800
并且可能表述为 A 不等于周一或者 A 等于某值，或者在数值大于或小于某个数的情况下，这种只有一个变量的约束我们称之为一元
and maybe says A is not equal to Monday or A is equal to something, or in the case of numbers greater than or less than something, a constraint that just has one variable we consider to be a unary

4190
06:32:51,022 --> 06:32:51,364
约束。
constraint.

4191
06:32:51,886 --> 06:32:58,000
这与二元约束形成对比，二元约束是指涉及两个变量的约束，例如：
And this is in contrast to something like a binary constraint, which is a constraint that involves two variables, for example.

4192
06:32:58,222 --> 06:33:01,156
这就是我们之前看过的那些约束。
So this would be a constraint like the ones we were looking at before.

4193
06:33:01,454 --> 06:33:09,520
像 a 不等于 b 这样的就是二元约束的一个例子，因为它是一个涉及两个变量的约束，
Something like a does not equal b is an example of a binary constraint because it is a constraint that has two variables involved in it,

4194
06:33:09,760 --> 06:33:17,284
即 a 和 b，我们用连接变量 a 到变量 b 的弧或边来表示它。
a and b, and we represented that using some arc or some edge that connects variable a to variable b.

4195
06:33:17,902 --> 06:33:26,692
利用这些关于一元约束和二元约束的知识，我们可以对特定的约束满足问题做出不同的判断。
And using this knowledge of, okay, what is a unary constraint, what is a binary constraint, there are different types of things we can say about a particular constraint satisfaction problem.

4196
06:33:26,880 --> 06:33:31,012
其中一点就是，我们可以尝试让问题达到节点一致。
And one thing we can say is we can try and make the problem node consistent.

4197
06:33:31,598 --> 06:33:33,120
那么节点一致是什么意思呢？
So what does node consistency mean?

4198
06:33:33,360 --> 06:33:40,932
节点一致意味着一个变量定义域中的所有值都满足该变量的一元约束。
Node consistency means we have all of the values in a variable's domain satisfying that variable's unary constraints.

4199
06:33:41,486 --> 06:33:50,240
也就是说，对于我们约束满足问题中的每一个变量，如果所有的值都满足该特定变量的一元约束，
So for each of the variables inside of our constraint satisfaction problem, if all of the values satisfy the unary constraints for that particular variable,

4200
06:33:50,414 --> 06:33:58,308
我们就可以说整个问题是节点一致的，或者如果我们只想针对一个节点，也可以说这个特定的变量是节点一致的。
we can say that the entire problem is node consistent, or we can even say that a particular variable is node consistent if we just want to make one node

4201
06:33:58,560 --> 06:33:59,716
自身一致。
consistent within itself.

4202
06:34:00,558 --> 06:34:02,000
那这具体是什么样子的呢？
So what does that actually look like?

4203
06:34:02,286 --> 06:34:07,684
让我们来看一个简化后的例子，不再有那么多不同的类别，我们只有两个类别，
Let's look at now a simplified example where instead of having a whole bunch of different classes, we just have two classes,

4204
06:34:08,000 --> 06:34:12,080
a 和 b，它们中的每一个都在周一、周二或周三中任何一天有一场考试。
a and b, each of which has an exam on either Monday or Tuesday or Wednesday.

4205
06:34:12,270 --> 06:34:16,484
这是变量 a 的定义域，而这是变量 b 的定义域。
So this is the domain for the variable a, and this is the domain for the variable b.

4206
06:34:17,102 --> 06:34:19,300
现在让我们假设我们有这些约束条件：
And now let's imagine we have these constraints.

4207
06:34:19,918 --> 06:34:24,420
a 不等于周一，B 不等于周二，B 不等于周一，A 不等于 B。
a not equal to Monday, B not equal to Tuesday, B not equal to Monday, A not equal to B.

4208
06:34:24,942 --> 06:34:27,908
这就是这个特定问题中的约束条件。
So those are the constraints that we have on this particular problem.

4209
06:34:28,558 --> 06:34:32,228
我们现在可以尝试执行节点一致性检查。
And what we can now try to do is enforce node consistency.

4210
06:34:32,526 --> 06:34:40,612
节点一致性意味着我们要确保任何变量定义域中的所有值都符合其一元约束。
And node consistency just means we make sure that all of the values for any variable's domain satisfy its unary constraints.

4211
06:34:41,230 --> 06:34:45,124
我们可以从尝试让节点 A 达到节点一致性开始。
And so we can start by trying to make node A node consistent.

4212
06:34:45,550 --> 06:34:50,788
比如，它一致吗？A 定义域内的每一个值都符合它的一元约束吗？
Like, is it consistent? Does every value inside of A's domain satisfy its unary constraints?

4213
06:34:51,118 --> 06:35:00,260
嗯，最初我们会发现周一并不符合 A 的一元约束，因为我们有一个一元约束规定 A 不等于周一，
Well, initially we'll see that Monday does not satisfy A's unary constraints, because we have a constraint, a unary constraint here, that A is not equal to Monday,

4214
06:35:00,686 --> 06:35:02,692
但周一仍然在 A 的定义域中。
but Monday is still in A's domain.

4215
06:35:03,246 --> 06:35:10,788
所以这就不符合节点一致性，因为虽然我们在定义域里有周一，但它不是这个特定节点的有效值。
And so this is something that is not node consistent, because we have Monday in the domain, but this is not a valid value for this particular node.

4216
06:35:11,150 --> 06:35:13,120
那我们该如何让这个节点变得一致呢？
And so how do we make this node consistent?

4217
06:35:13,390 --> 06:35:18,564
为了让节点达到一致性，我们要做的就是把周一从 A 的定义域中移除。
Well, to make the node node consistent, what we'll do is we'll just go ahead and remove Monday from A's domain.

4218
06:35:18,830 --> 06:35:24,548
现在 A 只能是周二或周三，因为我们之前有约束规定 A 不等于周一。
Now A can only be on Tuesday or Wednesday because we had this constraint that said A is not equal to Monday.

4219
06:35:25,390 --> 06:35:28,480
到这一步为止，A 就达到节点一致性了。
And at this point now, A is node consistent.

4220
06:35:28,590 --> 06:35:36,640
对于 A 可以取到的每一个值（周二和周三），都没有与之冲突的一元约束。
For each of the values that A can take on, Tuesday and Wednesday, there is no constraint that is a unary constraint that conflicts with that idea.

4221
06:35:36,720 --> 06:35:39,012
没有约束说 A 不能是周二。
There is no constraint that says that A can't be Tuesday.

4222
06:35:39,150 --> 06:35:42,308
也没有一元约束说 A 不能是周三。
There is no unary constraint that says that A cannot be on Wednesday.

4223
06:35:42,990 --> 06:35:44,560
现在我们可以把注意力转到 B 上。
And so now we can turn our attention to B.

4224
06:35:44,880 --> 06:35:52,880
B 也有一个定义域：周一、周二和周三，我们可以开始看看这些变量是否也符合一元约束。
B also has a domain, Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday, and we can begin to see whether those variables satisfy the unary constraints as well.

4225
06:35:53,166 --> 06:35:54,480
好，这里有一个一元约束。
Well, here's a unary constraint.

4226
06:35:54,720 --> 06:36:04,708
B 不等于周二，而这个由周一、周二和周三组成的定义域似乎并不满足这一项，因为周二，作为变量 b 可能取到的值，
B is not equal to Tuesday, and that does not appear to be satisfied by this domain of Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday, because Tuesday, this possible value that the variable b could take on,

4227
06:36:05,120 --> 06:36:09,060
与“b 不等于周二”这一一元约束不一致。
is not consistent with this unary constraint, that b is not equal to Tuesday.

4228
06:36:09,582 --> 06:36:13,440
为了解决这个问题，我们将把周二从 B 的定义域中移除。
So to solve that problem, we'll go ahead and remove Tuesday from B's domain.

4229
06:36:13,582 --> 06:36:21,280
现在 B 的定义域只包含周一和周三，但事实是，我们对变量 b 还设置了另一个一元约束，就在这里。
Now B's domain only contains Monday and Wednesday, but as it turns out, there's yet another unary constraint that we placed on the variable b, which is here.

4230
06:36:21,646 --> 06:36:23,140
B 不等于周一。
B is not equal to Monday.

4231
06:36:23,840 --> 06:36:30,000
这意味着在 B 的定义域中，这个值“周一”与 B 的一元约束不一致，
That means that this value, Monday, inside of B's domain, is not consistent with B's unary constraints,

4232
06:36:30,190 --> 06:36:35,172
因为我们有一个约束规定 B 不能是周一，所以我们可以从 B 的定义域中移除周一。
because we have a constraint that says the B cannot be Monday, and so we can remove Monday from B's domain.

4233
06:36:35,360 --> 06:36:38,480
现在我们已经处理完所有的一元约束了。
And now we've made it through all of the unary constraints.

4234
06:36:38,560 --> 06:36:46,948
我们还没有考虑这个二元约束，但我们已经考虑了所有的一元约束，也就是涉及单个变量的所有约束，
We've not yet considered this constraint, which is a binary constraint, but we've considered all of the unary constraints, all of the constraints that involve just a single variable,

4235
06:36:47,310 --> 06:36:51,840
并且我们确保了每个节点都符合这些一元约束。
and we've made sure that every node is consistent with those unary constraints.

4236
06:36:51,950 --> 06:36:55,268
所以我们可以说，现在我们实现了节点一致性。
So we can say that now we have enforced node consistency.

4237
06:36:55,600 --> 06:37:04,388
这意味着对于这些可能的节点中的每一个，我们都可以从定义域中选择任何一个值，而不会导致一元约束被违反。
That for each of these possible nodes, we can pick any of these values in the domain, and there won't be a unary constraint that is violated as a result of it.

4238
06:37:05,582 --> 06:37:07,664
所以，强制执行节点一致性相当简单。
So, node consistency is fairly easy to enforce.

4239
06:37:07,824 --> 06:37:12,100
我们只需对每个节点进行处理，确保定义域中的值符合一元约束。
We just take each node, make sure the values in the domain satisfy the unary constraints.

4240
06:37:12,366 --> 06:37:17,156
情况变得更有趣一点的是当我们考虑不同类型的一致性时。
Where things get a little bit more interesting is when we consider different types of consistency.

4241
06:37:17,504 --> 06:37:20,228
比如像弧一致性这样的东西。
Something like arc consistency, for example.

4242
06:37:20,718 --> 06:37:27,876
而弧一致性是指一个变量定义域中的所有值都满足该变量的二元约束。
And arc consistency refers to when all of the values in a variable's domain satisfy the variable's binary constraints.

4243
06:37:28,302 --> 06:37:34,788
所以当我们试图实现弧一致性时，我们不再仅仅考虑涉及 A 的一元约束。
So when we're looking at trying to make a arc consistent, we're no longer just considering the unary constraints that involve a.

4244
06:37:35,054 --> 06:37:39,664
我们还要尝试考虑所有涉及 A 的二元约束。
We're trying to consider all of the binary constraints that involve a as well.

4245
06:37:39,790 --> 06:37:46,852
也就是说，在那个我们之前查看的约束图中，任何连接 A 与另一个变量的边。
So any edge that connects a to another variable inside of that constraint graph that we were taking a look at before.

4246
06:37:47,598 --> 06:37:55,524
更正式一点说，弧一致性中的“弧”其实就是指约束图中连接这两个节点的“边”。
Put a little bit more formally, arc consistency, and arc really is just another word for an edge that connects two of these nodes inside of our constraint graph.

4247
06:37:55,918 --> 06:37:58,564
我们可以像这样更精确地定义我们的一致性。
We can define our consistency a little more precisely like this.

4248
06:37:59,086 --> 06:38:07,664
为了让变量 x 相对于另一个变量 y 达到弧一致，我们需要从
In order to make some variable x arc consistent with respect to some other variable y, we need to remove any element

4249
06:38:08,078 --> 06:38:16,420
x 的定义域中移除任何元素，以确保 x 的每一个选择，即 x 定义域中的每一个选择，都有 y 的可能选择。
from x's domain to make sure that every choice for x, every choice in x's domain has a possible choice for y.

4250
06:38:17,518 --> 06:38:25,252
换句话说，如果我有一个变量 x，并且我想让 x 达到弧一致，那么我会查看 x 所有可能取到的值，
So put another way, if I have a variable x and I want to make x n arc consistent, then I'm going to look at all of the possible values that x can take on

4251
06:38:25,550 --> 06:38:31,184
并确保对于所有这些可能的值，我仍然可以为 y 做出一个选择。
and make sure that for all of those possible values, there is still some choice that I can make for y.

4252
06:38:31,438 --> 06:38:38,276
如果 x 和 y 之间存在弧，要确保 y 也有我可以选择的可能选项。
if there's some arc between x and y, to make sure that y has a possible option that I can choose as well.

4253
06:38:39,182 --> 06:38:40,544
那么让我们来看一个例子。
So let's look at an example of that.

4254
06:38:40,782 --> 06:38:49,380
回到之前的这个例子，我们已经通过规定 A 只能是周二或周三来强制执行节点一致性，因为我们知道 A 不能是周一。
Going back to this example from before, we enforced node consistency already by saying that A can only be on Tuesday or Wednesday, because we knew that A could not be on Monday.

4255
06:38:49,646 --> 06:38:57,540
我们还说 B 的定义域只包含周三，因为我们知道 B 不等于周二，而且 B 也不等于周一。
And we also said that B's only domain only consists of Wednesday, because we know that B does not equal Tuesday, and also B does not equal Monday.

4256
06:38:58,382 --> 06:39:04,676
现在让我们开始考虑弧一致性。让我们试着让 A 与 B 达到弧一致。
So now let's begin to consider arc consistency. Let's try and make A arc consistent with B.

4257
06:39:05,006 --> 06:39:15,908
这意味着要让 A 相对于 B 达到弧一致，意味着对于我们在 A 定义域中做的任何选择，在 B 的定义域中都有一个对应的、一致的选择。
And what that means is to make A arc consistent with respect to B means that for any choice we make in A's domain, there is some choice we can make in B's domain that is going to be consistent.

4258
06:39:16,558 --> 06:39:17,188
我们可以试一下。
And we can try that.

4259
06:39:17,486 --> 06:39:20,464
对于 A，我们可以选择周二作为 A 的可能值。
For A, we can choose Tuesday as a possible value for A.

4260
06:39:20,718 --> 06:39:26,144
如果我为 A 选择周二，那么是否存在一个 B 的值能满足这个二元约束？
If I choose Tuesday for A, is there a value for B that satisfies the binary constraint?

4261
06:39:26,382 --> 06:39:32,868
没错，B选周三就能满足“A不等于B”这个约束，因为周二不等于周三。
Well yes, B Wednesday would satisfy this constraint that A does not equal B because Tuesday does not equal Wednesday.

4262
06:39:33,504 --> 06:39:36,580
但是，如果我们给A选周三的话，
However, if we chose Wednesday for A,

4263
06:39:37,230 --> 06:39:42,624
那么在B的定义域里就没有能满足这个二元约束的选择了。
well then there is no choice in B's domain that satisfies this binary constraint.

4264
06:39:42,784 --> 06:39:49,220
我没法给B选一个值来满足“A不等于B”，因为我知道B必须是周三。
There is no way I can choose something for B that satisfies A does not equal B because I know B must be Wednesday.

4265
06:39:49,902 --> 06:39:54,596
所以，如果我遇到这种情况，即看到A有一个可能的值，
And so if ever I run into a situation like this where I see that here is a possible value for A,

4266
06:39:55,310 --> 06:40:01,892
但对应的B却没有任何能满足二元约束的选项时，这就意味着它不符合弧一致性。
such that there is no choice of value for B that satisfies the binary constraint, well then this is not art consistent.

4267
06:40:02,350 --> 06:40:07,588
为了让它符合弧一致性，我需要把周三从A的定义域中移除。
And to make it art consistent, I would need to take Wednesday and remove it from A's domain.

4268
06:40:07,824 --> 06:40:14,624
因为周三不可能作为A的选项，因为它与B的这个二元约束不一致。
Because Wednesday was not going to be a possible choice I can make for A, because it wasn't consistent with this binary constraint for B.

4269
06:40:14,784 --> 06:40:21,796
我没法给A选周三，同时还能通过给B选择一个值来获得可行解。
There was no way I could choose Wednesday for A and still have an available solution by choosing something for B as well.

4270
06:40:22,542 --> 06:40:25,744
所以现在，我成功实现了弧一致性。
So here now I've been able to enforce arc consistency.

4271
06:40:26,030 --> 06:40:35,716
这样做之后，实际上我已经解决了整个问题。在给定这些约束、即A和B可以在周一、周二或周三考试的情况下，目前看来唯一的解是：
And in doing so, I've actually solved this entire problem. That given these constraints where A and B can have exams on either Monday or Tuesday or Wednesday, the only solution, as it would appear,

4272
06:40:35,918 --> 06:40:40,304
A的考试必须在周二，B的考试必须在周三。
is that A's exam must be on Tuesday and B's exam must be on Wednesday.

4273
06:40:40,494 --> 06:40:42,468
这是我目前唯一可用的选项。
And that is the only option available to me.

4274
06:40:43,822 --> 06:40:49,540
如果我们想把这种一致性应用到更大的图上，而不仅仅是看某一个特定的对，
So if we want to apply our consistency to a larger graph, not just looking at one particular pair of our consistency,

4275
06:40:49,824 --> 06:40:56,964
我们也可以这样做，并且可以开始正式化为了强制执行一致性的算法，伪代码应该长什么样。
there are ways we can do that too, and we can begin to formalize what the pseudocode would look like for trying to write an algorithm that enforces our consistency.

4276
06:40:57,486 --> 06:41:00,544
我们先从定义一个名为 修正 的函数开始。
And we'll start by defining a function called revise.

4277
06:41:01,070 --> 06:41:08,548
修正 将接收一个 约束满足问题（即约束满足问题）作为输入，以及两个变量 x 和 y。
Revise is going to take as input a CSP, otherwise known as a constraint satisfaction problem, and also two variables x and y.

4278
06:41:08,942 --> 06:41:17,184
修正 要做的是让 x 相对于 y 达到弧一致性，也就是说从 x 的定义域中移除
And what revise is going to do is it is going to make x arc consistent with respect to y, meaning remove anything from x's

4279
06:41:17,344 --> 06:41:20,772
任何不给 y 提供可能选项的项。
domain that doesn't allow for a possible option for y.

4280
06:41:21,710 --> 06:41:22,464
这是怎么运作的呢？
How does this work?

4281
06:41:22,830 --> 06:41:29,024
首先，我们要记录是否进行了修改。修正 最终会返回 true 或 false。
Well, we'll go ahead and first keep track of whether or not we've made a revision. Revise is ultimately going to return true or false.

4282
06:41:29,230 --> 06:41:33,344
如果我们对 X 的定义域进行了修改，它就会返回 true。
It'll return true in the event that we did make a revision to X's domain.

4283
06:41:33,550 --> 06:41:38,916
如果我们没有对 x 的定义域做任何更改，它就返回 false，稍后我们会看到为什么这样做很有用。
It'll return false if we didn't make any change to X's domain, and we'll see in a moment why that's going to be helpful.

4284
06:41:39,758 --> 06:41:42,884
但我们先声明 revised 等于 false，表示还没有进行任何更改。
But we start by saying revised equals false, we haven't made any changes.

4285
06:41:43,886 --> 06:41:48,800
然后我们说，好，让我们遍历 x 定义域中所有可能的值。
Then we'll say, all right, let's go ahead and loop over all of the possible values in X's domain.

4286
06:41:49,070 --> 06:41:57,520
也就是说，遍历 x 的定义域，对于 x 中的每一个小项 x，我要确保对于这些选择中的每一个，我在 y 中都有可用的选择
So loop over x's domain for each little x in x's domain, I want to make sure that for each of those choices, I have some available choice in y

4287
06:41:57,840 --> 06:42:04,516
来满足在我的 约束满足问题（约束满足问题）中定义的二元约束。
that satisfies the binary constraints that are defined inside of my CSP, inside of my constraint satisfaction problem.

4288
06:42:05,120 --> 06:42:05,440
所以，
So

4289
06:42:06,286 --> 06:42:13,700
如果出现这种情况：y 的定义域中没有任何值能满足 x 和 y 的约束，
if ever it's the case that there is no value y in y's domain that satisfies the constraint for x and y,

4290
06:42:14,766 --> 06:42:19,204
那么，这意味着这个值 x 不应该出现在 x 的定义域中。
well, if that's the case, that means that this value x shouldn't be in x's domain.

4291
06:42:19,886 --> 06:42:25,956
所以我会把 x 从 x 的定义域中删除，并将 revised 设置为 true，因为我确实修改了 x 的定义域。
So I'll go ahead and delete x from x's domain, and I'll set revised equal to true because I did change x's domain.

4292
06:42:26,080 --> 06:42:38,180
我通过移除小写 x 来修改 x 的定义域，之所以移除它是因为它不符合弧一致性。我根本无法为 y 选择一个能满足 xy 约束的值。
I changed x's domain by removing little x, and I removed little x because it wasn't art consistent. There was no way I could choose a value for y that would satisfy this xy constraint.

4293
06:42:39,342 --> 06:42:44,676
所以在这种情况下，我们会把 revised 设置为 true，并且对 x 定义域中的每一个值都重复这个过程。
So in this case we'll go ahead and set revised equal true, and we'll do this again and again for every value in x's domain.

4294
06:42:44,880 --> 06:42:53,028
有时这没问题，但在其他情况下，它可能导致 y 没有可选的选项，在这种情况下，我们需要从 x 的定义域中移除这个值。
Sometimes it might be fine, in other cases it might not allow for a possible choice for y, in which case we need to remove this value from x's domain.

4295
06:42:53,198 --> 06:42:57,988
最后，我们只需返回 revised 来表示我们是否真的做出了更改。
And at the end, we just return revised to indicate whether or not we actually made a change.

4296
06:42:59,022 --> 06:43:08,960
所以这个函数，也就是 修正 函数，实际上是刚才我在图形上演示的操作的实现，它能让一个变量 x 与另一个变量变得弧一致，
So this function then, this revised function, is effectively an implementation of what you saw me do graphically a moment ago, and it makes one variable, x, arc consistent with another variable,

4297
06:43:09,166 --> 06:43:09,988
在这种情况下就是 y。
in this case y.

4298
06:43:10,862 --> 06:43:20,068
但通常来说，当我们想要强制执行一致性时，我们往往不仅是针对单个弧，而是要让整个约束满足问题都达到弧一致性。
But generally speaking, when we want to enforce our consistency, we'll often want to enforce arc consistency not just for a single arc, but for the entire constraint satisfaction problem.

4299
06:43:20,430 --> 06:43:24,720
事实证明，也有一种算法可以做到这一点，那个算法被称为 AC3。
And it turns out there's an algorithm to do that as well, and that algorithm is known as AC3.

4300
06:43:25,166 --> 06:43:31,300
AC3 接收一个约束满足问题，并确保整个问题的弧一致性。
AC3 takes a constraint satisfaction problem and it enforces arc consistency across the entire problem.

4301
06:43:32,110 --> 06:43:32,800
它是怎么做到的呢？
How does it do that?

4302
06:43:33,102 --> 06:43:39,396
它基本上会维护一个队列，或者说就是一串所有需要变得一致的弧。
Well, it's going to basically maintain a queue, or basically just a line of all of the arcs that it needs to make consistent.

4303
06:43:39,726 --> 06:43:46,800
随着时间的推移，当我们开始处理弧一致性时，可能会从那个队列中移除一些内容，也可能需要向队列中添加一些内容
And over time, we might remove things from that queue as we begin dealing with arc consistency, and we might need to add things to that queue as well

4304
06:43:46,958 --> 06:43:49,700
如果还有更多需要让它们变得弧一致的东西。
if there are more things we need to make arc consistent.

4305
06:43:50,606 --> 06:43:56,388
所以我们将从一个包含约束满足问题中所有弧的队列开始，
So we'll go ahead and start with a queue that contains all of the arcs in the constraint satisfaction problem,

4306
06:43:56,560 --> 06:44:01,220
即连接两个具有某种二元约束的节点的所有边。
all of the edges that connect two nodes that have some sort of binary constraint between them.

4307
06:44:02,158 --> 06:44:06,160
现在，只要队列不为空，就还有工作要做。
And now, as long as the queue is non-empty, there is work to be done.

4308
06:44:06,320 --> 06:44:09,840
这个队列包含了所有我们需要让其变得弧一致的内容。
The queue is all of the things that we need to make arc consistent.

4309
06:44:10,062 --> 06:44:13,060
所以只要队列不为空，我们就还有任务要完成。
So as long as the queue is non-empty, there's still things we have to do.

4310
06:44:13,582 --> 06:44:14,372
我们要做什么呢？
What do we have to do?

4311
06:44:15,118 --> 06:44:19,440
我们将从队列中开始出队。从队列中移除一个元素。
Well, we'll start by dequeuing from the queue. Remove something from the queue.

4312
06:44:19,598 --> 06:44:23,108
严格来说，它不一定非得是一个队列，但用队列是处理这类问题的一种传统方式。
And strictly speaking, it doesn't need to be a queue, but a queue is a traditional way of doing this.

4313
06:44:23,438 --> 06:44:32,196
我们从队列中出队，这会给我们一个弧，即 x 和 y，这两个变量就是我想让 x 与 y 变得弧一致的变量。
We'll dequeue from the queue, and that'll give us an arc, x and y, these two variables where I would like to make x arc consistent with y.

4314
06:44:32,942 --> 06:44:35,600
那我们如何让 x 与 y 变得弧一致呢？
So how do we make x arc consistent with y?

4315
06:44:35,822 --> 06:44:39,360
嗯，我们可以直接使用刚才提到的那个 修正 函数。
Well, we can go ahead and just use that revise function that we talked about a moment ago.

4316
06:44:39,630 --> 06:44:48,160
我们调用 修正 函数，输入是约束满足问题，以及这些变量 x 和 y，因为我想让 x 与
We call the revise function, passing as input the constraint satisfaction problem, and also these variables x and y, because I want to make x arc

4317
06:44:48,320 --> 06:44:55,200
y 变得一致。换句话说，移除 x 定义域中任何不给 y 留下可用选项的数值。
consistent with y. In other words, remove any values from x's domain that don't leave an available option for y.

4318
06:44:55,854 --> 06:44:57,604
回想一下，修正 返回什么？
And recall, what does revised return?

4319
06:44:57,902 --> 06:45:06,320
它在我们确实做出更改时返回 true，比如因为没有给 y 提供可选方案而从 x 的定义域中删除了某些内容。
Well, it returns true if we actually made a change, if we removed something from X's domain because there wasn't an available option for y, for example.

4320
06:45:06,638 --> 06:45:10,340
而在我们完全没有对 x 的定义域做任何更改时，它返回 false。
And it returns false if we didn't make any change to x's domain at all.

4321
06:45:10,734 --> 06:45:17,040
结果证明，如果 修正 返回 false，也就是我们没做任何更改，那么对于这个弧，就没有太多工作要做。
And it turns out if revised returns false, if we didn't make any changes, well then there's not a whole lot more work to be done here for this arc.

4322
06:45:17,134 --> 06:45:19,524
我们可以直接处理队列中的下一个弧。
We can just move ahead to the next arc that's in the queue.

4323
06:45:20,622 --> 06:45:30,912
但如果我们做了更改，比如通过移除 x 定义域中的值来缩小 x 的定义域，那么我们可能会意识到这会导致后续出现问题，
But if we did make a change, if we did reduce x's domain by removing values from x's domain, well, then what we might realize is that this creates potential problems later on,

4324
06:45:31,150 --> 06:45:35,364
这意味着原本与 x 弧一致的某些弧，
that it might mean that some arc that was arc consistent with x.

4325
06:45:35,758 --> 06:45:41,252
那个节点可能不再与 x 弧一致了，因为虽然以前我们能为 x 选择一个选项，
that node might no longer be arc consistent with x, because while there used to be an option that we could choose for x,

4326
06:45:41,632 --> 06:45:48,836
但现在可能不行了，因为我们刚刚移除的某些属于 x 的内容，可能是为了让其他弧保持弧一致所必需的。
now, there might not be, because now we might have removed something from x that was necessary for some other arc to be arc consistent.

4327
06:45:49,230 --> 06:45:56,836
所以只要我们修改过 X 的定义域，我们就需要把一些东西加入到队列中，也就是一些我们需要检查的额外弧。
And so if ever we did revise X's domain, we're going to need to add some things to the queue, some additional arcs that we might want to check.

4328
06:45:57,294 --> 06:45:58,084
我们该怎么做呢？
How do we do that?

4329
06:45:58,606 --> 06:46:02,592
首先我们要检查的是确保 x 的定义域不是零。
Well, first thing we want to check is to make sure that x's domain is not zero.

4330
06:46:02,926 --> 06:46:10,592
如果 x 的定义域是零，意味着 x 完全没有可用的选项，这意味着你根本无法解决这个约束满足问题。
If x's domain is zero, that means there are no available options for x at all, and that means that there's no way you can solve the constraint satisfaction problem.

4331
06:46:10,798 --> 06:46:19,044
如果我们把 X 的定义域全部删除了，我们就直接在这里返回 false，表示由于 X 的定义域里没剩下任何东西，所以无法解决问题。
If we've removed everything from X's domain, we'll go ahead and just return false here to indicate there's no way to solve the problem because there's nothing left in X's domain.

4332
06:46:19,630 --> 06:46:20,388
否则，
But otherwise,

4333
06:46:21,422 --> 06:46:32,272
如果 X 的定义域里还有东西，只是比之前少一些，那么我们将遍历 x 所有邻居中除了 y 以外的每一个变量 z；
if there are things left in X's domain, but fewer things than before, well then what we'll do is we'll loop over each variable z that is in all of x's neighbors, except for y;

4334
06:46:32,432 --> 06:46:43,204
y 我们已经处理过了，但我们会考虑 x 的所有其他邻居，并问自己：好，那么从这些 z 到 x 的弧，可能不再是弧一致了。
y we already handled, but we'll consider all of x's other's neighbors and ask ourselves: all right, well that arc from each of those z to x, that arc might no longer be arc consistent.

4335
06:46:43,392 --> 06:46:51,556
因为虽然对于每个 z，之前可能都有一个可选的选项供我们为 x 选择以对应 z 的每一个可能值，但现在可能没有了
Because while for each z, there might have been a possible option and we could choose for x to correspond with each of z's possible values, now there might not be

4336
06:46:51,822 --> 06:46:54,148
因为我们从 x 的定义域中删除了一些元素。
because we removed some elements from x's domain.

4337
06:46:54,670 --> 06:47:02,052
所以我们在这里的操作是：对所有这些邻居 z，将弧 zx 入队，也就是添加到 Q 中。
And so what we'll do here is we'll go ahead and enqueue, adding something to the q, this arc zx, for all of those neighbors z.

4338
06:47:02,830 --> 06:47:08,356
因此我们需要把一些弧加回 Q 中，以便继续强制执行弧一致性。
So we need to add back some arcs to the q in order to continue to enforce arc consistency.

4339
06:47:09,198 --> 06:47:12,548
在最后，如果我们完成了所有这些过程，我们就可以返回 true。
At the very end, if we make it through all this process, then we can return true.

4340
06:47:13,678 --> 06:47:20,032
这就是 AC3，一种用于在约束满足问题上强制执行弧一致性的算法。
But this now is AC3, this algorithm for enforcing arc consistency on a constraint satisfaction problem.

4341
06:47:20,192 --> 06:47:28,228
核心思想其实就是记录下所有可能需要变得弧一致的弧，通过调用 修正 函数让它们变回弧一致。
And the big idea is really just keep track of all of the arcs that we might need to make arc consistent, make it arc consistent by calling the revise function.

4342
06:47:28,494 --> 06:47:36,356
如果我们对其进行了修改，那么就会有一些新的弧可能需要被添加到队列中，以确保即使在从某个变量的定义域中移除了一些元素后，所有内容依然是弧一致的。
and if we did revise it, then there are some new arcs that might need to be added to the queue in order to make sure that everything is still arc consistent.

4343
06:47:36,592 --> 06:47:41,060
即便是在我们删除了特定变量定义域中的某些元素之后。
even after we've removed some of the elements from a particular variable's domain.

4344
06:47:42,030 --> 06:47:51,268
那么如果我们尝试在一个这样的图上强制执行弧一致性会发生什么？在这个图中，每个变量的定义域都是周一、周二和周三。
So what then would happen if we tried to enforce arc consistency on a graph like this, on a graph where each of these variables has a domain of Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday?

4345
06:47:51,662 --> 06:47:57,092
结果发现，通过在这个图上强制执行弧一致性，它可以解决某些类型的问题。
Well, it turns out that by enforcing arc consistency on this graph, well, it can solve some types of problems.

4346
06:47:57,486 --> 06:47:59,392
这里实际上没有任何变化。
Nothing actually changes here.

4347
06:47:59,726 --> 06:48:08,672
对于任何特定的弧，即只考虑两个变量，我总有一种方法：无论我为其中一个做出的选择是什么，都能为另一个做出选择，
For any particular arc, just considering two variables, there's always a way for me to just, for any of the choices I make for one of them, make a choice for the other one,

4348
06:48:08,846 --> 06:48:12,352
因为有三个选项，而我只需要这两个不同即可。
because there are three options and I just need the two to be different from each other.

4349
06:48:12,654 --> 06:48:22,112
所以实际上非常容易就判定一个弧是弧一致的，因为如果我为 D 选择周一，那么我只需为 B 选择一个不是周一的选项就行了。
So this is actually quite easy to just take an arc and just declare that it is arc consistent, because if I pick, Monday for D, then I just pick something that isn't Monday for B.

4350
06:48:22,350 --> 06:48:31,716
在弧一致性中，我们只考虑两个节点之间的二元约束，我们还没有真正考虑到其他所有节点。
In arc consistency, we only consider consistency between a binary constraint between two nodes, and we're not really considering all of the rest of the nodes yet.

4351
06:48:32,494 --> 06:48:40,868
所以仅仅使用 AC3，即强制执行弧一致性，有时可以起到缩小定义域的作用，从而让寻找解变得更容易，
So just using AC3, the enforcement of arc consistency, that can sometimes have the effect of reducing domains to make it easier to find solutions,

4352
06:48:41,230 --> 06:48:43,780
但它并不总是能真正解决问题。
but it will not always actually solve the problem.

4353
06:48:44,174 --> 06:48:47,780
我们可能仍需要通过某种搜索来尝试找到一个解。
We might still need to somehow search to try and find a solution.

4354
06:48:48,302 --> 06:48:51,712
我们可以使用传统的经典搜索算法来尝试这样做。
And we can use classical traditional search algorithms to try to do so.

4355
06:48:51,982 --> 06:48:55,152
你们会记得，一个搜索问题通常由这些部分组成：
You'll recall that a search problem generally consists of these parts.

4356
06:48:55,312 --> 06:49:05,252
我们有一些初始状态、一些动作、一个将我从一个状态带到另一个状态的状态转移模型，以及一个用来判断我是否正确达成目标的目标测试，
We have some initial state, some actions, a transition model that takes me from one state to another state, a goal test to tell me have I satisfied my objective correctly,

4357
06:49:05,582 --> 06:49:11,460
还有一些路径代价函数，因为在解决迷宫的情况下，我正试图尽可能快地到达目标。
and then some path cost function, because in the case of maze solving, I was trying to get to my goal as quickly as possible.

4358
06:49:12,192 --> 06:49:18,436
所以你可以把约束满足问题（约束满足问题）建模为这类搜索问题之一。
So you could formulate a CSP or a constraint satisfaction problem as one of these types of search problems.

4359
06:49:18,832 --> 06:49:27,312
初始状态将仅仅是一个空赋值，其中“赋值”就是我将特定变量分配给特定值的一种方式。
The initial state will just be an empty assignment, where an assignment is just a way for me to assign any particular variable to any particular value.

4360
06:49:27,662 --> 06:49:31,236
所以如果是一个空赋值，意味着还没有任何变量被分配到任何值上，
So if an empty assignment is no variables are assigned to any values yet,

4361
06:49:31,950 --> 06:49:39,872
那么我可以采取的动作就是向该赋值中添加一些“变量等于值”的对，也就是说对于这个赋值，
then the action I can take is adding some new variable equals value pair to that assignment, saying for this assignment,

4362
06:49:40,032 --> 06:49:42,212
让我为这个变量添加一个新值。
let me add a new value for this variable.

4363
06:49:42,894 --> 06:49:50,436
而状态转移模型只是定义了当你采取那个动作时会发生什么。你会得到一个新的包含该变量等于该值的赋值。
And the transition model just defines what happens when you take that action. You get a new assignment that has that variable equal to that value inside of it.

4364
06:49:51,086 --> 06:49:57,092
目标测试就是检查确保所有变量都已分配，并确保所有约束都已满足。
The goal test is just checking to make sure all the variables have been assigned and making sure all the constraints have been satisfied.

4365
06:49:57,632 --> 06:50:02,592
而路径代价函数在这里就无关紧密了。我并不真的在乎路径到底是什么样子的。
and the path cost function is sort of irrelevant. I don't really care about what the path really is.

4366
06:50:02,766 --> 06:50:07,332
我只关心找到一个能满足所有约束的赋值。
I just care about finding some assignment that actually satisfies all of the constraints.

4367
06:50:07,662 --> 06:50:09,552
所以实际上，所有的路径成本都是一样的。
So really all the paths have the same cost.

4368
06:50:09,632 --> 06:50:12,036
我并不在乎通往目标的路径。
I don't really care about the path to the goal.

4369
06:50:12,272 --> 06:50:16,100
我只关心解本身，就像我们之前讨论过的那样。
I just care about the solution itself, much as we've talked about now before.

4370
06:50:17,230 --> 06:50:25,776
然而这里的问题是，如果我们只是简单地实现这个幼稚的搜索算法，比如通过广度优先搜索或深度优先搜索，这将会非常、非常低效。
The problem here though is that if we just implement this naive search algorithm just by implementing like breadth-first search or depth-first search, this is going to be very, very inefficient.

4371
06:50:25,902 --> 06:50:31,460
而且我们有一些方法可以利用约束满足问题本身结构中的高效性。
And there are ways we can take advantage of efficiencies in the structure of a constraint satisfaction problem itself.

4372
06:50:31,918 --> 06:50:39,776
其中一个核心思想是我们可以对这些变量进行排序，而无论我们按什么顺序分配变量并不重要。
And one of the key ideas is that we can really just order these variables, and it doesn't matter what order we assign variables in.

4373
06:50:39,936 --> 06:50:47,204
“a 等于 2 再到 b 等于 8”的赋值与“b 等于 8 再到 a 等于 2”的赋值是完全相同的。
The assignment a equals two and then b equals eight is identical to the assignment of b equals eight and then a equals two.

4374
06:50:47,616 --> 06:50:52,548
改变顺序并不会改变该赋值的基本性质。
Switching the order doesn't really change anything about the fundamental nature of that assignment.

4375
06:50:53,294 --> 06:51:01,732
因此，我们可以尝试对搜索算法这一概念进行一些修正，以便专门应用于像约束满足问题这样的问题。
And so there are some ways that we can try and revise this idea of a search algorithm to apply it specifically for a problem like a constraint satisfaction problem.

4376
06:51:02,190 --> 06:51:08,996
事实证明，我们在讨论约束满足问题时通常会使用的搜索算法是被称为回溯搜索的算法。
And it turns out the search algorithm we'll generally use when talking about constraint satisfaction problems is something known as backtracking search.

4377
06:51:09,358 --> 06:51:14,532
而且回溯搜索的核心思想是，我们会继续对变量进行赋值。
And the big idea of backtracking search is we'll go ahead and make assignments from variables to values.

4378
06:51:14,830 --> 06:51:22,980
如果我们卡住了，也就是说我们到达了一个在保留必须遵守的约束的同时无法再向前推进的地方，
And if ever we get stuck, we arrive at a place where there is no way we can make any forward progress while still preserving the constraints that we need to enforce.

4379
06:51:23,598 --> 06:51:26,628
我们就会回溯并尝试别的东西。
We'll go ahead and backtrack and try something else instead.

4380
06:51:27,630 --> 06:51:35,332
所以回溯搜索的基本轮廓如下：它看起来像是一个名为 回溯 的函数，它接受一个赋值作为输入
So the very basic sketch of what backtracking search looks like is it looks like this a function called backtrack that takes as input an assignment

4381
06:51:35,726 --> 06:51:37,540
以及一个约束满足问题。
and a constraint satisfaction problem.

4382
06:51:37,838 --> 06:51:40,256
所以最初，我们没有任何已分配的变量。
So initially, we don't have any assigned variables.

4383
06:51:40,398 --> 06:51:45,776
因此当我们开始回溯搜索时，这个赋值只是一个不包含任何变量的空赋值。
So when we begin backtracking search, this assignment is just going to be the empty assignment with no variables inside of it.

4384
06:51:46,062 --> 06:51:48,452
但稍后我们会看到这是一个递归函数。
But we'll see later this is going to be a recursive function.

4385
06:51:49,422 --> 06:51:52,132
所以 回溯 函数接收赋值和问题作为输入。
So backtrack takes as input the assignment and the problem.

4386
06:51:53,262 --> 06:51:58,884
如果赋值已完成，意味着所有变量都已分配，我们就返回该赋值。
If the assignment is complete, meaning all of the variables have been assigned, we just return that assignment.

4387
06:51:59,246 --> 06:52:02,564
当然，最初不会是这种情况，因为我们从空赋值开始。
That of course won't be true initially, because we start with an empty assignment.

4388
06:52:02,766 --> 06:52:04,816
但随着时间的推移，我们可能会向这个赋值中添加内容。
But over time we might add things to that assignment.

4389
06:52:04,942 --> 06:52:07,776
所以如果赋值确实完成了，那我们就结束了。
So if ever the assignment actually is complete, then we're done.

4390
06:52:07,982 --> 06:52:10,212
直接返回那个赋值即可。
Then just go ahead and return that assignment.

4391
06:52:10,862 --> 06:52:12,484
否则，还有工作要做。
But otherwise, there's some work to be done.

4392
