我们希望计算机能做的是，让我们的 AI 能够找出将输入映射到输出的某种函数。
And what we would like the computer to do is we would like our AI to be able to figure out some function that maps inputs to outputs.

4699
07:20:27,374 --> 07:20:33,380
所以我们有一大堆数据，通常包含一些输入、一些证据、一些信息，这些是计算机可以获取的。
So we have a whole bunch of data that generally consists of some kind of input, some evidence, some information that the computer will have access to.

4700
07:20:33,774 --> 07:20:39,652
我们希望计算机根据这些输入信息，来预测某些输出将会是什么。
And we would like the computer, based on that input information, to predict what some output is going to be.

4701
07:20:39,982 --> 07:20:48,932
我们会给它一些数据，让计算机在上面进行模型训练，从而开始理解这些信息是如何运作的，以及输入和输出是如何相互关联的。
And we'll give it some data so that the computer can train its model on to begin to understand how it is that this information works and how it is that the inputs and outputs relate to each other.

4702
07:20:49,454 --> 07:20:55,876
但最终，我们希望我们的计算机能够找到某种函数，在给定这些输入的情况下，能够得到相应的输出。
But ultimately, we hope that our computer will be able to figure out some function that, given those inputs, is able to get those outputs.

4703
07:20:56,622 --> 07:20:59,232
监督学习中包含几种不同的任务。
There are a couple of different tasks within supervised learning.

4704
07:20:59,438 --> 07:21:02,564
我们将重点关注并首先开始的是被称为分类的任务。
The one we'll focus on and start with is known as classification.

4705
07:21:02,798 --> 07:21:11,392
分类是这样一个问题：如果我给你一大堆输入，你需要找到某种方法将这些输入映射到离散类别中，
And classification is the problem where if I give you a whole bunch of inputs, you need to figure out some way to map those inputs into discrete categories,

4706
07:21:11,566 --> 07:21:17,152
你可以决定这些类别是什么，而计算机的工作就是预测这些类别将会是什么。
where you can decide what those categories are, and it's the job of the computer to predict what those categories are going to be.

4707
07:21:17,358 --> 07:21:26,212
例如，我给你关于一张钞票的信息，比如一张美元，我要求你预测它是否属于真币类别，
So that might be, for example, I give you information about a banknote, like a US dollar, and I'm asking you to predict for me does it belong to the category of authentic banknotes,

4708
07:21:26,446 --> 07:21:29,060
或者它属于假币类别？
or does it belong to the category of counterfeit banknotes?

4709
07:21:29,472 --> 07:21:35,236
你需要对输入进行分类，我们希望训练计算机去找出某种函数来完成这项计算。
You need to categorize the input, and we want to train the computer to figure out some function to be able to do that calculation.

4710
07:21:36,110 --> 07:21:44,672
另一个例子可能是天气情况，这是我们在本课程中已经讨论过一点的内容，即我们想预测在给定的某一天，那天是否会下雨。
Another example might be the case of weather, something we've talked about a little bit so far in this class, where we would like to predict on a given day, is it going to rain on that day,

4711
07:21:44,910 --> 07:21:46,244
那天天气会阴天吗？
is it going to be cloudy on that day?

4712
07:21:46,574 --> 07:21:54,532
在看我们如何通过给计算机提供所有精确概率来处理——如果满足这些条件，下雨的概率是多少——之前，
And before we've seen how we could do this if we really give the computer all the exact probabilities for, if these are the conditions, what's the probability of rain?

4713
07:21:54,766 --> 07:22:00,196
虽然我们往往无法获得那些信息，但我们拥有大量的数据。
Oftentimes we don't have access to that information though, but what we do have access to is a whole bunch of data.

4714
07:22:00,622 --> 07:22:08,272
所以如果我们想预测诸如“是否会下雨”这类问题，我们可以给计算机提供关于过去这些日子的历史信息，包括下雨的日子和没下雨的日期，
So if we wanted to be able to predict something like, is it going to rain or is it not going to rain, we would give the computer historical information about days when it was

4715
07:22:08,272 --> 07:22:13,668
并让计算机去这些数据中寻找规律。
raining and days when it was not raining, and ask the computer to look for patterns in that data.

4716
07:22:14,126 --> 07:22:15,428
那么这些数据可能长什么样呢？
So what might that data look like?

4717
07:22:15,758 --> 07:22:18,192
嗯，我们可以把这些数据结构化成这样一个表格。
Well, we could structure that data in a table like this.

4718
07:22:18,432 --> 07:22:27,872
这可能是我们表格的样子：对于任何特定的日期，我们都有关于那天的湿度、气压等信息，而且重要的是，我们还有一个标签，
might be what our table looks like, where for any particular day, going back, we have information about that day's humidity, that day's air pressure, and then importantly, we have a label,

4719
07:22:28,110 --> 07:22:32,752
即人类标注出的在特定日期是下雨还是没下雨。
something where the human has said that on this particular day it was raining or it was not raining.

4720
07:22:33,006 --> 07:22:42,272
你可以用大量数据填满这个表格，而之所以称之为监督学习练习，是因为有人去标注了每一个数据点。
So you could fill in this table with a whole bunch of data, and what makes this what we would call a supervised learning exercise is that a human has gone in and labeled each of these data points.

4721
07:22:42,432 --> 07:22:48,612
标注为：当湿度和压力达到这些数值时，那天是下雨天；而这一天不是下雨天。
Said that on this day, when these were the values for the humidity and pressure, that day was a rainy day, and this day was a not rainy day.

4722
07:22:49,230 --> 07:22:58,272
然后我们希望计算机能够做到的是，根据这些输入，比如湿度和压力，判断出应该给那一天分配什么标签。
And what we would like the computer to be able to do then is to be able to figure out, given these inputs, given like the humidity and the pressure, can the computer predict what label

4723
07:22:58,432 --> 07:22:59,712
应该与那一天相关联？
should be associated with that day?

4724
07:22:59,872 --> 07:23:05,700
那天看起来更像是下雨天，还是更像没下雨的日期？
Does that day look more like it's going to be a day that rains, or does it look more like a day when it's not going to rain?

4725
07:23:06,606 --> 07:23:14,752
用稍微数学一点的方式来说，你可以把它看作一个接收两个输入的函数，这些输入就是我们的计算机可以获取到的数据点，
Put a little bit more mathematically, you can think of this as a function that takes two inputs, the inputs being the data points that our computer will have access to,

4726
07:23:14,832 --> 07:23:16,272
比如湿度和压力。
things like humidity and pressure.

4727
07:23:16,558 --> 07:23:20,004
所以我们可以写一个函数 f，它接收湿度和压力作为输入。
So we could write a function f that takes as input, both humidity and pressure.

4728
07:23:20,526 --> 07:23:29,072
然后输出将是我们给这些特定输入点分配的类别，即与该输入关联的标签。
And then the output is going to be what category we would ascribe to these particular input points, what label we would associate with that input.

4729
07:23:29,262 --> 07:23:37,392
我们在这里看到了一些示例数据点：给定湿度和压力的数值，我们预测是下雨还是没下雨。
So we've seen a couple of example data points here, where given this value for humidity and this value for pressure, we predict is it going to rain or is it not going to rain?

4730
07:23:37,552 --> 07:23:40,432
这些信息是我们从现实世界中收集到的。
And that's information that we just gathered from the world.

4731
07:23:40,592 --> 07:23:47,556
我们在不同日期测量了湿度和压力，并观察到那天到底有没有下雨。
We measured on various different days what the humidity and pressure were, we observed whether or not we saw rain or no rain on that particular day.

4732
07:23:48,046 --> 07:23:51,428
而这个函数 f 就是我们想要去拟合的对象。
And this function f is what we would like to approximate.

4733
07:23:51,822 --> 07:23:55,552
现在，计算机和我们人类其实并不完全清楚这个函数 f 是如何运作的。
Now the computer and we humans don't really know exactly how this function f works.

4734
07:23:55,632 --> 07:23:57,156
它可能是一个非常复杂的函数。
It's probably quite a complex function.

4735
07:23:57,806 --> 07:24:00,548
所以我们要做的就是尝试去估算它。
So what we're going to do instead is attempt to estimate it.

4736
07:24:00,942 --> 07:24:04,272
我们希望建立一个假设函数 h，
We would like to come up with a hypothesis function, h,

4737
07:24:05,102 --> 07:24:08,112
它将试图去拟合 f 的功能。
which is going to try to approximate what f does.

4738
07:24:08,272 --> 07:24:15,312
我们想要构建一个函数 h，它同样接收相同的输入，并产生相应的输出：下雨或没下雨。
We want to come up with some function h that will also take the same inputs and will also produce an output, rain or no rain.

4739
07:24:15,694 --> 07:24:19,492
理想情况下，我们希望这两个函数尽可能一致。
And ideally, we'd like these two functions to agree as much as possible.

4740
07:24:19,982 --> 07:24:26,752
因此，监督学习分类任务的目标就是找出这个函数 h 长什么样。
So the goal then of the supervised learning classification tasks is going to be to figure out what does that function h look like?

4741
07:24:26,912 --> 07:24:34,468
考虑到所有这些信息和数据，我们该如何开始评估给特定数据点分配什么类别或标签？
How can we begin to estimate, given all of this information, in all of this data, what category or what label should be assigned to a particular data point?

4742
07:24:35,278 --> 07:24:36,992
那么，从哪里开始做起呢？
So where could you begin doing this?

4743
07:24:37,358 --> 07:24:43,152
嗯，在这种情况下的一个合理的做法是，因为我有两个数值，我可以尝试把它们绘制到
Well, a reasonable thing to do, especially in this situation, I have two numerical values, is I could try to plot this on

4744
07:24:43,952 --> 07:24:46,948
一个拥有两个轴的图表上，即 x 轴和 y 轴。
a graph that has two axes, an x-axis and a y-axis.

4745
07:24:47,438 --> 07:24:53,952
在这种情况下，我们只使用两个数值作为输入，但随着你增加更多输入，这种思路同样适用。
And in this case, we're just going to be using two numerical values as input, but these same types of ideas scale as you add more and more inputs as well.

4746
07:24:54,112 --> 07:25:00,592
我们将东西绘制在二维空间中，但正如我们很快会看到的，你可以增加更多输入，并想象多维空间中的情况。
We'll be plotting things in two dimensions, but as we'll soon see, you could add more inputs and just imagine things in multiple dimensions.

4747
07:25:00,672 --> 07:25:10,032
虽然我们人类很难在视觉上构思出超出三维以上的任何事物，但对于计算机来说，在更多维度中去思考没有任何问题。
And while we humans have trouble conceptualizing anything really beyond three dimensions, at least visually, a computer has no problem with trying to imagine things in many, many more dimensions.

4748
07:25:10,192 --> 07:25:14,352
因为对计算机而言，每个维度只是它记录的一个独立数字。
That for a computer, each dimension is just some separate number that it is keeping track of.

4749
07:25:14,446 --> 07:25:20,484
所以，如果为了解决问题而让计算机在十维或一百维空间中思考，也是合理的。
So it wouldn't be unreasonable for a computer to think in ten dimensions or 100 dimensions to be able to try to solve a problem.

4750
07:25:20,814 --> 07:25:28,708
但目前我们有两个输入，所以我们将事物绘制在两个轴上：x 轴代表湿度，y 轴代表气压。
But for now we've got two inputs, so we'll graph things along two axes, an x-axis, which will here represent humidity, and a y axis, which here represents pressure.

4751
07:25:29,358 --> 07:25:36,912
我们可以这样做：把所有下雨的日子都找出来，尝试把它们画在这个图表上，看看它们落在什么位置。
And what we might do is say, let's take all of the days that were raining and just try to plot them on this graph and see where they fall on this graph.

4752
07:25:37,006 --> 07:25:45,892
这些可能是所有的雨天，每个雨天都是这里的一个蓝色点，对应特定的湿度值和气压值。
And here might be all of the rainy days, where each rainy day is one of these blue dots here that corresponds to a particular value for humidity and a particular value for pressure.

4753
07:25:46,766 --> 07:25:48,992
然后我可以用同样的方法处理没下雨的日子。
And then I might do the same thing with the days that were not rainy.

4754
07:25:49,262 --> 07:25:56,420
比如找出所有没下雨的日期，确定它们在这两个输入中的数值，并把它们也画到这个图表上。
Say take all the not rainy days, figure out what their values were for each of these two inputs, and go ahead and plot them on this graph as well.

4755
07:25:56,878 --> 07:25:58,032
我在这里用红色标注了它们。
And I've here plotted them in red.

4756
07:25:58,112 --> 07:26:02,180
所以这里的蓝色代表雨天，红色代表没下雨的日期。
So blue here stands for a rainy day, red here stands for a not rainy day.

4757
07:26:02,734 --> 07:26:06,372
这就是我的计算机可以获取到的所有输入信息。
And this then is the input that my computer has access to all of this input.

4758
07:26:07,022 --> 07:26:15,268
我希望电脑能够做到的是训练一个模型，这样当我面对一个新的、没有关联标签的输入时，
And what I would like the computer to be able to do is to train a model such that if I'm ever presented with a new input, that doesn't have a label associated with it,

4759
07:26:15,552 --> 07:26:17,508
比如这个白点一样的东西，
something like this white dot here.

4760
07:26:18,030 --> 07:26:26,592
我希望能根据这两个输入的数值来预测：我们应该把它归类为蓝点（雨天），还是红点（没下雨的日期）？
I would like to predict, given those values for each of the two inputs, is: should we classify it as a blue dot, a rainy day, or should we classify it as a red dot?

4761
07:26:26,862 --> 07:26:27,588
也就是非雨天？
a not rainy day?

4762
07:26:28,494 --> 07:26:33,872
如果你只是从图形上观察这张图，试图判断这个白点是属于蓝色类别，
And if you're just looking at this picture graphically, trying to say, all right, this white dot, does it look like it belongs to the blue category,

4763
07:26:33,952 --> 07:26:36,068
还是属于红色类别？
or does it look like it belongs to the red category?

4764
07:26:36,432 --> 07:26:40,192
我认为大多数人都会同意它可能属于蓝色类别。
I think most people would agree that it probably belongs to the blue category.

4765
07:26:40,272 --> 07:26:44,516
为什么呢？因为它看起来离其他的蓝点很近。
And why is that? Well, it looks like it's close to other blue dots.

4766
07:26:45,198 --> 07:26:48,912
这并不是一个非常正式的概念，但我们马上就会把它形式化。
And that's not a very formal notion, but it's a notion that we'll formalize in just a moment.

4767
07:26:49,006 --> 07:26:56,432
因为它似乎离这个蓝点很近，没有其他东西比它更近，那么我们可以说它应该被归类为蓝色。
That because it seems to be close to this blue dot here, like nothing else is closer to it, then we might say that it should be categorized as blue.

4768
07:26:56,592 --> 07:27:01,472
基于这些输入，它应该落入那个类别，即我认为那天会是雨天。
It should fall into that category of I think that day is going to be a rainy day, based on that input.

4769
07:27:01,712 --> 07:27:04,032
虽然可能不是百分之百准确，但这是一个相当不错的
Might not be totally accurate, but it's a pretty good

4770
07:27:04,032 --> 07:27:11,472
推测。而这种类型的算法实际上是一种非常流行且常见的机器学习算法，被称为“最近邻分类”。
guess. And this type of algorithm is actually a very popular and common machine learning algorithm known as nearest neighbor classification.

4771
07:27:11,694 --> 07:27:18,192
这是一个用于解决这类分类问题的算法。在最近邻分类中，它会执行这个算法。
It's an algorithm for solving these classification type problems. And in nearest neighbor classification, it's going to perform this algorithm.

4772
07:27:18,272 --> 07:27:24,352
它的做法是：给定一个输入，它会选择离该输入最近的数据点的类别。
What it'll do is given an input, it will choose the class of the nearest data point to that input.

4773
07:27:24,558 --> 07:27:29,316
这里的“类别”指的就是类别，比如下雨或不下雨，伪造或非伪造。
By class, we just here mean category, like rain or no rain, counterfeit or not counterfeit.

4774
07:27:29,742 --> 07:27:34,116
我们根据最接近的数据点来选择类别。
And we choose the category or the class based on the nearest data point.

4775
07:27:34,638 --> 07:27:39,460
所以面对所有这些数据时，我们只需看最近的数据点是蓝色点还是红色点？
So given all that data, we just looked at is the nearest data point a blue point or is it a red point?

4776
07:27:39,918 --> 07:27:44,432
根据这个问题的答案，我们就能做出某种判断。
And depending on the answer to that question, we were able to make some sort of judgment.

4777
07:27:44,592 --> 07:27:48,452
我们可以说，我们认为它是蓝色的，或者我们认为它是
We were able to say something like, we think it's going to be blue or we think it's going to be

4778
07:27:48,512 --> 07:27:52,432
红色的。同样，我们也可以把这个应用到我们遇到的其他数据点上。
red. So likewise we could apply this to other data points that we encounter as well.

4779
07:27:52,750 --> 07:27:59,396
如果突然出现这个数据点，嗯，它的最近邻是红色，所以我们就把它分类为红色点，即不下雨。
If suddenly this data point comes about, well, its nearest data is red, so we would go ahead and classify this as a red point, not raining.

4780
07:28:00,206 --> 07:28:05,092
不过，当你看到像这里这个白色点时，情况就变得有点复杂了。
Things get a little bit trickier though, when you look at a point like this white point over here.

4781
07:28:05,710 --> 07:28:06,992
你问同样的问题。
And you ask the same sort of question.

4782
07:28:07,232 --> 07:28:13,952
它应该属于蓝色点的类别（下雨天），还是属于红色点的类别（不下雨的
Should it belong to the category of blue points, the rainy days, or should it belong to the category of red points, the not rainy

4783
07:28:13,952 --> 07:28:20,832
日子）？现在，最近邻分类会说，解决这个问题的方法是看哪个点离它最近。
days? Now, nearest neighbor classification would say the way you solve this problem is look at which point is nearest to that point.

4784
07:28:20,992 --> 07:28:28,932
你看这个最近的点，它是红色的，是一个不下雨的日子，因此，根据最近邻分类，我会说这个未标记的点
You look at this nearest point and say it's red, it's a not rainy day, and therefore, according to nearest neighbor classification, I would say that this unlabeled point,

4785
07:28:29,230 --> 07:28:32,900
嗯，它也应该是红色的。它也应该被分类为不下雨的一天。
well, that should also be red. It should also be classified as a not rainy day.

4786
07:28:33,742 --> 07:28:41,220
但你的直觉可能会认为这是一个合理的判断，既然最近的东西是不下雨的一天，那干脆就猜它是不下雨的一天。
But your intuition, might think that that's a reasonable judgment to make, that it's the closest thing is a not rainy day, so may as well guess that it's a not rainy day.

4787
07:28:41,486 --> 07:28:49,220
但从大局来看，可能也是合理的，即：是的，它最近的点确实是一个红点，
But it's probably also reasonable to look at the bigger picture of things, and to say, yes, it is true that the nearest point to it was a red point,

4788
07:28:49,582 --> 07:28:52,420
但它被一大堆其他的蓝点包围着。
but it's surrounded by a whole bunch of other blue points.

4789
07:28:53,070 --> 07:28:58,820
所以从大局来看，有理由认为这个点实际上应该是蓝色的。
So looking at the bigger picture, there's potentially an argument to be made that this point should actually be blue.

4790
07:28:59,310 --> 07:29:01,392
而仅凭这些数据，我们其实无法确定。
And with only this data, we actually don't know for sure.

4791
07:29:01,632 --> 07:29:10,148
我们得到了一些输入，即我们试图预测的东西，但我们并不一定知道输出会是什么。所以在这种情况下，很难说哪一个才是正确的。
We are given some input, something we're trying to predict, and we don't necessarily know what the output is going to be. So in this case, which one is correct is difficult to say.

4792
07:29:10,432 --> 07:29:17,444
但通常情况下，考虑多个邻居而不仅仅是一个邻居，有时能给我们更好的结果。
But oftentimes considering more than just a single neighbor, considering multiple neighbors, can sometimes give us a better result.

4793
07:29:18,158 --> 07:29:26,032
因此，有一种变体叫做 K 最近邻分类算法，其中 k
