5085
07:57:54,128 --> 07:58:01,124
这取决于数据集、你能获取到的信息，以及你最终想要预测的函数长什么样。
It's going to depend on the data set, the information you have access to, it's going to depend on what the function looks like that you're ultimately trying to predict.

5086
07:58:01,262 --> 07:58:08,688
而这就是很多研究和实验发挥作用的地方，即去探索如何最好地进行这类预测。
And this is where a lot of research and experimentation can be involved in trying to figure out how it is to best perform that kind of estimation.

5087
07:58:09,582 --> 07:58:14,372
但分类只是你在监督式机器学习中可能遇到的任务之一。
But classification is only one of the tasks that you might encounter in supervised machine learning.

5088
07:58:14,702 --> 07:58:19,360
因为在分类中，我们试图预测的是某些离散类别。
Because in classification, what we're trying to predict is some discrete category.

5089
07:58:19,520 --> 07:58:24,100
我们尝试预测是红色还是蓝色，下雨或没下雨，真品或伪造品。
We're trying to predict red or blue, rain or not rain, authentic or counterfeit.

5090
07:58:24,910 --> 07:58:27,908
但有时我们想要预测的是一个实数。
But sometimes what we want to predict is a real numbered value.

5091
07:58:28,302 --> 07:58:32,900
针对这种情况，我们有一个相关的、不是分类而是被称为回归的问题。
And for that we have a related problem, not classification, but instead known as regression.

5092
07:58:33,390 --> 07:58:42,560
回归是监督式学习中的一种问题，其中我们试图学习一个将输入映射到输出的函数，与之前一样，但不同的是输出不再是离散类别，
And regression is the supervised learning problem where we try and learn a function mapping inputs to outputs, same as before, but instead of the outputs being discrete categories,

5093
07:58:42,734 --> 07:58:51,428
比如下雨或没下雨这类东西。在回归问题中，输出值通常是连续值，是我们想要预测的某个实数。
things like rain or not rain, in a regression problem, the output values are generally continuous values, some real number that we would like to predict.

5094
07:58:52,014 --> 07:58:53,200
这种情况也经常发生。
This happens all the time as well.

5095
07:58:53,454 --> 07:58:59,520
你可以想象一家公司如果想弄清楚广告的效果，可能会采用这种方法。
You might imagine that a company might take this approach if it's trying to figure out, for instance, what the effect of its advertising is.

5096
07:58:59,680 --> 07:59:05,252
例如，投入的广告费用如何转化为公司产品的销量。
Like how do advertising dollars spent translate into sales for the company's product, for example.

5097
07:59:05,806 --> 07:59:11,520
因此他们可能想尝试预测一个函数，该函数以广告支出金额作为输入。
And so they might like to try to predict some function that takes as input the amount of money spent on advertising.

5098
07:59:11,680 --> 07:59:18,276
这里我们只使用一个输入，但同样地，如果你有大量不同类型的数据可以利用，你也可以将其扩展到更多输入。
And here we're just going to use one input, but again, you could scale this up to many more inputs as well if you have a lot of different kinds of data you have access to.

5099
07:59:18,670 --> 07:59:23,680
目标是学习一个函数，根据给定的广告支出金额，得出相应的销售额。
And the goal is to learn a function that given this amount of spending on advertising, we're going to get this amount in sales.

5100
07:59:23,760 --> 07:59:32,036
你可以基于大量数据来进行判断，比如过去每个月我们花了多少广告费，以及当时的销售情况。
And you might judge based on having access to a whole bunch of data, like for every past month, here is how much we spent on advertising, and here is what sales were.

5101
07:59:32,270 --> 07:59:40,640
我们想要预测一种假设函数，同样是根据广告支出的金额来预测，在这种情况下，
And we would like to predict some sort of hypothesis function that again, given the amount spent on advertising, can predict, in this case,

5102
07:59:40,800 --> 07:59:50,980
它是一个实数，一个关于公司本月、本季度或我们选择的任何时间单位内预期销售额的数值估计。
some real number, some number estimate of how much sales we expect that company to do in this month or in this quarter or whatever unit of time we're choosing to measure things in.

5103
07:59:51,886 --> 07:59:59,652
所以，同样地，解决这类问题的方法是，我们可以尝试使用线性回归这种方法，把这些数据拿出来并画成图。
And so again, the approach to solving this type of problem, we could try using a linear regression type approach where we take this data and we just plot it.

5104
07:59:59,918 --> 08:00:07,840
在 x-axis 上我们有广告支出金额，在 y-axis 上我们有销售额，我们可能只是想试着画出一条能够很好地
On the x-axis we have advertising dollars spent, on the y-axis we have sales, and we might just want to try and draw a line that does a pretty good

5105
08:00:07,840 --> 08:00:12,720
去估算广告与销售之间这种关系的线。
job of trying to estimate this relationship between advertising and sales.

5106
08:00:12,880 --> 08:00:18,960
在这种情况下，与之前不同的是，我们不是试图将数据点划分到离散类别中，而是，在这种情况中，
And in this case, unlike before, we're not trying to separate the data points into discrete categories, but instead, in this case,

5107
08:00:19,040 --> 08:00:24,880
我们只是试图找一条能拟合广告和销售之间这种关系的线。
we're just trying to find a line that approximates this relationship between advertising and sales.

5108
08:00:25,040 --> 08:00:33,200
这样，如果我们想算出特定广告预算下的预估销售额，只需在这一条线上查一下，看看对于这么多广告支出，
So that if we want to figure out what the estimated sales are for a particular advertising budget, you just look it up in this line, figure out for this amount of advertising,

5109
08:00:33,360 --> 08:00:37,120
我们能获得多少销售额，并以此来进行预测。
we would have this amount of sales, and just try and make the estimate that way.

5110
08:00:37,422 --> 08:00:46,148
所以你可以尝试画出一条线，再次强调，通过各种不同的技术来调整权重，试图让这条线尽可能完美地拟合数据。
And so you can try and come up with a line, again, figuring out how to modify the weights using various different techniques to try and make it so that this line fits as well as possible.

5111
08:00:47,694 --> 08:00:54,788
那么，在这些试图解决机器学习风格问题的方法中，问题变成了我们如何评估这些方法？
So, with all of these approaches then to trying to solve machine learning style problems, the question becomes how do we evaluate these approaches?

5112
08:00:54,960 --> 08:00:59,200
我们该如何评估我们能提出的各种不同的假设？
How do we evaluate the various different hypotheses that we could come up with?

5113
08:00:59,280 --> 08:01:09,124
因为每种算法都会给我们提供某种假设，即一个将输入映射到输出的函数，而我们想知道这个函数的效果如何。
Because each of these algorithms will give us some sort of hypothesis, some function that maps inputs to outputs, and we want to know how well does that function work.

5114
08:01:09,582 --> 08:01:16,132
你可以把评估这些假设并试图获得更好的假设，看作是一个优化问题。
And you can think of evaluating these hypotheses and trying to get a better hypothesis as kind of like an optimization problem.

5115
08:01:16,366 --> 08:01:18,724
在优化问题中，正如你之前提到的，
In an optimization problem, as you recall from before,

5116
08:01:19,374 --> 08:01:23,844
我们要么是试图通过寻找
we were either trying to maximize some objective function by trying to find

5117
08:01:24,526 --> 08:01:30,596
全局最大值来最大化某个目标函数，要么是试图通过寻找某些全局最小值来最小化某个代价函数。
a global maximum, or we were trying to minimize some cost function by trying to find some global minimum.

5118
08:01:30,990 --> 08:01:37,988
而在评估这些假设的情况下，我们可以说这个我们要最小化的代价函数，
And in the case of evaluating these hypotheses, one thing we might say is that this cost function, the thing we're trying to minimize,

5119
08:01:38,160 --> 08:01:41,700
我们可能是在尝试最小化我们所说的损失函数。
we might be trying to minimize what we would call a loss function.

5120
08:01:42,062 --> 08:01:48,960
而什么是损失函数呢？它是一个用来衡量我们的函数表现有多差的函数。
And what a loss function is, is it is a function that is going to estimate for us how poorly our function performs.

5121
08:01:49,120 --> 08:01:58,628
更正式地说，每当我们预测错误时，就像是效用的损失，这种效用的损失会增加到我们损失函数的输出中。
More formally, it's like a loss of utility by whenever we predict something that is wrong, that is a loss of utility that's going to add to the output of our loss function.

5122
08:01:59,438 --> 08:02:06,880
你可以设计任何你想要的损失函数，只要它是一种数学上的估算方法，在给定这些数据点、已知实际输出，
And you could come up with any loss function that you want, just some mathematical way of estimating, given each of these data points, given what the actual output is,

5123
08:02:06,960 --> 08:02:12,388
以及我们预测的输出（即我们的估计）的情况下，就可以计算出某种数值上的损失。
and given what our projected output is, our estimate, you could calculate some sort of numerical loss for it.

5124
08:02:12,782 --> 08:02:17,316
不过有几个常用的损失函数值得讨论一下，这样你就见识过了。
But there are a couple of popular loss functions that are worth discussing, just so that you've seen them before.

5125
08:02:18,062 --> 08:02:26,116
当涉及到离散类别时，比如下雨或不下雨、真品或假货，一种方法就是 0-1 损失函数。
When it comes to discrete categories, things like rain or not rain, counterfeit or not counterfeit, one approach is the zero, one loss function.

5126
08:02:26,478 --> 08:02:28,740
它的工作原理是，对于每一个数据点，
And the way that works is for each of the data points,

5127
08:02:29,454 --> 08:02:37,440
我们的损失函数将实际输出作为输入（比如实际上是下雨还是不下雨），并考虑到我们的预测。
our loss function takes as input what the actual output is, like whether it was actually raining or not raining, and takes our prediction into account.

5128
08:02:37,614 --> 08:02:41,508
给定这个数据点，我们预测的是下雨还是不下雨？
Did we predict, given this data point, that it was raining or not raining?

5129
08:02:41,902 --> 08:02:47,396
如果实际值等于预测值，那么 0-1 损失函数就会判定损失为零。
And if the actual value equals the prediction, well then the 0 1 loss function will just say the loss is zero.

5130
08:02:47,520 --> 08:02:50,820
因为我们能够正确预测，所以没有效用的损失。
There was no loss of utility because we were able to predict correctly.

5131
08:02:51,758 --> 08:02:57,840
否则，如果实际值与我们的预测不一致，那么在这种情况下，我们的损失就是 1。
And otherwise, if the actual value was not the same thing as what we predicted, well then in that case our loss is one.

5132
08:02:58,160 --> 08:03:05,028
我们损失了一些东西，损失了一些效用，因为我们预测的函数输出并不是它的真实情况。
We lost something, lost some utility, because what we predicted was the output of the function was not what it actually was.

5133
08:03:05,646 --> 08:03:16,292
在这种情况下，我们的目标就是提出一个能够最小化总经验损失的假设，也就是如果我们把所有这些数据点的损失加起来，总共损失了多少。
And the goal then in a situation like this would be to come up with some hypothesis that minimizes the total empirical loss, the total amount that we've lost, if you add up for all these data points,

5134
08:03:16,480 --> 08:03:20,100
即实际输出是什么，以及你的假设会预测出什么。
what the actual output is and what your hypothesis would have predicted.

5135
08:03:20,974 --> 08:03:29,600
所以在这种情况下，比如我们回到将日期分类为下雨或不下雨的情况，如果我们确定了这个决策边界，我们该如何评估这个决策边界呢？
So in this case, for example, if we go back to classifying days as raining or not raining, and we came up with this decision boundary, how would we evaluate this decision boundary?

5136
08:03:29,680 --> 08:03:33,120
它比在这一边或者在那边画线要好多少？
How much better is it than drawing the line here or drawing the line there?

5137
08:03:33,390 --> 08:03:41,840
嗯，我们可以拿每一个输入数据点，每个数据点都有一个标签，即是下雨还是不下雨，然后我们可以将其与预测结果进行比较，
Well, we could take each of the input data points, and each input data point has a label, whether it was raining or whether it was not raining, and we could compare it to the prediction,

5138
08:03:42,000 --> 08:03:46,884
也就是我们预测是下雨还是不下雨，并给出一个数值作为结果。
whether we predicted it would be raining or not raining, and assign it a numerical value as a result.

5139
08:03:47,790 --> 08:03:54,880
例如，这些点全都是雨天，而且我们预测它们是雨天，因为它们落在线的下方。
So for example, these points over here, they were all rainy days, and we predicted they would be rainy, because they fall on the bottom side of the line.

5140
08:03:55,150 --> 08:03:56,228
所以它们的损失为零。
So they have a loss of zero.

5141
08:03:56,480 --> 08:03:58,160
在这些情况下没有任何损失。
Nothing lost from those situations.

5142
08:03:58,382 --> 08:04:04,548
同样，对于这边的某些点也是一样的，它们不是雨天，而我们也预测它们不是雨天。
And likewise, same is true for some of these points over here, where it was not raining and we predicted it would not be raining either.

5143
08:04:05,134 --> 08:04:15,204
产生损失的是像这里这个点和那里那个点这样的情况，我们预测它们不下雨，但实际上它们是蓝色点，也就是下雨了。
Where we do have loss are points like this point here and that point there, where we predicted that it would not be raining, but in actuality it's a blue point, it was raining.

5144
08:04:15,694 --> 08:04:21,636
或者同样在这里，我们预测会下雨，但实际上它是红色点，也就是说没下雨。
Or likewise here, we predicted that it would be raining, but in actuality it's a red point, it was not raining.

5145
08:04:21,902 --> 08:04:26,276
因此，我们错误地分类了这些我们试图进行训练的数据点。
And so as a result, we miscategorized these data points that we were trying to train on.

5146
08:04:27,054 --> 08:04:29,120
结果就是，这里产生了一些损失。
And as a result, there's some loss here.

5147
08:04:29,280 --> 08:04:34,436
这里、那里、这里、那里的每个都是 1，例如在这种情况下，总损失为 4。
One loss here, there, here, and there, for a total loss of four, for example, in this case.

5148
08:04:34,798 --> 08:04:42,916
这可能就是我们评估或说明这条线比其他位置的线、或者更靠下的线更好的方法，
And that might be how we would estimate or how we would say that this line is better than a line that goes somewhere else, or a line that's further down,

5149
08:04:43,120 --> 08:04:45,520
因为这条线可能会最小化损失。
because this line might minimize the loss.

5150
08:04:45,614 --> 08:04:52,644
如果你只是在我们的空间中画一条直线，那么除了这四个损失点之外就没有更好的办法了。
That there's no way to do better than just these four points of loss if you're just drawing a straight line through our

5151
08:04:52,800 --> 08:04:55,588
所以 0-1 损失函数会检查：
space. So the 0-1 loss function checks.

5152
08:04:56,238 --> 08:04:57,680
我们预测对了吗？还是错了？
Did we get it right? Did we get it wrong?

5153
08:04:57,902 --> 08:05:00,196
如果我们预测对了，损失就是零，没有任何损失。
If we got it right, the loss is zero, nothing lost.

5154
08:05:00,560 --> 08:05:04,080
如果我们预测错了，那么该数据点的损失函数就会显示为 1。
If we got it wrong, then our loss function for that data point says one.

5155
08:05:04,400 --> 08:05:14,948
我们将所有这些数据点的损失相加，得到某种经验损失，即在算法可以获取的所有原始数据点中总共损失了多少。
And we add up all of those losses across all of our data points to get some sort of empirical loss, how much we have lost across all of these original data points that our algorithm had access to.

5156
08:05:16,334 --> 08:05:26,404
还有其他形式的损失，在处理更多实值情况时效果非常好，比如广告预算与销售额之间的映射关系。
There are other forms of loss as well that work especially well when we deal with more real-valued cases, cases like the mapping between advertising budget and amount that we do in sales, for example.

5157
08:05:26,640 --> 08:05:33,284
因为在这种情况下，你不仅关心数值是否完全正确，你还关心你的预测离实际值有多近。
Because in that case, you care not just that you get the number exactly right, but you care how close you were to the actual value.

5158
08:05:33,600 --> 08:05:42,080
如果实际销售额是 2800 美元，而你预测的是 2900 美元，那可能就挺不错的。
If the actual value is you did like $2,800 in sales, and you predicted that you would do $2,900 in sales, maybe that's pretty good.

5159
08:05:42,160 --> 08:05:45,988
这比你预测只有 1000 美元要好得多。
That's much better than if you had predicted you'd do $1,000 in sales, for example.

5160
08:05:46,414 --> 08:05:50,560
因此，我们希望我们的损失函数也能考虑到这一点。
And so we would like our loss function to be able to take that into account as well.

5161
08:05:51,440 --> 08:06:00,932
不仅要考虑实际值和预期值是否完全相同，还要考虑到它们之间的差距。
take into account not just whether the actual value and the expected value are exactly the same, but also take into account how far apart they were.

5162
08:06:01,742 --> 08:06:04,960
为此，一种方法就是我们所说的 L1 损失。
And so for that, one approach is what we call L1 loss.

5163
08:06:05,294 --> 08:06:09,060
L1 损失不只是看实际值和预测值是否相等，
L1 loss doesn't just look at whether actual and predicted are equal to each other,

5164
08:06:09,966 --> 08:06:14,692
而是取「实际值减去预测值」的绝对值。
but we take the absolute value of the actual value minus the predicted value.

5165
08:06:14,960 --> 08:06:25,764
换句话说，我们只是在计算实际值和预测值之间相差多少，并将所有数据点的这些差异相加，从而得出最终结果。
In other words, we just ask how far apart were the actual and predicted values, and we sum that up across all of the data points to be able to get what our answer ultimately is.

5166
08:06:26,830 --> 08:06:29,312
那么，这在我们的数据集中具体是什么样子的呢？
So, what might this actually look like for our data set?

5167
08:06:29,582 --> 08:06:40,004
如果我们回到之前的表达方式，即 x-axis 是广告，y-axis 是销售额，那条线就是我们的预测，也就是针对特定广告量的估算值，
Well, if we go back to this representation where we had advertising along the x-axis, sales along the y-axis, our line was our prediction, our estimate for any given amount of advertising,

5168
08:06:40,206 --> 08:06:47,812
也就是我们预测的销售量，而 L1 损失就是它在销售轴上垂直方向上的距离。
what we predicted sales was going to be, and our L1 loss is just how far apart vertically along the sales axis.

5169
08:06:48,206 --> 08:06:50,628
我们的预测是基于每一个数据点的。
our prediction was from each of the data points.

5170
08:06:50,990 --> 08:06:58,884
所以我们可以计算出预测值与每个数据点之间确切的差距，并据此算出总体的损失量
So we could figure out exactly how far apart our prediction was from each of the data points, and figure out as a result of that what our loss is overall

5171
08:06:59,152 --> 08:07:05,668
对于这个特定的假设，只需将这些不同数据点的各项个体损失全部相加即可。
for this particular hypothesis, just by adding up all of these various different individual losses for each of these data points.

5172
08:07:05,998 --> 08:07:09,540
我们的目标随后就是试图最小化这个损失，也就是尝试找到一条线，
And our goal then is to try and minimize that loss, to try and come up

5173
08:07:10,286 --> 08:07:18,244
通过判断估算的销售量与实际销售量之间的差距，来最小化效用损失。
with some line that minimizes what the utility loss is by judging how far away our estimate amount of sales is from the actual amount of sales.

5174
08:07:18,894 --> 08:07:23,268
事实证明还有其他的损失函数。其中一种非常流行的是 L2 损失。
And turns out there are other loss functions as well. One that's quite popular is the L2 loss.

5175
08:07:23,662 --> 08:07:33,232
L2 损失不再仅仅使用绝对值来衡量实际值与预测值的差距，而是使用「实际值减去预测值」的平方。
The L2 loss, instead of just using the absolute value, like how far away the actual value is from the predicted value, it uses the square of actual minus predicted.

5176
08:07:33,312 --> 08:07:42,912
也就是说，它计算实际值和预测值之间的差距并对其求平方，从而更严厉地惩罚那些预测较差的情况。
So how far apart are the actual and predicted value, and it squares that value, effectively penalizing much more harshly, anything that is a worse prediction.

5177
08:07:43,150 --> 08:07:53,072
想象一下，如果你有两个数据点，它们的预测值与实际值的偏差都是 1，而另一个数据点的预测值与其实际值的偏差是 2，
So you imagine if you have two data points that you predict as being, one value away from their actual value, as opposed to one data point that you predict as being two

5178
08:07:53,232 --> 08:07:54,948
偏离其实际值的距离。
away from its actual value.

5179
08:07:55,374 --> 08:08:05,156
那个偏差为 2 的点会被更严厉地惩罚，因为它会把实际值和预测值之间的差值进行平方。
The L2 loss function will more harshly penalize that one that is two away, because it's going to square however much the difference is between the actual value and the predicted value.

5180
08:08:05,422 --> 08:08:10,308
根据具体情况，你可能会根据你想最小化的目标来选择不同的损失函数。
And depending on the situation, you might want to choose a loss function depending on what you care about minimizing.

5181
08:08:10,512 --> 08:08:15,712
如果你非常在意减少离群情况下的误差，那么你可能想考虑这种方法。
If you really care about minimizing the error on more outlier cases, then you might want to consider something like this.

5182
08:08:15,854 --> 08:08:21,472
但如果你有很多离群值且并不特别在乎对它们的建模，那么 L1 损失函数可能更合适。
But if you've got a lot of outliers and you don't necessarily care about modeling them, then maybe an L1 loss function is preferable.

5183
08:08:21,646 --> 08:08:25,636
但这其中存在权衡，你需要根据特定的数据集做出决定。
But there are trade-offs here that you need to decide based on a particular set of data.

5184
08:08:26,478 --> 08:08:33,152
但是无论使用哪种损失函数，或者我们尝试做任何事情时，都会面临一个被称为「过拟合」的问题。
But what you do run the risk of with any of these loss functions, with anything that we're trying to do, is a problem known as overfitting.

5185
08:08:33,422 --> 08:08:42,192
过拟合是机器学习中一个很大的问题，每当模型与数据集契合得过于紧密时就会发生，结果就是
And overfitting is a big problem that you can encounter in machine learning, which happens any time a model fits too closely with a data set, and as a result

5186
08:08:42,352 --> 08:08:43,684
无法泛化。
fails to generalize.

5187
08:08:44,398 --> 08:08:47,364
我们希望我们的模型能够准确地预测
We would like our model to be able to accurately predict

5188
08:08:48,110 --> 08:08:51,908
我们所能获取的数据中的数据、输入和输出对。
data and inputs and output pairs for the data that we have access to.

5189
