但我们可能还有一些红色方块，那是会受到某种惩罚的地方，是某些我们不希望智能体前往的坏地方
But then we might also have some, red squares that are places where you get some sort of punishment, some bad place where we don't want the agent to go.

5467
08:36:12,366 --> 08:36:17,924
如果它最终进入红方格，我们的智能体就会因此受到某种惩罚
And if it ends up in the red square, then our agent is going to get some sort of punishment as a result of that.

5468
08:36:18,222 --> 08:36:21,456
但智能体最初并不知道所有这些细节
But the agent originally doesn't know all of these details.

5469
08:36:21,536 --> 08:36:27,876
它不知道这些状态与惩罚相关，但也许它知道这个状态与奖励相关，或者它可能不知道
It doesn't know that these states are associated with punishments, but maybe it does know that this state is associated with a reward, maybe it doesn't,

5470
08:36:28,110 --> 08:36:33,028
但它只需要与环境互动，来弄清楚该做什么以及不该做什么
but it just needs to sort of interact with the environment to try and figure out what to do and what not to

5471
08:36:33,870 --> 08:36:42,532
所以智能体做的第一件事是，在没有额外信息、不知道惩罚是什么、也不知道奖励在哪里的情况下，它可能只是尝试采取一个动作
do. So the first thing the agent might do is given no additional information, if it doesn't know what the punishments are, it doesn't know where the rewards are, it just might try and take an action.

5472
08:36:43,022 --> 08:36:46,980
它采取了一个动作，结果发现自己受到了一定程度的惩罚
And it takes an action and ends up realizing that it got some sort of punishment.

5473
08:36:47,502 --> 08:36:49,412
那么它从这次经历中学到了什么呢？
And so what does it learn from that experience?

5474
08:36:49,742 --> 08:36:55,696
嗯，它可能会学到在未来处于这个状态时，不要采取向右移动的动作
Well, it might learn that when you're in this state in the future, don't take the action, move to the right.

5475
08:36:55,776 --> 08:36:57,056
也就是说那个是一个糟糕的动作
That that is a bad action to take.

5476
08:36:57,166 --> 08:37:04,996
也就是说在未来，如果你再次回到这个状态，就在这个特定状态下不要采取向右走的动作，因为它会导致惩罚
That in the future, if you ever find yourself back in the state, don't take this action of going to the right when you're in this particular state, because that leads to punishment.

5477
08:37:05,390 --> 08:37:06,564
这至少是它的直觉所在
That might be the intuition at least.

5478
08:37:06,656 --> 08:37:13,956
然后你可以尝试其他的动作。你向上移动，好，那并没有带来任何即时奖励，也许试点别的，然后再试点别的
And so you could try doing other actions. You move up, all right, that didn't lead to any immediate rewards, maybe try something else, then maybe try something else.

5479
08:37:14,606 --> 08:37:18,656
好的，现在你发现又受到了惩罚，于是你从这次经历中学到了一些东西
And all right, now you found that you got another punishment, and so you learn something from that experience.

5480
08:37:18,736 --> 08:37:28,644
所以下次当你进行这整个过程时，你知道如果你最终进入这个方格，就不应该采取向下动作，因为处于这个状态并执行那个动作最终会导致
So the next time you do this whole process, you know that if you ever end up in this square, you shouldn't take the down action, because being in this state and taking that action ultimately leads to

5481
08:37:29,294 --> 08:37:32,420
某种惩罚，换句话说，就是负奖励
some sort of punishment, a negative reward, in other words.

5482
08:37:32,974 --> 08:37:41,856
这个过程不断重复。你可以想象让我们的智能体去探索世界，随着时间的推移不断学习，哪些状态往往对应糟糕的动作，随时间推移而学习
And this process repeats. You might imagine just letting our agent explore the world, learning over time. what states tend to correspond with poor actions, learning over time.

5483
08:37:41,856 --> 08:37:50,180
哪些状态对应糟糕的动作，直到最终，如果它尝试足够多的随机事物，它可能会发现最后当你到达这个状态时
what states correspond with poor actions, until eventually, if it tries enough things randomly, it might find that eventually, when you get to this state,

5484
08:37:50,510 --> 08:37:55,364
如果你在这个状态下采取向上动作，它可能会发现你实际上从中获得了一项奖励
if you take the up action in this state, it might find that you actually get a reward from that.

5485
08:37:56,046 --> 08:38:02,148
它能从中学到的是，如果你处于这个状态，你应该采取向上动作，因为它会带来奖励
And what it can learn from that is that if you're in this state, you should take the up action, because that leads to a reward.

5486
08:38:02,510 --> 08:38:10,176
随着时间的推移，你还可以学到，如果你处在这个状态，你应该采取向左的动作，因为那会带你进入这个状态，也能让你最终获得奖励
And over time, you can also learn that if you're in this state, you should take the left action because that leads to this state that also lets you eventually get to the reward.

5487
08:38:10,256 --> 08:38:18,016
所以你开始随着时间推移不仅学会哪些动作在特定状态下是好的，还学到哪些动作是坏的
So you begin to learn over time not only which actions are good in particular states, but also which actions are bad.

5488
08:38:18,350 --> 08:38:27,492
这样一旦你知道了一系列通往某种奖励的良好动作序列，我们的智能体就可以遵循这些指令，遵循它所学到的经验
Such that once you know some sequence of good actions that leads you to some sort of reward, our agent can just follow those instructions, follow the experience that it has learned.

5489
08:38:27,696 --> 08:38:35,536
我们没有告诉智能体目标是什么，也没告诉它惩罚在哪里，但智能体可以从这些经验中开始学习
We didn't tell the agent what the goal was, we didn't tell the agent where the punishments were, but the agent can begin to learn from this experience

5490
08:38:35,630 --> 08:38:39,556
并学会在未来更好地执行这类任务
and learn to begin to perform these sorts of tasks better in the future.

5491
08:38:40,654 --> 08:38:42,496
那么现在让我们试着把这个想法公式化。
And so let's now try to formalize this idea.

5492
08:38:42,656 --> 08:38:49,296
将「在这个状态下采取这个动作是好事还是坏事」这个想法公式化。
Formalize the idea that we would like to be able to learn in this state, taking this action, is that a good thing or a bad thing?

5493
08:38:49,614 --> 08:38:53,284
强化学习有很多不同的模型。我们今天只看其中一种。
There are lots of different models for reinforcement learning. We're just going to look at one of them today.

5494
08:38:53,582 --> 08:38:56,836
我们要看的这种方法被称为 Q learning。
And the one that we're going to look at is a method known as Q learning.

5495
08:38:57,230 --> 08:39:07,332
Q learning 的核心是学习一个函数，即函数 q，它接收输入 S 和 A，其中 S 是状态，A 是你在该状态下采取的动作。
And what Q learning is all about is it's about learning a function, a function q, that takes inputs S and A, where S is a state and A is an action that you take in that state.

5496
08:39:07,726 --> 08:39:15,876
这个 Q 函数的作用是估算：在当前状态下，采取这个动作能获得多少奖励
And what this Q function is going to do is it is going to estimate the value how much reward will I get from taking this action

5497
08:39:16,416 --> 08:39:17,572
？
in this state?

5498
08:39:18,830 --> 08:39:28,560
最初我们不知道这个 q 函数应该是多少，但随着时间的推移，基于经验，通过尝试各种事物并观察结果，我想试着学习出 q
Originally, we don't know what this q function should be, but over time, based on experience, based on trying things out and seeing what the result is, I would like to try and learn what q

5499
08:39:28,720 --> 08:39:34,320
对于任何特定的状态以及我在该状态下可能采取的任何特定动作。
of sa is for any particular state and any particular action that I might take in that state.

5500
08:39:34,670 --> 08:39:35,520
那么具体的方法是什么？
So what is the approach?

5501
08:39:35,758 --> 08:39:42,692
好的，最初的方法是让所有状态 S 和所有动作 A 的 qSA 都等于零。
Well, the approach originally is we'll start with qSA equal to zero for all states S and for all actions A.

5502
08:39:42,880 --> 08:39:50,532
也就是说，在还没开始任何操作、还没有任何经验之前，我不知道在任何给定状态下采取任何动作的价值。
That initially, before I've ever started anything, before I've had any experiences, I don't know the value of taking any action in any given state.

5503
08:39:50,798 --> 08:39:54,372
所以我假设全线上的这些值都是零。
So I'm going to assume that the value is just zero all across the board.

5504
08:39:55,214 --> 08:40:02,788
但随着我与世界互动，随着我获得奖励或惩罚，或者进入一个既没奖励也没惩罚的单元格时，
But then as I interact with the world, as I experience rewards or punishments, or maybe I go to a cell where I don't get either a reward or a punishment,

5505
08:40:03,310 --> 08:40:04,708
我想在某种程度上更新
I want to somehow update

5506
08:40:05,454 --> 08:40:14,884
我对 QSA 的估算。我希望根据获得的经验、奖励和惩罚不断更新对 QSA 的估算，这样在未来，
my estimate of QSA. I want to continually update my estimate of QSA based on the experiences and rewards and punishments that I've received, such that in the future,

5507
08:40:15,200 --> 08:40:18,596
我对哪些状态下哪些动作是好的，会有更好的认知。
my knowledge of what actions are good in what states will be better.

5508
08:40:19,150 --> 08:40:25,040
所以当我们采取一个动作并获得某种奖励时，我想估算出 QSA 的新值。
So when we take an action and receive some sort of reward, I want to estimate the new value of QSA.

5509
08:40:25,614 --> 08:40:27,748
我的估算基于几个不同的因素。
And I estimate that based on a couple of different things.

5510
08:40:28,270 --> 08:40:33,188
我根据执行该动作并进入下一个状态所获得的奖励来估算它。
I estimate it based on the reward that I'm getting from taking this action and getting into the next state.

5511
08:40:33,774 --> 08:40:44,228
但假设情况还没结束，假设还有我可能采取的后续动作，我还需要考虑到期望未来奖励。
But assuming the situation isn't over, assuming there are still future actions that I might take as well, I also need to take into account the expected future rewards.

5512
08:40:44,590 --> 08:40:52,708
如果你想象一个智能体与环境互动，有时你会执行一个动作并获得奖励，但随后你还可以继续进行更多动作并获得更多奖励，
That if you imagine an agent interacting with the environment, and sometimes you'll take an action and get a reward, but then you can keep taking more actions and get more rewards,

5513
08:40:52,880 --> 08:40:54,080
这两者都是相关的。
that these both are relevant.

5514
08:40:54,240 --> 08:40:58,212
包括我从当前步骤获得的即时奖励，以及我的未来奖励。
Both the current reward I'm getting from this current step and also my future reward.

5515
08:40:58,446 --> 08:41:07,280
有时我可能愿意采取一个不会立即带来奖励的步骤，因为我知道在后续过程中它会带来更多奖励。
And it might be the case that I'll want to take a step that doesn't immediately lead to a reward, because later on down the line I know it will lead to more rewards as well.

5516
08:41:07,502 --> 08:41:15,140
所以，智能体获得的当前奖励与它将获得的未来奖励之间存在一种平衡。
So there's a balancing act between current rewards that the agent experiences and future rewards that the agent experiences as well.

5517
08:41:16,654 --> 08:41:19,040
然后我们需要更新 QSA。
And then we need to update QSA.

5518
08:41:19,534 --> 08:41:24,068
因此，我们根据当前奖励和期望未来奖励来估算 QSA 的值。
So we estimate the value of QSA based on the current reward and the expected future rewards.

5519
08:41:24,270 --> 08:41:29,124
接着，我们需要更新这个 Q 函数，以纳入这一新估算。
And then we need to update this Q function to take into account this new estimate.

5520
08:41:29,422 --> 08:41:34,596
现在，在执行这个过程的过程中，我们已经对它可能的值有了初步估算。
Now we already, as we go through this process, we'll already have an estimate for what we think the value is.

5521
08:41:35,054 --> 08:41:42,116
现在我们有了新的估值，然后我们需要以某种方式将这两个估值结合起来，接下来我们将看看一些更正式的方法来实现这一点。
Now we have a new estimate, and then somehow we need to combine these two estimates together, and we'll look at more formal ways that we can actually begin to do that.

5522
08:41:42,926 --> 08:41:47,364
为了展示这个公式的具体样子，这是我们在 Q 学习中采用的方法。
So to actually show you what this formula looks like, here is the approach we'll take with Q-learning.

5523
08:41:47,726 --> 08:41:51,716
我们再次从所有状态下 Q(S, A) 等于零开始。
We're going to again start with Q of S and A being equal to zero for all states.

5524
08:41:52,398 --> 08:41:56,068
然后每当我们处于状态 S 时采取动作 A，
And then every time we take an action A in state S

5525
08:41:56,960 --> 08:42:03,460
并观察到奖励 R 时，我们将更新我们对 Q(S, A) 的估值。
and observe a reward R, we're going to update our value, our estimate, for Q of SA.

5526
08:42:04,110 --> 08:42:11,524
其中的思路是：我们要计算新估值减去现有估值的差值。
And the idea is that we're going to figure out what the new value estimate is minus what our existing value estimate is.

5527
08:42:12,160 --> 08:42:17,188
也就是说，我们对在当前状态下采取该动作的价值有一些预设的认知。
So we have some preconceived notion for what the value is for taking this action in this state.

5528
08:42:17,440 --> 08:42:20,320
也许我们的预期是，目前认为它的价值是
Maybe our expectation is we currently think the value is

5529
08:42:20,320 --> 08:42:24,240
10。但随后我们将估算我们现在认为它应该是多少。
10. But then we're going to estimate what we now think it's going to be.

5530
08:42:24,430 --> 08:42:26,628
也许新的估值是 20 之类的。
Maybe the new value estimate is something like 20.

5531
08:42:27,214 --> 08:42:34,404
那么这就产生了一个差值，即新估值比当前估值高出 10 个点。
So there's a delta of like 10 that our new value estimate is 10 points higher than what our current value estimate happens to be.

5532
08:42:35,150 --> 08:42:36,580
因此我们有几种选择。
And so we have a couple of options here.

5533
08:42:37,134 --> 08:42:45,188
我们需要决定在多大程度上调整我们对在特定状态下采取该动作的当前预期。
We need to decide how much we want to adjust our current expectation of what the value is of taking this action in this particular state.

5534
08:42:45,680 --> 08:42:54,240
而这个差异，即我们在现有认知基础上增加或减少多少，取决于这个参数
And what that difference is, how much we add or subtract from our existing notion of how much that we expect the value to be, is dependent on this parameter

5535
08:42:54,400 --> 08:42:56,388
alpha，也称为学习率。
alpha, also called a learning rate.

5536
08:42:56,654 --> 08:43:04,100
Alpha 实际上代表了我们对新信息的重视程度与对旧信息的重视程度之间的比例。
And alpha represents, in effect, how much we value new information compared to how much we value old information.

5537
08:43:04,654 --> 08:43:08,160
如果 alpha 的值是 1，意味着我们非常看重新信息。
An alpha value of one means we really value new information.

5538
08:43:08,334 --> 08:43:11,972
但如果我们有了新估值，那么旧的估值就不重要了。
But if we have a new estimate, then it doesn't matter what our old estimate is.

5539
08:43:12,160 --> 08:43:17,796
我们只考虑新估值，因为我们总是希望考虑到新的信息。
We're only going to consider our new estimate because we always just want to take into consideration, our new information.

5540
08:43:18,254 --> 08:43:27,040
这种运作方式是：如果你设想 alpha 为 1，那么我们取 Q(S, A) 的旧值，然后加上 1
So the way that works is that if you imagine alpha being one, well then we're taking the old value of QSA and then adding one

5541
08:43:27,200 --> 08:43:31,600
乘以（新估值减去旧估值），这最终就只剩下新估值。
times the new value minus the old value, and that just leaves us with the new value.

5542
08:43:31,822 --> 08:43:36,900
所以当 alpha 为 1 时，我们只考虑新估值是多少。
So when alpha is one, all we take into consideration is what our new estimate happens to be.

5543
08:43:37,582 --> 08:43:42,320
但随着时间的推移，当我们积累了大量的经验时，我们已经拥有了一些现有信息。
But over time, as we go through a lot of experiences, we already have some existing information.

5544
08:43:42,480 --> 08:43:47,620
我们可能已经尝试过这个动作九次，而现在我们刚刚进行了第十次尝试。
We might have tried taking this action nine times already, and now we just tried it a tenth time.

5545
08:43:47,982 --> 08:43:57,892
我们不想只考虑这第十次的经验，我也不想忽略前九次经验的意义，那些也是我不希望丢失的数据。
And we don't only want to consider this tenth experience, I also want to consider the fact that my prior nine experiences, those were meaningful too, and that's data I don't necessarily want to lose.

5546
08:43:58,190 --> 08:44:03,200
因此这个 alpha 控制着这一决策，决定了新信息的权重。
And so this alpha controls that decision, controls how important is the new information.

5547
08:44:03,440 --> 08:44:08,836
零意味着忽略所有新信息，保持 Q 值不变。
Zero would mean ignore all the new information, just keep this Q value the same.

5548
08:44:09,294 --> 08:44:16,836
一意味着用新信息完全替换旧信息，而在两者之间，则是在这两个值之间寻找某种平衡。
One means replace the old information entirely with the new information, and somewhere in between, keep some sort of balance between these two values.

5549
08:44:17,838 --> 08:44:20,548
我们也可以把这个等式写得更正式一些。
We can put this equation a little bit more formally as well.

5550
08:44:20,928 --> 08:44:27,332
旧估值是我们对在特定状态下采取该动作的价值的旧有估计。
The old value estimate is our old estimate for what the value is of taking this action in a particular state.

5551
08:44:27,598 --> 08:44:37,380
这就是 Q(s, a)。我们先写下它，然后给它加上一些内容。我们要加上 alpha 乘以新值估计减去旧值估计的部分。
That's just q of s and a. So we have it once here, and we're going to add something to it. We're going to add alpha times the new value estimate minus the old value estimate.

5552
08:44:37,678 --> 08:44:41,188
不过旧的价值估计，我们只需要调用这个 Q function 来获取。
But the old value estimate we just look up by calling this Q function.

5553
08:44:42,222 --> 08:44:44,128
那么什么是新的价值估计呢？
And what then is the new value estimate?

5554
08:44:44,288 --> 08:44:50,948
基于我们刚刚获得的这次经验，在当前这个特定状态下采取这个动作的最新估值是多少？
Based on this experience we have just taken, what is our new estimate for the value of taking this action in this particular state?

5555
08:44:51,470 --> 08:44:53,476
嗯，它由两部分组成。
Well, it's going to be composed of two parts.

5556
08:44:53,968 --> 08:44:59,396
第一部分是：我在这个状态下执行这个动作后，刚刚获得了多少奖励？
It's going to be composed of what reward did I just get from taking this action in this state?

5557
08:44:59,918 --> 08:45:05,060
第二部分是：从现在开始，我预期未来的奖励是多少？
And then it's going to be what can I expect my future rewards to be from this point forward?

5558
08:45:05,614 --> 08:45:06,468
所以它就是
So it's going to be

5559
08:45:07,374 --> 08:45:13,892
R，也就是我现在获得的某些奖励，加上我预测在未来能获得的任何奖励。
R, some reward I'm getting right now, plus whatever I estimate I'm going to get in the future.

5560
08:45:14,446 --> 08:45:16,528
那我该如何估算未来的奖励呢？
And how do I estimate what I'm going to get in the future?

5561
08:45:16,750 --> 08:45:19,888
嗯，这又是对这个 Q function 的另一次调用。
Well, it's a bit of another call to this Q function.

5562
08:45:20,046 --> 08:45:28,356
它是指在所有可能采取的下一个动作中取最大值，也就是说，在所有这些可能的动作中，
It's going to be take the maximum across all possible actions I could take next and say, all right, of all of these possible actions I could take,

5563
08:45:28,768 --> 08:45:31,140
哪一个能带来最高的奖励？
which one is going to have the highest reward?

5564
08:45:31,470 --> 08:45:33,408
所以这个公式看起来有点复杂。
So this then looks a little bit complicated.

5565
08:45:33,568 --> 08:45:37,156
这就是我们执行这种更新的思路。
This is going to be our notion for how we're going to perform this kind of update.

5566
08:45:37,408 --> 08:45:46,564
即：我有一些关于在当前状态下采取该动作价值的估计，也就是旧的估值，然后我会根据新信息来更新它。
That I have some estimate, some old estimate for what the value is of taking this action in this state, and I'm going to update it based on new information.

5567
08:45:46,830 --> 08:45:57,444
我获得了一些奖励，预测了未来的奖励，并利用这些信息来更新我对在这个特定状态下采取该动作所能获得的奖励的估值。
That I experience some reward, I predict what my future reward is going to be, and using that I update what what I estimate the reward will be for taking this action in this particular state.

5568
08:45:57,806 --> 08:46:00,448
此外，你还可以对这个算法进行其他一些改进。
And there are other additions you might make to this algorithm as well.

5569
08:46:00,686 --> 08:46:05,568
有时候，你可能并不想让未来的奖励与当前的奖励同等对待。
Sometimes it might not be the case that future rewards you want to wait equally to current rewards.

5570
08:46:05,728 --> 08:46:10,048
也许你希望智能体更看重现在的奖励，而不是以后的奖励。
Maybe you want an agent that values like reward now over reward later.

5571
08:46:10,350 --> 08:46:19,648
所以有时你甚至可以在这里加入另一个项，也就是另一个参数，来对未来的奖励进行折扣，并认为未来的奖励不如立即获得的奖励有价值。
And so sometimes you can even add another term in here, some other parameter, where you discount future rewards and say future rewards are not as valuable as rewards immediately.

5572
08:46:19,790 --> 08:46:24,324
在当前时间步获得奖励比等上一年后再获得奖励要好。
The getting reward in the current time step is better than waiting a year and getting rewards later.

5573
08:46:24,528 --> 08:46:28,484
但那个参数应该设成多少，是由程序员来决定的。
But that's something up to the programmer to decide what that parameter ought to be.

5574
08:46:29,134 --> 08:46:36,740
但这个整个公式的核心思想是：每当我们获得一些新的奖励时，我们都会把这些考虑进去。
But the big picture idea of this entire formula is to say that every time we experience some new reward, we take that into account.

5575
08:46:36,928 --> 08:46:40,228
我们更新对该动作好坏程度的估值。
We update our estimate of how good is this action.

5576
08:46:40,686 --> 08:46:43,908
这样在未来，我们就可以基于这个算法来做决策了。
And then in the future, we can make decisions based on that algorithm.

5577
08:46:44,128 --> 08:46:54,532
一旦我们对每个状态和每个动作采取后的价值都有了良好的估算，我们就可以实现类似贪婪决策策略的操作。
Once we have some good estimate for every state and for every action, what the value is of taking that action, then we can do something like implement a greedy decision-making policy.

5578
08:46:54,862 --> 08:47:05,248
也就是说，如果我处于某个状态并想知道该采取什么动作，那么我会考虑所有可能的动作中，Q(s, a) 的值是多少？
That if I am in a state and I want to know what action should I take in that state, well then I consider for all of my possible actions, what is the value of QSA?

5579
08:47:05,648 --> 08:47:08,804
也就是我在那个状态下采取那个动作的估算价值是多少？
What is my estimated value of taking that action in that state?

5580
08:47:09,038 --> 08:47:14,404
然后在计算完这个表达式后，我只需选择那个具有最高值的动作。
And I will just pick the action that has the highest value after I evaluate that expression.

5581
08:47:15,246 --> 08:47:19,808
所以我选择价值最高的动作，并根据这个来决定我该采取什么行动。
So I pick the action that has the highest value, and based on that, that tells me what action I should take.

5582
08:47:19,888 --> 08:47:27,716
在任何给定的状态下，我都可以贪婪地判断，在所有可能的动作中，这个动作能给我最高的预期价值，
At any given state that I'm in, I can just greedily say, across all my actions, this action gives me the highest expected value,

5583
08:47:27,950 --> 08:47:32,228
因此我会选择这个作为我采取的行动。
and so I'll go ahead and choose that action as the action that I take as well.

5584
08:47:33,262 --> 08:47:35,888
但这种方法也有缺点。
But there is a downside to this kind of approach.

5585
08:47:36,142 --> 08:47:42,628
这种缺点出现在类似这样的情况：我们知道存在某种能让我获得奖励的解决方案，
And the downside comes up in a situation like this, where we know that, there is some solution that gets me to the reward,

5586
08:47:44,046 --> 08:47:49,700
我们的智能体已经找到了它，但这并不一定是最好的或者最快的方法。
and our agent has been able to figure that out, but it might not necessarily be the best way or the fastest way.

5587
08:47:49,968 --> 08:47:59,364
如果允许智能体多探索一点，它可能会发现通过另一条路径——也就是走这条特定的路径——能更快获得奖励，
If the agent is allowed to explore a little bit more, it might find that it can get the reward faster by taking some other route instead, by going through this particular path

5588
08:47:59,630 --> 08:48:02,020
这是到达那里的更快捷路径，
that is a faster way to get to

5589
08:48:02,702 --> 08:48:03,556
也就是那个最终目标。
that ultimate goal.

5590
08:48:04,206 --> 08:48:07,364
也许我们希望智能体也能发现这一点。
And maybe we would like for the agent to be able to figure that out as well.

5591
08:48:07,598 --> 08:48:15,844
但如果智能体总是采取它已知最好的动作，那么当它到达这个特定的方格时，它并不知道这是一个好的行动，
But if the agent always takes the actions that it knows to be best, well when it gets to this particular square, it doesn't know that this is a good action

5592
08:48:16,110 --> 08:48:17,508
因为它从未真正尝试过。
because it's never really tried it.

5593
08:48:17,710 --> 08:48:21,568
但它知道向下走最终能通往奖励。
But it knows that going down eventually leads its way to this reward.

5594
08:48:21,870 --> 08:48:28,804
所以它以后可能会学到只走这条路，而永远不会去探索并尝试那条路径。
So it might learn in the future that it should just always take this route and it's never going to explore and go along that route instead.

5595
08:48:29,582 --> 08:48:35,044
所以在强化学习中，存在“探索”与“利用”之间的权衡。
So in reinforcement learning, there is this tension between exploration and exploitation.

5596
08:48:35,342 --> 08:48:40,048
“利用”通常指利用 AI 已经掌握的知识。
And exploitation generally refers to using knowledge that the AI already has.

5597
08:48:40,270 --> 08:48:44,964
AI 已经知道这个动作能带来奖励，所以我们就采用这个动作。
The AI already knows that this is a move that leads to reward, so we'll go ahead and use that move.

5598
08:48:45,390 --> 08:48:54,628
而“探索”则是关于去尝试那些我们之前可能没怎么深入探索过的其他动作，因为其中某些动作，即使我目前对它一无所知，
And exploration is all about exploring other actions that we may not have explored as thoroughly before, because maybe one of these actions, even if I don't know anything about it,

5599
08:48:55,008 --> 08:48:59,236
也可能更快带来更好的奖励，或者在未来带来更多奖励。
might lead to better rewards faster or to more rewards in the future.

5600
08:49:00,046 --> 08:49:07,428
因此，一个只利用信息而不去探索的智能体或许能获得奖励，但它可能无法最大化其奖励，
And so an agent that only ever exploits information and never explores might be able to get reward, but it might not maximize its rewards,

5601
08:49:07,712 --> 08:49:10,592
因为它不知道还有哪些其他的可能性。
because it doesn't know what other possibilities are out there.

5602
08:49:10,798 --> 08:49:14,948
这些可能性只有通过利用“探索”才能获知。
Possibilities that would only know about by taking advantage of exploration.

5603
08:49:15,758 --> 08:49:17,220
那么我们该如何解决这个问题呢？
And so how can we try and address this?

5604
08:49:17,582 --> 08:49:25,700
其中一种可能的解决方案被称为 epsilon 贪婪算法，其中我们将 epsilon 设置为我们想要进行随机动作的频率。
Well, one possible solution is known as the epsilon greedy algorithm, where we set epsilon equal to how often we want to just make a random move.

5605
08:49:25,934 --> 08:49:31,748
也就是说，我们会偶尔执行一个随机动作，以此来尝试探索并看看会发生什么。
Where occasionally we will just make a random move in order to say, let's try to explore and see what happens.

5606
08:49:33,102 --> 08:49:39,972
那么该算法的逻辑就是：以 1 减去 epsilon 的概率，选择估计出的最佳动作。
And then the logic of the algorithm will be with probability 1 minus epsilon, choose the estimated best move.

5607
08:49:40,718 --> 08:49:43,140
在贪婪情况下，我们总是选择最好的动作。
In a greedy case, we'd always choose the best move.

5608
08:49:43,566 --> 08:49:50,148
但在 epsilon 贪婪中，我们大部分时间会选择最好的动作，或者有时会选择最好的动作，
But in epsilon greedy, we're most of the time going to choose the best move, or sometimes going to choose the best move,

5609
08:49:50,446 --> 08:49:55,140
但有时以 epsilon 的概率，我们会选择一个随机动作。
but sometimes with probability epsilon, we're going to choose a random move instead.

5610
08:49:55,982 --> 08:50:03,332
所以每当我们面临采取行动的选择时，有时我们会选择最好的动作，有时我们只是选择一个随机动作。
So every time we're faced with the ability to take an action, sometimes we're going to choose the best move, sometimes we're just going to choose a random move.

5611
08:50:03,886 --> 08:50:13,312
因此，这种类型的算法在强化学习语境下非常强大，因为它不总是只选择当前最好的可能动作，而是有时，特别是在早期阶段，
So this type of algorithm then can be quite powerful in a reinforcement learning context by not always just choosing the best possible move right now, but sometimes, especially early on,

5612
08:50:13,552 --> 08:50:19,268
允许你采取随机动作，从而让你能够更多地探索各种不同的可能状态和动作。
allowing yourself to make random moves that allow you to explore various different possible states and actions more.

5613
08:50:19,438 --> 08:50:29,668
而且随着时间的推移，你可能会不断降低 epsilon 的值，在你更有信心已经探索过所有可能性后，选择最好的动作。
And maybe over time you might decrease your value of epsilon more and more often, choosing the best move after you're more confident that you've explored what all of the possibilities actually are.

5614
08:50:30,542 --> 08:50:35,684
所以我们可以把这个应用到实践中，强化学习的一个非常常见的应用是在游戏领域。
So we can put this into practice, and one very common application of reinforcement learning is in game playing.

5615
08:50:35,886 --> 08:50:43,780
如果你想教一个智能体如何玩游戏，你只需让它玩很多次，然后在游戏结束时给出一个奖励信号。
That if you want to teach an agent how to play a game, you just let the agent play the game a whole bunch, and then the reward signal happens at the end of the game.

5616
08:50:44,142 --> 08:50:49,380
当游戏结束时，如果我们的 AI 赢了，它会获得 1 的奖励，例如。
When the game is over, if our AI won the game, it gets a reward of one, for example.

5617
08:50:49,614 --> 08:50:52,592
如果它输了，它会得到 -1 的奖励。
And if it lost the game, it gets a reward of negative one.

5618
08:50:52,974 --> 08:51:01,712
从那开始，它就开始学习哪些动作是好的，哪些动作是坏的。你不需要告诉 AI 什么好什么坏，AI 会根据这个奖励自行判断出来。
And from that it begins to learn what actions are good and what actions are bad. You don't have to tell the AI what's good and what's bad, but the AI figures it out based on that reward.

5619
08:51:01,872 --> 08:51:09,028
赢球是一个信号，输球是另一个信号，基于所有这些信息，它开始推断出自己实际上应该做出什么样的决策。
Winning the game is some signal, losing the game is some signal, and based on all of that, it begins to figure out what decisions it should actually make.

5620
08:51:09,870 --> 08:51:13,412
那么有一个非常简单的游戏，你可能玩过，叫做 NIM。
So one very simple game, which you may have played before, is a game called NIM.

5621
08:51:13,774 --> 08:51:17,792
在 NIM 游戏中，你有许多不同堆里的物体。
And in the game of NIM, you've got a whole bunch of objects in a whole bunch of different piles.

5622
08:51:18,030 --> 08:51:20,672
这里我把每一个堆表示成一个单独的行。
Where here I've represented each pile as an individual row.

5623
08:51:21,038 --> 08:51:25,952
所以第一个堆里有一个物体，第二个有三个，第三个有五个，第四个有七个。
So you've got one object in the first pile, three in the second pile, five in the third pile, seven in the fourth pile.

5624
08:51:26,254 --> 08:51:31,632
NIM 是一个双人游戏，玩家轮流从这些堆中移除物体。
And the game of NIM is a two-player game where players take turns removing objects from piles.

5625
08:51:31,854 --> 08:51:40,112
规则是：在任何给定的回合，你可以从这些堆中的任意一个、也就是这几行中的任何一行里，移除任意数量的物体。
And the rule is that on any given turn, you are allowed to remove as many objects as you want from any one of these piles, any one of these rows.

5626
08:51:40,272 --> 08:51:46,500
你必须至少移除一个物体，但你可以从恰好其中一个堆中移除任意数量的物体。
You have to remove at least one object, but you can remove as many as you want from exactly one of the piles.

5627
08:51:46,766 --> 08:51:49,604
谁拿走最后一个物体，谁就输了。
And whoever takes the last object loses.

5628
08:51:50,638 --> 08:51:54,352
所以玩家一可能会从这个堆里拿走四个。
So player one might remove four from this pile here.

5629
08:51:54,638 --> 08:52:00,272
玩家二可能也会从这个堆里拿走四个。现在我们剩下四个堆：1、3、1 和 3。
Player two might remove four from this pile here. So now we've got four piles left, one, three, one, and three.

5630
08:52:00,494 --> 08:52:03,684
玩家一可能会把第二个堆全部拿走。
Player one might remove, the entirety of the second pile.

5631
08:52:03,952 --> 08:52:06,032
如果玩家二采取策略的话，
Player two, if they're being strategic,

5632
08:52:07,472 --> 08:52:09,508
可能会从第三个堆里拿走两个。
might remove two from the third pile.

5633
08:52:09,806 --> 08:52:12,708
现在剩下三个堆，每个堆里只剩下一个物体。
Now we've got three piles left, each with one object left.

5634
08:52:13,102 --> 08:52:21,828
玩家一可能从一个堆中拿走一个，玩家二从另一个堆中拿走一个，现在轮到玩家一从最后一个堆中选择这一个物体时，
Player one might remove one from one pile, player two removes one from the other pile, and now player one is left with choosing this one object from the last pile,

5635
08:52:22,062 --> 08:52:24,260
此时玩家一就输掉比赛了。
at which point player one loses the game.

5636
08:52:24,654 --> 08:52:26,912
这是一个相当简单的游戏，就是一些物体的堆。
So fairly simple game, piles of objects.

5637
08:52:27,118 --> 08:52:32,804
每一轮你选择从一个堆中移除多少个物体，谁拿走最后一个物体谁就输了。
Any turn you choose how many objects to remove from a pile, whoever removes the last object loses.

5638
08:52:33,198 --> 08:52:39,312
这种类型的游戏可以非常容易地编码进 AI 中，因为状态其实只是四个数字。
And this is the type of game you could encode into an AI fairly easily, because the states are really just four numbers.

5639
08:52:39,472 --> 08:52:42,628
每个状态仅仅是这四个堆中各自有多少个物体。
Every state is just how many objects in each of the four piles.

5640
08:52:43,022 --> 08:52:48,228
而动作就是诸如“我要从这些单独的堆中的每一个里拿走多少个”之类的操作。
And the actions are things like how many am I going to remove from each one of these individual piles?

5641
08:52:48,974 --> 08:52:50,752
奖励会在最后发放。
And the reward happens at the end.

5642
08:52:50,990 --> 08:52:55,460
如果你是那个必须移除最后一个物体的玩家，你就会受到某种惩罚。
That if you were the player that had to remove the last object, then you get some sort of punishment.

5643
08:52:55,822 --> 08:53:01,284
但如果你不是，而对方玩家必须移除最后一个物体，那么你就获得奖励。
But if you were not and the other player had to remove the last object, well then you get some sort of reward.

5644
08:53:01,774 --> 08:53:07,620
所以我们可以展示一个演示，我实现了一个 AI 来玩 NIM 游戏。
So we could actually try and show a demonstration of this that I've implemented an AI to play the game of NIM.

5645
08:53:08,654 --> 08:53:08,992
好的。
All right.

5646
08:53:09,070 --> 08:53:16,912
现在我们要做的就是通过让 AI 与自己进行一定场次的对战来训练它，从而创建一个 AI，
so here what we're going to do is create an AI as a result of training the AI on some number of games that the AI is going to play against itself,

5647
08:53:17,070 --> 08:53:23,312
这里的思路是 AI 通过与自己对战，从每场经历中学习，并学会未来该如何行动。
where the idea is the AI will play games against itself, learn from each of those experiences, and learn what to do in the future.

5648
08:53:23,598 --> 08:53:25,952
然后我这个人类就会和 AI 对战。
And then I, the human, will play against the AI.

5649
08:53:26,286 --> 08:53:33,732
最初我们可以设置训练次数为零，这意味着我们不让 AI 进行任何自我对战来积累经验。
So initially we'll say train zero times, meaning we're not going to let the AI play any practice games against itself in order to learn from its experiences.

5650
08:53:33,998 --> 08:53:35,748
我们只是看看它表现如何。
We're just going to see how well it plays.

5651
08:53:36,782 --> 08:53:38,180
看起来有四个堆。
And it looks like there are four piles.

5652
08:53:38,352 --> 08:53:41,220
我可以选择从任何一个堆中移除多少个物体。
I can choose how many I remove from any one of the piles.

5653
08:53:41,518 --> 08:53:45,860
比如，我可能会从第三堆中移除五个物体。
So maybe from pile three I will remove five objects, for example.

5654
08:53:46,672 --> 08:53:49,952
现在 AI 选择从第零堆中拿走一个物品。
so now AI chose to take one item from pile zero.

5655
08:53:50,286 --> 08:53:52,548
所以现在我剩下这些堆，例如。
So I'm left with these piles now, for example.

5656
08:53:52,942 --> 08:54:00,804
在这里我可以选择，比如我想从第二堆中移除，我把那五个全部拿走。
And so here I could choose maybe to say, I would like to remove from pile two, I'll remove all five of them, for example.

5657
08:54:01,646 --> 08:54:03,872
然后 AI 选择从第一堆中拿走两个。
And so AI chose to take two away from pile one.

5658
08:54:04,206 --> 08:54:07,876
现在我剩下两个堆，一个有三个物体，一个有两个物体。
Now I'm left with one pile that has one object, one pile that has two objects.

5659
08:54:08,398 --> 08:54:17,156
所以从第三堆里我移除两个物体，现在 AI 除了拿走最后一个没别的选择了，游戏结束，我赢了。
So from pile three, I will remove two objects, and now I've left the AI with no choice but to take that last one, and so the game is over and I was able to win.

5660
08:54:17,678 --> 08:54:24,356
但我之所以能赢是因为 AI 只是在随机操作。它没有任何可以用来做这些判断的先前经验。
But I did so because the AI was really just playing randomly. It didn't have any prior experience that it was using in order to make these sorts of judgments.

5661
08:54:24,814 --> 08:54:28,832
现在让我让 AI 进行大约 10,000 场游戏的自我训练。
Now let me let the AI train itself on like 10,000 games.

5662
08:54:29,038 --> 08:54:32,612
我要让 AI 与自己对战，进行 10,000 场 NIM 游戏。
I'm going to let the AI play 10,000 games of NIM against itself.

5663
08:54:32,846 --> 08:54:39,140
每当它赢或输时，它都会从那次经验中学习，从而掌握未来该做什么、不该做什么。
Every time it wins or loses, it's going to learn from that experience and learn in the future what to do and what not to do.

5664
08:54:39,790 --> 08:54:40,452
那么现在，
So here then,

5665
08:54:41,102 --> 08:54:42,244
我来再次运行这个程序。
I'll go ahead and run this again.

5666
08:54:42,510 --> 08:54:50,272
现在你可以看到 AI 在进行大量的训练游戏，也就是与自己对战的 10,000 场练习，现在它会让我做这些决策了。
And now you see the AI running through a whole bunch of training games, 10,000 training games against itself, and now it's going to let me make these sorts of decisions.

5667
08:54:50,382 --> 08:54:52,260
现在我要和 AI 对战了。
So now I'm going to play against the AI.

5668
08:54:52,526 --> 08:54:55,140
也许我从第三堆里拿走一个。
Maybe I'll remove one from pile three.

5669
08:54:55,712 --> 08:54:58,884
然后 AI 把第三堆全部拿走了，所以我剩下三个堆。
and the AI took everything from pile three, so I'm left with three piles.

5670
08:54:59,392 --> 08:55:03,172
接下来我从第二堆中移除三个物品。
I'll go ahead and from pile two, maybe remove three items.

5671
08:55:04,590 --> 08:55:09,732
AI 从堆 0 中拿走一个。我剩下两个堆，每个堆里有两个物品。
and the AI removes one item from pile zero. I'm left with two piles, each of which has two items in it.

5672
08:55:10,352 --> 08:55:12,964
我想我得从堆 1 中拿走一个。
I'll remove one from pile one, I guess.

5673
08:55:14,350 --> 08:55:20,192
AI 从堆 2 中拿走了两个，所以我只能从堆 1 中拿走一个了。
and the AI took two from pile two, leaving me with no choice but to take one away from pile one.

5674
08:55:20,462 --> 08:55:28,672
所以看起来，在与自己对战 10,000 局 NIM 后，AI 学到了哪些状态和哪些动作往往是好的，
So it seems like after playing 10,000 games of NIM against itself, the AI has learned something about what states and what actions tend to be good,

5675
08:55:28,910 --> 08:55:36,352
并且开始学习某种模式，来预测在任何给定的
and has begun to learn some sort of pattern for how to predict what actions are going to be good and what actions are going to be bad in any given

5676
08:55:36,352 --> 08:55:45,792
状态下，哪些动作会是好动作，哪些动作会是坏动作。因此，强化学习可以成为实现这类游戏智能体的非常强大的技术，即那些仅通过从经验中学习就能很好地玩游戏的智能体，
state. So reinforcement learning can be a very powerful technique for achieving these sorts of game-playing agents, agents that are able to play a game well just by learning from experience,

5677
08:55:45,952 --> 08:55:51,472
无论这种经验是来自与其他人的对战，还是通过与自己对战并从中学习。
whether that's playing against other people, or by playing against itself and learning from those experiences as well.

5678
08:55:51,854 --> 08:55:56,912
现在，NIM 是一个比较容易用强化学习来处理的游戏，因为它的状态非常少。
Now, NIM is a bit of an easy game to use reinforcement learning for because there are so few states.

5679
08:55:57,072 --> 08:56:01,792
只有这些不同堆中物品数量对应的那么多状态。
There are only states that are as many as how many different objects are in each of these various different piles.

5680
08:56:02,062 --> 08:56:11,076
如果你考虑到像国际象棋这样的游戏，或者那些拥有更多、更多可能状态和更多、更多可选动作的游戏，你可能会觉得这会更难，
You might imagine that it's going to be harder if you think of a game like chess, or games where there are many, many more states and many, many more actions that you can imagine taking,

5681
08:56:11,312 --> 08:56:17,312
因为在这些情况下，很难为每一个状态和每一个动作去学习它的值。
where it's not going to be as easy to learn for every state and for every action what the value is going to be.

5682
08:56:17,550 --> 08:56:25,152
所以在那种情况下，我们不一定能精确地学到每个状态和每个动作的价值，但我们可以进行近似。
So oftentimes in that case, we can't necessarily learn exactly what the value is for every state and for every action, but we can approximate it.

5683
08:56:25,454 --> 08:56:33,792
就像我们之前看到的 Minimax 一样，我们可以使用深度限制的方法在特定时间点停止计算，我们可以进行类似的近似，
So much as we saw with Minimax, that we could use a depth limiting approach to stop calculating at a certain point in time, we can do a similar type of approximation,

5684
08:56:34,062 --> 08:56:42,500
在强化学习的语境中被称为函数近似。与其为每个状态和每个动作去学习 Q 值，
known as function approximation, in a reinforcement learning context, where instead of learning a value of Q for every state and every action,

5685
08:56:42,832 --> 08:56:52,032
我们只是使用一个函数来估算在特定状态下采取该动作的价值，这个估值可能基于该状态的各种不同特征，
we just have some function that estimates what the value is for taking this action in this particular state, that might be based on various different features of

5686
08:56:52,558 --> 08:56:53,072
这些特征是关于
the state

5687
08:56:53,966 --> 08:56:58,112
智能体当前所处的状态，你可能需要选择哪些特征才是真正重要的。
that the agent happens to be in, where you might have to choose what those features actually are.

5688
08:56:58,382 --> 08:57:08,192
但你可以开始学习一些能够超越单一特定状态和单一特定动作的规律，即如果你发现某些特征往往是好东西或坏东西。
But you can begin to learn some patterns that generalize beyond one specific state and one specific action, that you can begin to learn if certain features tend to be good things or bad things.

5689
08:57:08,494 --> 08:57:16,912
强化学习可以通过非常类似的机制，让你超越特定的状态进行泛化，比如如果另一个状态看起来很像这个状态，
Reinforcement learning can allow you, using a very similar mechanism, to generalize beyond one particular state and say, if this other state looks kind of like this state,

5690
08:57:17,134 --> 08:57:22,532
那么在其中一个状态中奏效的类似类型的动作，在另一个状态中可能也会奏效。
then maybe the similar types of actions that worked in one state will also work in another state as well.

5691
08:57:23,182 --> 08:57:30,032
因此，当你要处理具有越来越大状态空间的强化学习时，这种方法会非常有帮助，
And so this type of approach can be quite helpful as you begin to deal with reinforcement learning that exists in larger and larger state spaces

5692
08:57:30,126 --> 08:57:34,672
因为在这种情况下，去探索所有可能存在的状态是不切实际的。
where it's just not feasible to explore all of the possible states that could actually exist.

5693
08:57:36,078 --> 08:57:39,216
所以，强化学习主要分为两个类别。
So, there then are two of the main categories of reinforcement learning.

5694
08:57:39,456 --> 08:57:47,204
监督学习，即你拥有带标签的输入和输出对；以及强化学习，其中智能体从它获得的奖励或惩罚中进行学习。
Supervised learning, where you have labeled input and output pairs, and reinforcement learning, where an agent learns from rewards or punishments that it receives.

5695
08:57:47,456 --> 08:57:53,124
我们将简要提到的第三个主要的机器学习类别被称为无监督学习。
The third major category of machine learning that we'll just touch on briefly is known as unsupervised learning.

5696
08:57:53,326 --> 08:57:59,012
无监督学习发生在没有任何额外反馈、没有标签的情况下处理数据时。
And unsupervised learning happens when we have data without any additional feedback, without labels.

5697
08:57:59,246 --> 08:58:02,576
而在监督学习的情况下，我们所有的数据都有标签。
That in the supervised learning case, all of our data had labels.

5698
08:58:02,736 --> 08:58:09,376
我们将一个数据点标注为是雨天还是非雨天，并利用这些标签来推断出规律。
We labeled a data point with whether that was a rainy day or a not rainy day, and using those labels, we were able to infer what the pattern was.

5699
08:58:09,536 --> 08:58:17,616
或者我们将数据标记为假币或非假币，并利用这些标签进行推理和模式识别，从而弄清楚什么样的数据是真币，
Or we labeled data as a counterfeit banknote or not a counterfeit, and using those labels, we were able to draw inferences and patterns to figure out what

5700
08:58:17,870 --> 08:58:19,780
而什么样的不是。
does a banknote look like versus not.

5701
08:58:20,718 --> 08:58:27,812
在无监督学习中，我们无法获取任何标签，但我们仍然希望学习其中的一些规律。
In unsupervised learning, we don't have any access to any of those labels, but we still would like to learn some of those patterns.

5702
08:58:28,336 --> 08:58:33,156
而在无监督学习中，你可能想要执行的任务之一就是聚类。
And one of the tasks that you might want to perform in unsupervised learning is something like clustering.

5703
08:58:33,614 --> 08:58:41,796
聚类就是给定一组物体，将其组织成不同的簇，即相似的物体组。
Where clustering is just a task of given some set of objects, organize it into distinct clusters, groups of objects that are similar to one another.

5704
08:58:42,126 --> 08:58:44,228
聚类有很多应用场景。
And there's lots of applications for clustering.

5705
08:58:44,416 --> 08:58:54,256
它出现在基因研究中，如果你有一大堆不同的基因，并且在尝试跨群体或跨物种分析时，你想把它们聚类成相似的基因。
It comes up in genetic research where you might have a whole bunch of different genes and you want to cluster them into similar genes if you're trying to analyze across a population or across species.

5706
08:58:54,446 --> 08:58:59,216
它也出现在图像处理中，如果你想提取图像中的所有像素，并把它们聚类到图像的不同部分。
It comes up in an image if you want to take all the pixels of an image, cluster them into different parts of the image.

5707
08:58:59,536 --> 08:59:08,416
它在市场调研中也经常出现，比如你想把消费者分成不同的群体，以便知道针对特定产品的广告该投向哪些群体。
Comes a lot up in market research, if you want to divide your consumers into different groups so you know which groups to target with certain types of product advertisements, for example,

5708
08:59:08,576 --> 08:59:12,836
还有许多其他场景，聚类在这些情况下都非常适用。
and a number of other contexts as well in which clustering can be very applicable.

5709
08:59:13,216 --> 08:59:17,508
一种聚类技术是被称为 k-means 聚类的算法。
One technique for clustering is an algorithm known as k-means clustering.

5710
08:59:17,806 --> 08:59:24,292
k-means 聚类要做的事情是将我们所有的数据点分成 k 个不同的簇。
And what k means clustering is going to do is it is going to divide all of our data points into k different clusters,

5711
08:59:24,718 --> 08:59:32,228
它通过重复“将点分配到簇中，然后移动这些簇的中心”这一过程来实现。
and it's going to do so by repeating this process of assigning points to clusters and then moving around those clusters at centers.

5712
08:59:32,590 --> 08:59:41,892
我们将用中心来定义一个簇，即簇的中点，然后根据哪个中心离该点最近，就把点分配到那个簇中。
We're going to define a cluster by its center, the middle of the cluster, and then assign points to that cluster based on which center is closest to that point.

5713
08:59:42,350 --> 08:59:43,780
我现在给你们展示一个例子。
And I'll show you an example of that now.

5714
08:59:44,494 --> 08:59:55,204
例如，这里我有一大堆未标记的数据，只是分布在某种图形空间中的各种数据点，我想把它们分组到不同的簇中。
Here, for example, I have a whole bunch of unlabeled data, just various data points that are in some sort of graphical space, and I would like to group them into various different clusters.

5715
08:59:55,566 --> 08:59:57,136
但我最初不知道该怎么做。
But I don't know how to do that originally.

5716
08:59:57,296 --> 09:00:00,576
假设我想给这个群体分配三个簇。
And let's say I want to assign like three clusters to this group.

5717
09:00:00,782 --> 09:00:06,468
在 k-means 聚类中，你必须选择想要多少个簇，你可以尝试多个值并看看这些值的表现如何。
And you have to choose how many clusters you want in k-means clustering, that you could try multiple and see how well those values perform.

5718
09:00:06,798 --> 09:00:11,776
但我先从随机选择一些位置作为这些簇的中心开始。
But I'll start just by randomly picking some places to put the centers of those clusters.

5719
09:00:12,176 --> 09:00:19,844
也许我有一个蓝色簇、一个红色簇和一个绿色簇，我将这些簇的中心初始设在这里的这三个位置。
maybe I have a blue cluster, a red cluster, and a green cluster, and I'm going to start with the centers of those clusters just being in these three locations here.

5720
09:00:20,526 --> 09:00:31,652
k-means 聚类告诉我们要做的是：一旦有了簇的中心，就根据每个点离哪个簇中心最近，将其分配到对应的簇中。
And what k-means clustering tells us to do is once I have the centers of the clusters, assign every point to a cluster based on which cluster center it is closest to.

5721
09:00:32,462 --> 09:00:39,396
所以我们最终得到像这样的结果，其中所有这些点都比其他任何簇中心更靠近蓝色簇中心。
So we end up with something like this, where all of these points are closer to the blue cluster center than any other cluster center.

5722
09:00:40,176 --> 09:00:45,444
这里所有的这些点都比其他任何簇中心更靠近绿色簇中心。
All of these points here are closer to the green cluster center than any other cluster center.

5723
09:00:45,742 --> 09:00:52,068
然后这两个点加上这里的这些点，它们都是最接近红色簇中心的。
And then these two points plus these points over here, those are all closest to the red cluster center instead.

5724
09:00:53,102 --> 09:00:58,276
所以这就是将所有这些点分配到三个不同簇的一种可能方案。
So here then is one possible assignment of all these points to three different clusters.

5725
09:00:58,862 --> 09:00:59,696
但这并不理想。
But it's not great.

5726
09:00:59,950 --> 09:01:05,616
看起来在这个红色簇中，这些点分布得比较散；在这个绿色簇中，这些点也离得挺远。
That it seems like in this red cluster these points are kind of far apart, in this green cluster, these points are kind of far apart.

5727
09:01:05,776 --> 09:01:10,052
这可能不是我对如何聚类这些不同数据点的理想选择。
It might not be my ideal choice of how I would cluster these various different data points.

5728
09:01:10,606 --> 09:01:20,964
但 k-means 聚类是一个迭代过程，在我完成这一步后，还有下一步：就是在将所有点分配到最近的簇中心后，
But k-means clustering is an iterative process that after I do this, there is a next step, which is that after I've assigned all of the points to the cluster center that it is nearest to,

5729
09:01:21,296 --> 09:01:23,908
我们将重新调整簇的中心。
we are going to recenter the clusters.

5730
09:01:24,270 --> 09:01:33,696
也就是说，取这些簇的中心（就是这里的菱形形状），并将它们移动到该簇中所有点的中心位置，或者说有效地移动到平均位置。
Meaning take the cluster centers, these diamond shapes here, and move them to the middle, or the average effectively, of all of the points that are in that cluster.

5731
09:01:33,998 --> 09:01:41,668
所以我们要把这个蓝点，也就是蓝色中心，移动到所有被分配到蓝色簇的点的中心位置，
So we'll take this blue point, this blue center, and go ahead and move it to the middle or to the center of all of the points that were assigned to the blue cluster,

5732
09:01:41,936 --> 09:01:43,524
在这种情况下，它会稍微向右移动一点。
moving it slightly to the right in this case.

5733
09:01:43,918 --> 09:01:48,708
我们对红色也做同样的操作。我们将聚类中心移动到所有这些点的中心，
And we'll do the same thing for red. We'll move the cluster center to the middle of all of these

5734
09:01:49,422 --> 09:01:56,416
根据点的数量进行加权。因为这边的点更多，所以红色中心会向那边移动一点。
points, weighted by how many points there are. There are more points over here, so the red center ends up moving a little bit further that way.

5735
09:01:56,686 --> 09:02:05,136
同样地，对于绿色中心，由于这一侧的绿点更多，因此绿色中心会被拉向这个方向。
And likewise for the green center, there are many more points on this side of the green center, so the green center ends up being pulled a little bit further in this direction.

5736
09:02:05,966 --> 09:02:09,920
所以我们重新调整所有聚类的中心，然后重复这个过程。
so we re-center all of the clusters, and then we repeat the process.

5737
09:02:10,080 --> 09:02:15,588
现在我们将所有点重新分配到它们当前最近的聚类中心。
We go ahead and now reassign all of the points to the cluster center that they are now closest to.

5738
09:02:16,014 --> 09:02:20,320
由于我们移动了聚类中心，这些点的所属类别可能会发生变化。
And now that we've moved around the cluster centers, these cluster assignments might change.

5739
09:02:20,622 --> 09:02:26,500
这个点最初离红色中心更近，但现在它实际上离蓝色中心更近了。
That this point originally was closer to the red cluster center, but now it's actually closer to the blue cluster center.

5740
09:02:26,894 --> 09:02:28,292
这个点也是同样的道理。
Same goes for this point as well.

5741
09:02:28,480 --> 09:02:35,748
而这三个原本离绿色中心较近的点，现在反而离红色中心更近了。
And these three points that were originally closer to the green cluster center are now closer to the red cluster center instead.

5742
09:02:36,526 --> 09:02:43,716
所以我们可以重新分配每个数据点的颜色或所属聚类，然后再次重复这个过程。
So we can reassign what colors or which clusters each of these data points belongs to, and then repeat the process again.

5743
09:02:44,000 --> 09:02:50,308
将这些聚类的均值移动到属于该聚类的所有其他点中，
Moving each of these cluster means on the middles of the clusters to the mean, the average of all of the other

5744
09:02:51,214 --> 09:02:53,956
即所有恰好在那里的点的平均值，并再次重复这个过程。
points that happen to be there, and repeat the process again.

5745
09:02:54,318 --> 09:02:58,084
去把每个点分配到它们最近的那个聚类里。
Go ahead and assign each of the points to the cluster that they are closest to.

5746
09:02:58,478 --> 09:03:07,680
一旦我们达到一个所有点都已分配到最近中心且没有任何变化的状态，我们就达到了某种平衡状态，
So once we reach a point where we've assigned all the points to clusters to the cluster that they are nearest to, and nothing changed, we've reached a sort of equilibrium in this situation,

5747
09:03:07,840 --> 09:03:09,700
此时没有任何点的归属发生改变。
where no points are changing their allegiance.

5748
09:03:09,902 --> 09:03:17,040
结果就是，我们可以宣布这个算法结束了，现在我们已经将这些点分配到了三个不同的聚类中。
And as a result, we can declare this algorithm is now over, and we now have some assignment of each of these points into three different clusters.

5749
09:03:17,120 --> 09:03:24,400
看起来我们在识别哪些点彼此更相似、而非属于其他组的点的方面做得相当不错。
And it looks like we did a pretty good job of trying to identify which points are more similar to one another than they are to points in other groups.

5750
09:03:24,526 --> 09:03:29,796
所以我们现在有这里的绿色聚类，这里的蓝色聚类，还有那边的红色聚类。
So we have the green cluster down here, this blue cluster here, and then this red cluster over there as well.

5751
09:03:30,446 --> 09:03:35,716
而且我们完成这一切时，并没有利用任何标签来告诉我们这些不同的聚类分别是什么。
And we did so without any access to some labels to tell us what these various different clusters were.

5752
09:03:36,000 --> 09:03:43,360
我们只是在无监督的情况下使用算法，在没有任何标签的情况下，找出哪些点属于哪些类别。
We just used an algorithm in an unsupervised sense, without any of those labels, to figure out which points belonged to which categories.

5753
09:03:43,598 --> 09:03:47,108
这种聚类技术有很多应用场景。
And again, lots of applications for this type of clustering technique.

5754
09:03:47,662 --> 09:03:53,924
在机器学习的各个领域——包括监督学习、强化学习和无监督学习中，还有许多其他的算法。
And there are many more algorithms in each of these various different fields within machine learning, supervised and reinforcement and unsupervised.

5755
09:03:54,254 --> 09:03:58,960
但这些都是支撑许多此类技术的宏观基础理念。
But those are many of the big picture foundational ideas that underlie a lot of these techniques.

5756
09:03:59,212 --> 09:04:01,280
这些是我们试图解决的问题。
where These are the problems that we're trying to solve.

5757
09:04:01,486 --> 09:04:10,756
我们尝试通过多种不同的方法来解决这些问题，即获取数据并从中学习模式，无论是寻找相似的相邻数据点，
And we try and solve those problems using a number of different methods of trying to take data and learn patterns in that data, whether that's trying to find neighboring data points that are similar,

5758
09:04:10,894 --> 09:04:18,468
还是试图最小化某种损失函数，或者使用任何其他允许我们开始尝试解决这类问题的技术。
or trying to minimize some sort of loss function, or any number of other techniques that allow us to begin to try to solve these sorts of problems.

5759
09:04:19,342 --> 09:04:28,420
刚才我们回顾了一些现代机器学习的基础原理，即从数据中学习的能力，从而让计算机能够执行任务，
That then was a look at some of the principles that are at the foundation of modern machine learning, this ability to take data and learn from that data so that the computer can perform a task,

5760
09:04:28,560 --> 09:04:31,972
即使它们并没有被明确给出执行这些任务的指令。
even if they haven't explicitly been given instructions in order to do so.

5761
09:04:32,430 --> 09:04:38,320
下次我们将继续关于机器学习的讨论，看看还有哪些可以用来解决这类问题的技术。
Next time we'll continue this conversation about machine learning, looking at other techniques we can use for solving these sorts of problems.

5762
09:04:38,574 --> 09:04:39,204
到时见。
We'll see you then.

5763
09:05:11,520 --> 09:05:18,116
学习如何执行一项任务，即使我们作为程序员没有给计算机提供明确的操作指令。
Learn how to perform a task, even if we the programmers didn't give the computer explicit instructions for how to perform that task.

5764
09:05:18,766 --> 09:05:24,068
今天我们将转向机器学习中最流行的方法和工具之一：神经网络。
Today we transition to one of the most popular techniques and tools within machine learning, that of neural networks.

5765
09:05:24,558 --> 09:05:32,452
神经网络早在 20 世纪 40 年代就受到启发，当时的研究人员正在思考人类是如何学习的，他们研究了人类大脑中的神经科学，
And neural networks were inspired as early as the 1940s by researchers who were thinking about how it is that humans learn, studying neuroscience in the human brain,

5766
09:05:32,622 --> 09:05:38,852
并试图看看是否也能将这些想法应用于计算机，并模仿人类的学习过程来构建计算机的学习模型。
and trying to see whether or not we could apply those same ideas to computers as well, and model computer learning off of human learning.

5767
09:05:39,470 --> 09:05:41,360
那么，大脑的结构是怎样的呢？
So, how is the brain structured?

5768
09:05:41,520 --> 09:05:49,348
简单来说，大脑由大量的神经元组成，这些神经元相互连接并以某种方式进行交流。
Well, very simply put, the brain consists of a whole bunch of neurons, and those neurons are connected to one another and communicate with one another in some way.

5769
09:05:49,774 --> 09:05:56,932
特别是，如果你思考一下生物神经网络的结构，就像这样的结构，科学家们观察到了几个关键特性。
In particular, if you think about the structure of a biological neural network, something like this, there are a couple of key properties that scientists observed.

5770
09:05:57,280 --> 09:06:05,284
其中一个是这些神经元相互连接并接收来自彼此的电信号，即一个神经元可以将电信号传递给另一个神经元。
One was that these neurons are connected to each other and receive electrical signals from one another, that one neuron can propagate electrical signals to another neuron.

5771
09:06:06,062 --> 09:06:12,451
另一个点是，神经元会处理这些输入信号并被激活，也就是说，一个神经元会在特定点变得活跃，
And another point is that neurons process those input signals and then can be activated, that a neuron becomes activated at a certain point

5772
09:06:12,750 --> 09:06:16,196
然后可以在未来将信号进一步传递给其他神经元。
and then can propagate further signals onto neurons in the future.

5773
09:06:16,718 --> 09:06:25,167
于是问题变成了：我们能否借鉴这种人类通过大脑和神经元进行学习的生物学理念，并将其应用到机器上？
And so the question then became: could we take this biological idea of how it is that humans learn with brains and with neurons and apply that to a machine as well?

5774
09:06:25,390 --> 09:06:34,307
实际上，就是设计一个人工神经网络（或称 ANN），它是一个受这些生物神经网络启发的、用于学习的数学模型。
In effect, designing an artificial neural network, or an ANN, which will be a mathematical model for learning that is inspired by these biological neural networks.

5775
09:06:34,830 --> 09:06:40,688
而人工神经网络能让我们做到的，是它们首先能够模拟某种数学函数。
And what artificial neural networks will allow us to do is they will first be able to model some sort of mathematical function.

5776
09:06:40,848 --> 09:06:49,508
每当你看到一个神经网络（我们稍后会更多地接触它），每一个网络本质上都是一种将特定输入映射到特定输出的数学函数
Every time you look at a neural network, which we'll see more of later today, each one of them is really just some mathematical function that is mapping certain inputs to particular outputs

5777
09:06:49,870 --> 09:06:58,947
这取决于网络的结构，即我们在这个神经网络中放置特定的单元在什么位置，这将决定网络如何运行。
based on the structure of the network, that depending on where we place particular units inside of this neural network, that's going to determine how it is that the network is going to function.

5778
09:06:59,598 --> 09:07:07,008
特别是，人工神经网络提供了一种我们可以学习网络参数的方法。
And in particular, artificial neural networks are going to lend themselves to a way that we can learn what the network's parameters should be.

5779
09:07:07,246 --> 09:07:08,608
我们马上就会看到更多相关内容。
We'll see more on that in just a moment.

5780
09:07:08,814 --> 09:07:18,019
但本质上，我们想要一个模型，让我们能够轻松编写代码，让网络能够根据特定的输入数据，找出如何建模正确的数学函数。
But in effect, we want a model such that it is easy for us to be able to write some code that allows for the network to be able to figure out how to model the right mathematical function

5781
09:07:18,190 --> 09:07:26,820
因此，为了创建我们的人工神经网络，我们不再使用生物神经元，而是使用我们称之为“单元”的东西。
given a particular set of input data. So in order to create our artificial neural network, instead of using biological neurons, we're just going to use what we're going to call units.

5782
09:07:27,167 --> 09:07:33,956
神经网络内部的单元可以被视为图中的节点，在这里将用这样的蓝色圆圈来表示。
Units inside of a neural network, which we can represent kind of like a node in a graph, which will here be represented just by a blue circle like this.

5783
09:07:34,446 --> 09:07:39,008
这些人工单元，也就是人工神经元，可以相互连接。
And these artificial units, these artificial neurons, can be connected to one another.

5784
09:07:39,214 --> 09:07:45,284
例如，这里有两个通过这个图中的边连接的单元。
So here, for instance, we have two units that are connected by this edge inside of this graph, effectively.

5785
09:07:46,318 --> 09:07:51,568
所以我们现在要做的是，将这个想法视为一种从输入到输出的映射。
And so what we're going to do now is think of this idea as some sort of mapping from inputs to outputs.

5786
09:07:51,728 --> 09:07:57,860
我们有一个与另一个单元相连的单元，我们可以把这一侧视为输入，那一侧视为输出。
So we have one unit that is connected to another unit that we might think of this side as the input and that side of the output.

5787
09:07:58,413 --> 09:08:04,004
然后我们试图做的是找出如何解决问题，即如何建模某种数学函数。
And what we're trying to do then is to figure out how to solve a problem, how to model some sort of mathematical function.

5788
09:08:04,237 --> 09:08:13,476
这可能采取我们上次看到的某种形式，也就是我们有一些特定的输入，比如变量 x1 和 x2，在给定这些输入的情况下，我们想执行某些任务。
And this might take the form of something we saw last time, which was something like we have certain inputs like variables x1 and x2, and given those inputs, we want to perform some sort of task.

5789
09:08:13,807 --> 09:08:16,608
例如预测是否会下雨。
A task like predicting whether or not it's going to rain.

5790
09:08:16,782 --> 09:08:22,980
理想情况下，我们希望有一种方法，在给定代表与天气相关的变量的这些输入 x1 和 x2 时……
And ideally, we'd like some way, given these inputs x1 and x2, which stand for some sort of variables to do with the weather,

5791
09:08:23,167 --> 09:08:26,756
在这种情况下，我们希望能够进行布尔分类。
we would like to be able to predict, in this case, a Boolean classification.

5792
09:08:27,008 --> 09:08:29,476
是会下雨还是不会下雨？
Is it going to rain or is it not going to rain?

5793
09:08:30,125 --> 09:08:33,088
上次我们通过一个数学函数来实现这一点。
And we did this last time by way of a mathematical function.

5794
09:08:33,326 --> 09:08:40,964
我们定义了一个函数 h 作为我们的假设函数，它接收 x1 和 x2 作为输入，这两个是我们关心的处理输入变量。
We defined some function, h, for our hypothesis function, that took as input x1 and x2, the two inputs that we cared about processing,

5795
09:08:41,167 --> 09:08:45,540
目的是来判断我们认为会下雨还是不会下雨。
in order to determine whether we thought it was going to rain or whether we thought it was not going to rain.

5796
09:08:46,158 --> 09:08:51,012
那么问题变成了，这个假设函数是如何做出这一判断的？
The question then becomes, what does this hypothesis function do in order to make that determination?

5797
09:08:51,374 --> 09:08:57,924
上次我们决定使用这些输入变量的线性组合来确定输出应该是多少。
And we decided last time to use a linear combination of these input variables to determine what the output should be.

5798
09:08:58,190 --> 09:09:06,884
所以我们的假设函数等于类似这样的：权重零加上权重一乘以 x1，再加上权重二乘以 x2。
So our hypothesis function was equal to something like this weight zero plus weight one times x1 plus weight two times x2.

5799
09:09:07,598 --> 09:09:14,436
这里的情况是，x1 和 x2 是输入变量，是这个假设函数的输入。
So what's going on here is that x1 and x2, those are input variables, the inputs to this hypothesis function.

5800
09:09:14,989 --> 09:09:20,127
每一个输入变量都会乘以一个权重，也就是一个数字。
And each of those input variables is being multiplied by some weight, which is just some number.

5801
09:09:20,398 --> 09:09:26,688
所以 x1 被乘上权重一，x2 被乘上权重二，然后我们还有一个额外的权重，
So x1 is being multiplied by weight one, x2 is being multiplied by weight two, and we have this additional weight,

5802
09:09:26,848 --> 09:09:33,568
就是权重零，它并不乘以任何输入变量，它的作用只是让函数向上移动或者让函数的数值向下移动。
weight zero, that doesn't get multiplied by an input variable at all, that just serves to either move the function up or move the function's value down.

5803
09:09:33,807 --> 09:09:41,379
你可以把它看作是一个乘上某个占位值（比如数字一）的权重，因为它被乘了一，所以它没被乘上任何东西。
You can think of this as either a weight that's just multiplied by some dummy value, like the number one, and it's multiplied by one, and so it's not multiplied by anything.

5804
09:09:41,773 --> 09:09:48,608
或者有时在文献中，人们把这个变量权重零称为偏置，这样你可以把这些变量看作是略有不同的。
Or sometimes you'll see in the literature, people call this variable weight zero a bias, so that you can think of these variables as slightly different.

5805
09:09:48,688 --> 09:09:54,180
我们有乘上输入的权重，并且还会分别给结果加上一些偏置。
We have weights that are multiplied by the input, and we separately add some bias to the result as well.

5806
09:09:54,510 --> 09:09:58,947
当人们讨论神经网络和机器学习时，你会听到这两种术语都会被用到。
You'll hear both of those terminologies used when people talk about neural networks and machine learning.

5807
09:09:59,982 --> 09:10:07,663
所以，实际上我们在这里所做的就是，为了定义一个假设函数，我们只需要决定并弄清楚这些权重应该
So, in effect, what we've done here is that in order to define a hypothesis function, we just need to decide and figure out what these weights should

5808
09:10:07,663 --> 09:10:11,875
是多少，从而确定要乘上我们的输入以获得某种结果的数值。
be to determine what values to multiply by our inputs to get some sort of result.

5809
09:10:12,462 --> 09:10:17,663
当然，到最后，我们需要做的是进行某种分类，比如“有雨”或“无雨”。
Of course, at the end of this, what we need to do is make some sort of classification, like rainy or not rainy.

5810
09:10:18,061 --> 09:10:21,956
为了做到这一点，我们使用一种定义了某种阈值的函数。
And to do that, we use some sort of function that defines some sort of threshold.

5811
09:10:22,318 --> 09:10:26,464
例如，我们看到了阶跃函数，它的定义是：
And so we saw, for instance, the step function, which is defined as one

5812
09:10:28,014 --> 09:10:32,384
如果权重乘以输入的乘积至少为零，结果就是一，否则就是零。
if the result of multiplying the weights by the inputs is at least zero, otherwise it's zero.

5813
09:10:32,624 --> 09:10:35,424
你可以把中间这条线看作是一条虚线。
And you can think of this line down the middle as kind of like a dotted line.

5814
09:10:35,598 --> 09:10:40,944
实际上，它一直保持在零直到到达一点，然后函数就会跳跃或跳到一。
Effectively, it stays at zero all the way up to one point, and then the function steps or jumps up to one.

5815
09:10:41,294 --> 09:10:46,468
也就是说，在达到某个阈值之前它是零，而在达到特定阈值后它就是一。
So it's zero before it reaches some threshold, and then it's one after it reaches a particular threshold.

5816
09:10:46,894 --> 09:10:50,915
这就是我们定义所谓激活函数的一种方法。
And so this was one way we could define what we'll come to call an activation function.

5817
09:10:51,104 --> 09:10:57,540
一个决定输出何时变为活跃、从零变为一的函数。
A function that determines when it is that this output becomes active, changes to a zero one instead of being a zero.

5818
09:10:58,286 --> 09:11:06,544
但我们也看到，如果我们不想要纯粹的二分类，不想只有一或零，而是想允许一些中间的
But we also saw that if we didn't just want a purely binary classification, we didn't want purely one or zero, but we wanted to allow for some in-between

5819
09:11:06,733 --> 09:11:09,104
实数值，我们可以使用不同的函数。
real-numbered values, we could use a different function.

5820
09:11:09,262 --> 09:11:15,492
有很多种选择，但我们看的是具有 S 形曲线的逻辑回归Sigmoid函数。
And there are a number of choices, but the one that we looked at was the logistic sigmoid function that has sort of an S-shaped curve,

5821
09:11:15,758 --> 09:11:25,264
我们可以把它表示为一种概率，比如在中间某个位置，降雨概率可能是 0.5，而在稍后一点，降雨概率可能是 0.8。
where we could represent this as a probability that maybe somewhere in between, the probability of rain is something like 0.5, maybe a little bit later the probability of rain is 0.8.

5822
09:11:25,614 --> 09:11:32,064
所以与其只做 0 或 1 的二分类，我们也可以允许包含处于两者之间的数值。
And so rather than just have a binary classification of 0 or 1, we could allow for numbers that are in between as well.

5823
09:11:32,269 --> 09:11:40,580
事实证明还有许多其他不同类型的激活函数，激活函数的作用就是对权重乘积的结果加上偏置，
And it turns out there are many other different types of activation functions, where an activation function just takes the output of multiplying the weights together and adding that bias,

5824
09:11:40,942 --> 09:11:43,504
然后确定最终的输出应该是多少。
and then figuring out what the actual output should be.

5825
09:11:43,744 --> 09:11:47,424
另一个常用的就是修正线性单元，也就是我们常说的 ReLU。
Another popular one is the rectified linear unit, otherwise known as Relu.

5826
09:11:47,983 --> 09:11:52,771
它的工作原理是：它接收输入，并取该输入与零之间的最大值。
And the way that works is that it just takes its input and takes the maximum of that input and zero.

5827
09:11:52,942 --> 09:11:58,784
所以如果它是正数，就保持不变；但如果是零或者负数，它就会平滑到零。
So if it's positive, it remains unchanged, but if it's zero, if it's negative, it goes ahead and levels out at zero.

5828
09:11:58,958 --> 09:12:01,924
我们也可以选择其他的激活函数。
And there are other activation functions that we could choose as well.

5829
09:12:02,413 --> 09:12:10,224
简而言之，你可以把这些激活函数中的每一个都看作是应用于所有计算结果的一个函数。
But in short, each of these activation functions you can just think of as a function that gets applied to the result of all of this computation.

5830
09:12:10,384 --> 09:12:14,595
我们取一个函数 g，并将其应用于所有计算的结果。
We take some function g and apply it to the result of all of that calculation.

5831
09:12:15,374 --> 09:12:23,523
这就是我们上次看到的：定义一种假设函数，它接收输入，计算这些输入的线性组合，
And this then is what we saw last time: the way of defining some hypothesis function that takes in inputs, calculates some linear combination of those inputs,

5832
09:12:23,949 --> 09:12:28,163
然后通过某种激活函数来获得我们的输出。
and then passes it through some sort of activation function to get our output.

5833
09:12:28,718 --> 09:12:33,156
而这实际上就是最简单的神经网络模型。
And this actually turns out to be the model for the simplest of neural networks.

5834
09:12:33,343 --> 09:12:38,788
我们将用这种结构，把这个数学概念在图形上表示出来。
That we're going to instead represent this mathematical idea graphically by using a structure like this.

5835
09:12:39,341 --> 09:12:45,572
这里有一个拥有两个输入的神经网络，我们可以把这个看作 x1，这个是 x2，然后有一个输出，
Here then is a neural network that has two inputs, we can think of this as x1 and this is x2, and then one output,

5836
09:12:45,870 --> 09:12:51,972
比如在这个特定例子中，你可以把它看作是在分类我们认为是否会下雨。
which you can think of as classifying whether or not we think it's going to rain or not rain, for example, in this particular instance.

5837
09:12:52,622 --> 09:12:54,303
那么这个模型具体是如何运作的呢？
And so how exactly does this model work?

5838
09:12:54,574 --> 09:12:59,076
嗯，这两个输入中的每一个都代表我们的输入变量 x1 和 x2。
Well, each of these two inputs represents one of our input variables, x1 and x2.

5839
09:12:59,598 --> 09:13:06,532
注意这些输入通过这些边连接到输出上，这些边将由它们的权重来定义。
And notice that these inputs are connected to this output via these edges, which are going to be defined by their weights.

5840
09:13:06,989 --> 09:13:11,172
所以这些边每一条都有对应的权重，权重一和权重二。
So these edges each have a weight associated with them, weight one and weight two.

5841
09:13:11,949 --> 09:13:18,627
然后这个输出单元要做的是：根据这些输入和这些权重来计算出一个输出。
And then this output unit, what it's going to do is it is going to calculate an output based on those inputs and based on those weights.

5842
09:13:19,214 --> 09:13:27,716
这个输出单元会将所有输入乘以它们对应的权重，再加上这个偏置项，你可以把它看作是一个额外的 W0 项被加进去，
This output unit is going to multiply all the inputs by their weights, add in this bias term, which you can think of as an extra W0 term that gets added into it,

5843
09:13:28,014 --> 09:13:30,339
然后我们将其传递给一个激活函数。
and then we pass it through an activation function.

5844
09:13:31,053 --> 09:13:36,624
所以这只是用图形化的方式来表达我们上次看到的那个数学概念。
So this then is just a graphical way of representing the same idea we saw last time, just mathematically.

5845
09:13:36,750 --> 09:13:39,523
我们将这个称为一个非常简单的神经网络。
And we're going to call this a very simple neural network.

5846
09:13:40,078 --> 09:13:44,356
我们希望这个神经网络能够学会如何计算某个函数。
And we'd like for this neural network to be able to learn how to calculate some function.

5847
09:13:44,557 --> 09:13:53,983
我们希望神经网络去学习某个特定的函数，而神经网络将要学习 W0、W1 和 W2 的值应该是多少，以及激活函数应该是怎样的，
That we want some function for the neural network to learn, and the neural network is going to learn what should the values of W0, W1, and W2 be, what should the activation function be,

5848
09:13:54,190 --> 09:13:56,356
以便得到我们预期的结果。
in order to get the result that we would expect.

5849
09:13:57,262 --> 09:13:59,167
所以我们可以实际看一个例子。
So we can actually take a look at an example of this.

5850
09:13:59,406 --> 09:14:01,796
那么，我们可能会计算的一个非常简单的函数是什么呢？
What then is a very simple function that we might calculate?

5851
09:14:02,381 --> 09:14:10,767
好了，如果我们回顾一下之前学习命题逻辑时的内容，我们看过的最简单的函数之一就是像这样的 OR 函数，它有两个输入，
Well, if we recall back from when we were looking at propositional logic, one of the simplest functions we looked at was something like the OR function that takes two inputs,

5852
09:14:11,246 --> 09:14:19,408
x 和 y，如果其中任何一个或两个输入都是 1（即真），输出就是 1；否则，如果两个输入都是 0，
x and y, and outputs one, otherwise known as true, if either one of the inputs or both of them are one, and outputs a zero

5853
09:14:19,629 --> 09:14:21,732
输出就是 0。
if both of the inputs are zero or false.

5854
09:14:22,286 --> 09:14:25,572
这就是 OR 函数，而这是 OR 函数的真值表。
So this then is the OR function, and this was the truth table for the OR function.

5855
09:14:25,838 --> 09:14:33,860
只要任何一个输入是 1，函数的输出就是 1；只有当两个输入都是 0 时，输出才是 0。
That as long as either of the inputs are one, the output of the function is one, and the only case where the output is zero is where both of the inputs are zero.

5856
09:14:34,478 --> 09:14:40,368
那么问题来了，我们如何利用这个并训练一个神经网络来学习这个特定的函数？
