5882
09:16:17,807 --> 09:16:21,568
嗯，1 乘以 1 是 1，1 乘以 1 是 1，它们的和就是 2。
Well, one times one is one, one times one is one, the sum of those is two.

5883
09:16:22,125 --> 09:16:24,288
加上偏置项后，我得到数字 1。
I add the bias term to that, I get the number one.

5884
09:16:24,750 --> 09:16:30,820
在图上标注 1 的位置就在那儿，远超阈值，所以这里的输出也是 1。
One plotted on this graph is way over there, that's well beyond the threshold, and so this output is going to be one as well.

5885
09:16:31,053 --> 09:16:35,235
输出始终是 0 或 1，取决于我们是否超过了阈值。
The output is always zero or one, depending on whether or not we're past the threshold.

5886
09:16:35,534 --> 09:16:38,627
这个神经网络随后就模拟了 OR 函数。
And this neural network then models the OR function.

5887
09:16:38,848 --> 09:16:42,447
虽然这是一个非常简单的函数，但它依然能被正确建模。
A very simple function, definitely, but it still is able to model it correctly.

5888
09:16:42,542 --> 09:16:47,492
如果我给它输入，它会告诉我 x1 或 x2 的情况。
If I give it the inputs, it will tell me what x1 or x2 happens to be.

5889
09:16:48,078 --> 09:16:53,316
你也可以想象为其他函数做同样的事情。比如像 与 函数这样的函数，
And you could imagine trying to do this for other functions as well. A function like the and function, for instance,

5890
09:16:54,093 --> 09:16:59,012
它接收两个输入，并计算 x 和 y 是否都为真。
that takes two inputs and calculates whether both x and y are true.

5891
09:16:59,406 --> 09:17:03,728
所以如果 x 是 1 且 y 是 1，那么 x 与 y 的输出就是 1。
So if x is one and y is one, then the output of x and y is one.

5892
09:17:04,110 --> 09:17:06,595
但在所有其他情况下，输出都是 0。
But in all the other cases, the output is zero.

5893
09:17:07,150 --> 09:17:09,924
我们如何也能在神经网络中建模它呢？
How could we model that inside of a neural network as well?

5894
09:17:10,413 --> 09:17:19,396
结果发现我们可以用同样的方法来做，只不过不是用 -1 作为偏置，而是用 -2 作为偏置。
Well, it turns out we could do it in the same way, except instead of negative one as the bias, we can use negative two as the bias instead.

5895
09:17:20,014 --> 09:17:21,124
那最后看起来会是什么样？
What does that end up looking like?

5896
09:17:21,390 --> 09:17:26,692
嗯，如果我有 1 和 1，结果应该是 1，因为“真且真”等于“真”。
Well, if I had one and one, that should be one, because one true and true is equal to true.

5897
09:17:27,086 --> 09:17:28,688
好，我计算 1 乘以 1，那是 1。
Well, I take one times one, that's one.

5898
09:17:29,038 --> 09:17:31,940
1 乘以 1 是 1，到目前为止总和是 2。
One times one is one, I get a total sum of two so far.

5899
09:17:32,302 --> 09:17:41,796
现在我加上 -2 的偏置，得到值 0。而 0 在激活函数上刚好过了那个阈值，所以输出将是 1。
Now I add the bias of negative two and I get the value zero. And zero, when I plot it on the activation function, is just past that threshold, and so the output is going to be one.

5900
09:17:42,542 --> 09:17:50,528
但如果我加入任何其他输入，比如 1 和 0，那么这些的加权和就是 1 加 0 等于 1。
But if I add any other input, for example, like one and zero, well, the weighted sum of these is one plus zero is going to be one.

5901
09:17:51,053 --> 09:17:57,732
减去 2 后会得到 -1，而 -1 没有超过那个阈值，所以输出将是 0。
Minus two is going to give us negative one, and negative one is not past that threshold, and so the output is going to be zero.

5902
09:17:58,830 --> 09:18:05,487
所以，这些都是我们可以使用具有两个输入和一个输出的神经网络来建模的简单函数，
So, those then are some very simple functions that we can model using a neural network that has two inputs and one output,

5903
09:18:05,742 --> 09:18:10,848
我们的目标是找出这些权重应该是多少，从而确定输出应该是多少。
where our goal is to be able to figure out what those weights should be in order to determine what the output should be.

5904
09:18:11,086 --> 09:18:14,767
你也可以想象将此推广到计算更复杂的函数。
And you could imagine generalizing this to calculate more complex functions as well.

5905
09:18:14,848 --> 09:18:20,608
例如，给定湿度和气压，我们想计算降雨的概率。
That maybe given the humidity and the pressure, we want to calculate what's the probability that it's going to rain, for example.

5906
09:18:20,877 --> 09:18:22,767
或者我们可能想做一个回归类的问题。
Or we might want to do a regression style problem.

5907
09:18:22,848 --> 09:18:30,208
给定一定的广告投入和月份信息，也许我们想预测那个特定月份的预期销售额。
We're given some amount of advertising and given what month it is, maybe, we want to predict what our expected sales are going to be for that particular month.

5908
09:18:30,478 --> 09:18:33,508
所以你可以想象这些输入和输出也会有所不同。
So you could imagine these inputs and outputs being different as well.

5909
09:18:33,998 --> 09:18:37,604
事实证明，在某些问题中，我们不会只有两个输入。
And it turns out that in some problems, we're not just going to have two inputs.

5910
09:18:38,125 --> 09:18:46,848
而这些神经网络的优点是，我们可以将多个单元组合在一起，只需增加更多单元到其中，就能让我们的网络变得更复杂。
And the nice thing about these neural networks is that we can compose multiple units together, make our networks more complex just by adding more units into

5911
09:18:47,150 --> 09:18:48,388
这个特定的神经网络。
this particular neural network.

5912
09:18:48,750 --> 09:18:57,408
我们之前看的网络有两个输入和一个输出，但我们也可以很轻松地增加到三个输入，或者更多输入，
So the network we've been looking at has two inputs and one output, but we could just as easily say, let's go ahead and have three inputs in there, or have even more inputs,

5913
09:18:57,568 --> 09:19:07,044
我们可以随意决定问题中有多少个输入，它们都会用来计算我们想要了解的某种输出值。
where we could arbitrarily decide however many inputs there are to our problem, all going to be calculating some sort of output that we care about figuring out the value of.

5914
09:19:07,758 --> 09:19:10,180
那么，计算这些输出时的数学原理是什么呢？
How then does the math work for figuring out that output?

5915
09:19:10,510 --> 09:19:12,131
嗯，它的工作原理非常相似。
Well, it's going to work in a very similar way.

5916
09:19:12,494 --> 09:19:19,684
在两个输入的情况下，我们有由这些边表示的两个权重，我们将权重与数值相乘，并加上这个偏置项。
In the case of two inputs, we had two weights indicated by these edges, and we multiplied the weights by the numbers, adding this bias term.

5917
09:19:20,302 --> 09:19:27,332
在其他情况下也是同样的操作。如果我有三个输入，你可以想象将这三个输入中的每一个都乘以对应的权重。
And we'll do the same thing in the other cases as well. If I have three inputs, you'll imagine multiplying each of these three inputs by each of these weights.

5918
09:19:27,888 --> 09:19:30,848
如果我换成五个输入，我们也会做同样的事情。
if I had five inputs instead, we're going to do the same thing.

5919
09:19:31,150 --> 09:19:41,604
这里我是在说从 1 到 5 求和，即 $x_i$ 乘以权重 $w_i$。也就是说，取这五个输入变量中的每一个，乘以它们对应的权重，然后加上偏置。
Here I'm saying sum up from one to five, x i multiplied by weight i. So take each of the five input variables, multiply them by their corresponding weight, and then add the bias to that.

5920
09:19:41,934 --> 09:19:45,808
例如，这就是一个有五个输入进入这个神经网络的情况。
So this would be a case where there are five inputs into this neural network, for example.

5921
09:19:45,998 --> 09:19:53,408
但也可以更多，我们可以根据需要增加任何数量的节点，每次我们只需将所有这些输入变量相加，
But there could be more, arbitrarily many nodes that we want inside of this neural network, where each time we're just going to sum up all of those input variables,

5922
09:19:53,486 --> 09:19:57,156
乘以它们的权重，然后在最后加上偏置项。
multiplied by their weight, and then add the bias term at the very end.

5923
09:19:57,710 --> 09:20:04,196
因此，这允许我们通过扩大神经网络的规模来表示具有更多输入的各种问题。
And so this allows us to be able to represent problems that have even more inputs just by growing the size of our neural network.

5924
09:20:05,294 --> 09:20:10,756
现在，我们可能会提出的下一个问题是关于如何训练这些神经网络的问题。
Now, the next question we might ask is a question about how it is that we train these neural networks.

5925
09:20:10,848 --> 09:20:17,408
在 OR 函数和 AND 函数的情况下，它们足够简单，我可以直接告诉你权重应该是多少，
In the case of the OR function and the AND function, they were simple enough functions that I could just tell you, like here are what the weights should be,

5926
09:20:17,488 --> 09:20:22,980
而你可能也能自己推论出为了计算所需的输出，权重应该设成什么样。
and you could probably reason through it yourself what the weights should be in order to calculate the output that you want.

5927
09:20:23,278 --> 09:20:30,404
但通常情况下，对于像预测销售额或预测是否会下雨这样的函数，要弄清楚这些函数要复杂得多。
But in general, with functions like predicting sales or predicting whether or not it's going to rain, these are much trickier functions to be able to figure out.

5928
09:20:30,608 --> 09:20:37,220
我们希望计算机有一种机制来计算权重应该是多少，以及如何设置这些权重，
We would like the computer to have some mechanism of calculating what it is that the weights should be, how it is to set the weights,

5929
09:20:37,646 --> 09:20:42,852
从而让我们的神经网络能够准确地模拟我们想要估算的那个函数。
so that our neural network is able to accurately model the function that we care about trying to estimate.

5930
09:20:43,534 --> 09:20:49,092
事实证明，实现这一点的策略是受到微积分领域的启发，一种被称为梯度下降的技术。
And it turns out that the strategy for doing this, inspired by the domain of calculus, is a technique called gradient descent.

5931
09:20:49,582 --> 09:20:55,492
所谓梯度下降，就是训练神经网络时用于最小化损失的一种算法。
And what gradient descent is, it is an algorithm for minimizing loss when you're training a neural network.

5932
09:20:55,918 --> 09:21:03,248
回想一下，损失是指我们的假设函数表现有多差，我们可以定义特定的损失函数，
And recall that loss refers to how bad our hypothesis function happens to be, that we can define certain loss functions,

5933
09:21:03,502 --> 09:21:11,248
我们上次看了一些损失函数的例子，它们为任何特定的假设给出一个数值，说明它对数据的建模效果有多差。
and we saw some examples of loss functions last time that just give us a number for any particular hypothesis saying how poorly does it model the data?

5934
09:21:11,408 --> 09:21:18,468
它有多少个样本预测错误，或者与我们可能定义的其他假设函数相比，它的表现是更好还是更差。
How many examples does it get wrong, how much how are they worse or less bad as compared to other hypothesis functions that we might define.

5935
09:21:19,054 --> 09:21:22,244
而这个损失函数只是一个数学函数。
And this loss function is just a mathematical function.

5936
09:21:22,606 --> 09:21:29,156
当你有一个数学函数时，在微积分中，你可以计算被称为梯度的东西，你可以把它想象成斜率。
And when you have a mathematical function, in calculus, what you could do is calculate something known as the gradient, which you can think of as like a slope.

5937
09:21:29,328 --> 09:21:32,516
它是损失函数在任何特定点的变化方向。
It's the direction the loss function is moving at any particular point.

5938
09:21:32,942 --> 09:21:40,324
它告诉我们为了最小化损失量，我们应该朝哪个方向调整这些权重。
And what it's going to tell us is in which direction should we be moving these weights in order to minimize the amount of loss.

5939
09:21:41,070 --> 09:21:47,364
所以，总的来说，我们不会深入探讨其中的微积分细节，但梯度下降的高层逻辑大致如下。
And so, generally speaking, we won't get into the calculus of it, but the high-level idea for gradient descent is going to look something like this.

5940
09:21:47,822 --> 09:21:52,612
如果我们想训练一个神经网络，我们将从随机选择权重开始。
If we want to train a neural network, we'll go ahead and start just by choosing the weights randomly.

5941
09:21:52,848 --> 09:21:55,524
为神经网络中的所有权重随机分配数值。
Just pick random weights for all of the weights in the neural network.

5942
09:21:56,142 --> 09:22:02,596
然后，我们将利用可获取的输入数据来训练网络，从而确定权重的实际数值。
And then we'll use the input data that we have access to in order to train the network, in order to figure out what the weights should actually be.

5943
09:22:02,894 --> 09:22:04,868
所以我们要不断重复这个过程。
So we'll repeat this process again and again.

5944
09:22:05,358 --> 09:22:09,168
第一步是根据所有数据点来计算梯度。
The first step is we're going to calculate the gradient based on all of the data points.

5945
09:22:09,294 --> 09:22:15,108
也就是说，我们会查看所有数据，并找出在当前权重设置下，我们所在位置的梯度是多少。
So we'll look at all the data and figure out what the gradient is at the place where we currently are for the current setting of the weights,

5946
09:22:15,568 --> 09:22:23,716
这意味着为了减少总损失量、让我们的解决方案变得更好，我们应该朝哪个方向移动权重。
which means in which direction should we move the weights in order to minimize the total amount of loss in order to make our solution better.

5947
09:22:24,430 --> 09:22:32,228
一旦计算出那个梯度，即在损失函数中该往哪个方向移动，我们就可以根据梯度来更新这些权重了。
And once we've calculated that gradient, which direction we should move in the loss function, well then we can just update those weights according to the gradient,

5948
09:22:32,782 --> 09:22:37,568
朝着那个方向迈出一小步，试图让我们的解决方案稍微变好一点。
take a small step in the direction of those weights in order to try to make our solution a little bit better.

5949
09:22:37,806 --> 09:22:42,660
而我们迈出的这一步的大小是可变的，在训练特定的神经网络时你可以进行选择。
And the size of the step that we take, that's going to vary, and you can choose that when you're training a particular neural network.

5950
09:22:43,022 --> 09:22:49,732
简而言之，思路就是获取所有数据点，根据这些数据点判断权重应该往哪个方向移动。
But in short, the idea is going to be take all the data points, figure out based on those data points in what direction the weights should move,

5951
09:22:49,966 --> 09:22:52,848
然后让权重朝那个方向迈一小步。
and then move the weights one small step in that direction.

5952
09:22:53,134 --> 09:22:59,428
如果你不断重复这个过程，基于所有数据点每次微调一点权重，最终，
And if you repeat that process over and over again, adjusting the weights a little bit at a time based on all the data points, eventually,

5953
09:22:59,726 --> 09:23:04,048
你应该能得到一个相当不错的解来解决这类问题。
you should end up with a pretty good solution to trying to solve this sort of problem.

5954
09:23:04,270 --> 09:23:05,892
至少这是我们希望看到的结果。
At least that's what we would hope to happen.

5955
09:23:06,734 --> 09:23:14,448
现在，当你分析这个算法时，一个很好的问题是：计算过程中最耗时的部分是什么？
Now, as you look at this algorithm, a good question to ask anytime you're analyzing an algorithm is what is going to be the expensive part of doing the calculation?

5956
09:23:14,638 --> 09:23:19,236
哪些步骤需要投入大量工作去推算，哪些计算成本很高。
What's going to take a lot of work to try to figure out, what is going to be expensive to calculate.

5957
09:23:19,630 --> 09:23:26,128
特别是在梯度下降的情况下，真正昂贵的部分就是这里的“所有数据点”这一部分。
And in particular, in the case of gradient descent, the really expensive part is this all data points part right here.

5958
09:23:26,288 --> 09:23:34,404
因为必须提取所有数据点，并利用这些数据点来确定在当前权重设置下的梯度。
Having to take all of the data points and using all of those data points, figure out what the gradient is at this particular setting of all of the weights.

5959
09:23:34,688 --> 09:23:41,728
因为很有可能，在一个处理大量数据的庞大机器学习问题中，你需要计算大量的点。
Because odds are, in a big machine learning problem where you're trying to solve a big problem with a lot of data, you have a lot of data points in order to calculate.

5960
09:23:41,934 --> 09:23:47,408
而基于所有这些数据点来确定梯度会非常耗时，而且你还得反复执行很多次。
And figuring out the gradient based on all of those data points is going to be expensive, and you'll have to do it many times.

5961
09:23:47,648 --> 09:23:52,996
你可能会不断重复这个过程，遍历所有数据点，迈出一小步，
You'll likely repeat this process again and again and again, going through all the data points, taking one small step

5962
09:23:53,328 --> 09:23:58,436
在试图找出这些权重的最优设置时，如此反复操作。
over and over as you try and figure out what the optimal setting of those weights happens to be.

5963
09:23:59,246 --> 09:24:09,508
事实证明，我们理想情况下希望能够更快地训练神经网络，更快地收敛到某种能很好解决问题的方案。
It turns out that we would ideally like to be able to train our neural networks faster, to be able to more quickly converge to some sort of solution that is going to be a good solution to the problem.

5964
09:24:09,998 --> 09:24:14,852
在这种情况下，除了同时查看所有数据点的标准梯度下降，还有其他替代方案。
So in that case, there are alternatives to just standard gradient descent, which looks at all of the data points at once.

5965
09:24:15,214 --> 09:24:23,940
我们可以采用类似随机梯度下降的方法，它每次只随机选择一个数据点来计算梯度，
We can employ a method like stochastic gradient descent, which will randomly just choose one data point at a time to calculate the gradient based on,

5966
09:24:24,128 --> 09:24:26,628
而不是基于所有的数据点来计算。
instead of calculating it based on all of the data points.

5967
09:24:27,118 --> 09:24:35,716
这里的思路是：我们有一组权重设置，选出一个数据点，并根据这一个数据点来判断所有权重应该往哪个方向移动。
So the idea there is that we have some setting of the weights, we pick a data point, and based on that one data point, we figure out in which direction should we move all of the weights,

5968
09:24:35,888 --> 09:24:41,408
然后让权重朝那个微小的方向移动，接着再取下一个数据点重复同样的操作，不断循环这个过程。
and move the weights in that small direction, then take another data point and do that again, and repeat this process again and again.

5969
09:24:41,568 --> 09:24:51,076
也许会多次查看每一个数据点，但每次只用一个数据点来计算梯度，从而确定我们该往哪个方向走。
maybe looking at each of the data points multiple times, but each time only using one data point to calculate the gradient, to calculate which direction we should move in.

5970
09:24:51,662 --> 09:24:59,332
现在，仅使用一个数据点而不是所有数据点，可能会让我们对真实梯度的估计不够准确。
Now, just using one data point instead of all of the data points probably gives us a less accurate estimate of what the gradient actually is.

5971
09:24:59,758 --> 09:25:06,980
但从好的方面来说，基于一个数据点来计算梯度会快得多，
But on the plus side, it's going to be much faster to be able to calculate, that we can much more quickly calculate what the gradient is based on one data point

5972
09:25:07,182 --> 09:25:12,836
而不是基于所有数据点去计算，从而避免重复进行大量的计算工作。
instead of calculating based on all of the data points and having to do all of that computational work again and again.

5973
09:25:13,422 --> 09:25:17,508
所以，在查看所有数据点和只看一个数据点之间，存在权衡。
