09:33:30,000 --> 09:33:35,440
我们可以预测出一条线，将红点和蓝点线性分开。
we can predict a line that separates linearly the red points from the blue points.

6050
09:33:36,270 --> 09:33:43,684
但一个进行二分类的单一单元，也就是所谓的感知机，无法处理这种情况，
But a single unit that is making a binary classification, otherwise known as a perceptron, can't deal with a situation like this,

6051
09:33:44,494 --> 09:33:52,324
即我们之前见过的这种情况，其中没有一条直线能直接穿过数据，将红点与蓝点分开。
where we've seen this type of situation before, where there is no straight line that just goes straight through the data that will divide the red points away from the blue points.

6052
09:33:52,686 --> 09:33:54,916
这是一个更复杂的决策边界。
It's a more complex decision boundary.

6053
09:33:55,040 --> 09:34:02,308
决策边界在某种程度上需要涵盖这个圆圈内部的内容，而并没有任何线条能让我们处理这种情况。
The decision boundary somehow needs to capture the things inside of this circle, and there isn't really a line that will allow us to deal with that.

6054
09:34:03,118 --> 09:34:08,516
这就是感知机的局限性，这些根据输入做出二元决策的单元，
So this is the limitation of the perceptron, these units that just make these binary decisions based on their inputs,

6055
09:34:08,814 --> 09:34:15,120
单个感知机只能学习线性可分的决策边界。
that a single perceptron is only capable of learning a linearly separable decision boundary.

6056
09:34:15,280 --> 09:34:17,200
它能做的仅仅是定义一条线。
All it can do is define a line.

6057
09:34:17,454 --> 09:34:26,244
当然，它可以根据我们距离那个决策边界的远近来给出概率，但它只能基于线性决策边界做出判断。
And sure it can give us probabilities based on how close to that decision boundary we are, but it can only really decide based on a linear decision boundary.

6058
09:34:26,734 --> 09:34:34,800
因此，这似乎无法很好地泛用到涉及真实世界数据的场景中，因为现实世界的数据往往不是线性可分的。
And so this doesn't seem like it's going to generalize well to situations where real world data is involved, because real world data often isn't linearly separable.

6059
09:34:34,880 --> 09:34:40,420
通常并不是只要画一条线就能把数据分成多个组。
It often isn't the case that we can just draw a line through the data and be able to divide it up into multiple groups.

6060
09:34:41,262 --> 09:34:42,852
那么，解决这个问题的方法是什么呢？
So what then is the solution to this?

6061
09:34:43,310 --> 09:34:47,520
好的，目前提出的方案是多层神经网络的概念。
Well, what was proposed was the idea of a multi-layer neural network.

6062
09:34:47,630 --> 09:34:54,468
到目前为止，我们看到的神经网络都有一组输入和一组输出，输入与这些输出相连。
That so far, all of the neural networks we've seen have had a set of inputs and a set of outputs, and the inputs are connected to those outputs.

6063
09:34:55,438 --> 09:35:06,000
但在多层神经网络中，这是一个仍有输入层、有输出层，但在中间增加了一个或多个隐藏层的人工神经网络。
But in a multi-layer neural network, this is going to be an artificial neural network that has an input layer still, it has an output layer, but also has one or more hidden layers in between.

6064
09:35:06,240 --> 09:35:11,780
还有其他由人工神经元或单元组成的层，它们也会计算出自己的值。
Other layers of artificial neurons or units that are going to calculate their own values as well.

6065
09:35:12,430 --> 09:35:20,228
所以，与其使用这种具有三个输入和一个输出的神经网络，不如想象在中间加入一个隐藏层，
So instead of a neural network that looks like this, with three inputs and one output, you might imagine in the middle here injecting a hidden layer,

6066
09:35:20,878 --> 09:35:21,280
就像这样。
something like this.

6067
09:35:21,454 --> 09:35:23,280
这是一个包含四个节点的隐藏层。
This is a hidden layer that has four nodes.

6068
09:35:23,600 --> 09:35:28,932
你可以选择进入隐藏层的节点或单元的数量。你也可以拥有多个隐藏层。
You could choose how many nodes or units end up going into the hidden layer. you can have multiple hidden layers as well.

6069
09:35:29,326 --> 09:35:33,284
这样一来，每个输入就不再直接连接到输出。
And so now each of these inputs isn't directly connected to the output.

6070
09:35:33,646 --> 09:35:35,844
每个输入都连接到这个隐藏层。
Each of the inputs is connected to this hidden layer.

6071
09:35:36,398 --> 09:35:40,196
然后隐藏层中的所有节点，这些都会连接到那一个输出上。
And then all of the nodes in the hidden layer, those are connected to the one output.

6072
09:35:40,974 --> 09:35:46,276
所以这是我们迈向计算更复杂函数的一个步骤。
And so this is just another step that we can take towards calculating more complex functions.

6073
09:35:46,480 --> 09:35:54,596
每一个隐藏单元都会根据所有输入的线性组合来计算它的输出值，也就是所谓的激活值。
Each of these hidden units will calculate its output value, otherwise known as its activation, based on a linear combination of all the inputs.

6074
09:35:55,278 --> 09:36:00,480
一旦我们得到了这些节点的所有值（而不是仅仅作为输出），我们就重复同样的操作。
And once we have values for all of these nodes, as opposed to this just being the output, we do the same thing again.

6075
09:36:00,720 --> 09:36:07,460
通过将这些单元的每个值与其对应的权重相乘，来计算这个节点的输出。
Calculate the output for this node based on multiplying each of the values for these units by their weights as well.

6076
09:36:07,982 --> 09:36:13,892
所以实际上，它的工作原理是：我们从输入开始，它们与权重相乘以计算隐藏节点的数值，
So in effect, the way this works is that we start with inputs, they get multiplied by weights in order to calculate values for the hidden nodes,

6077
09:36:14,094 --> 09:36:18,980
然后这些值再与权重相乘，从而确定最终的输出。
those get multiplied by weights in order to figure out what the ultimate output is going to be.

6078
09:36:19,758 --> 09:36:25,252
这种分层结构的优势在于它赋予了我们建模更复杂函数的能力。
And the advantage of layering things like this is it gives us an ability to model more complex functions.

6079
09:36:25,614 --> 09:36:35,620
这意味着不再仅仅有一个将红点与蓝点分开的单一决策边界，这些隐藏节点中的每一个都可以学习到不同的决策边界，
That instead of just having a single decision boundary, a single line dividing the red points from the blue points, each of these hidden nodes can learn a different decision boundary,

6080
09:36:35,918 --> 09:36:40,644
我们可以结合这些决策边界来确定最终的输出。
and we can combine those decision boundaries to figure out what the ultimate output is going to be.

6081
09:36:40,974 --> 09:36:50,084
当我们开始想象更复杂的情况时，你可以想象这些节点中的每一个都在学习所有输入中的某些有用属性或特征，
And as we begin to imagine more complex situations, you could imagine each of these nodes learning some useful property or learning some useful feature of all of the inputs,

6082
09:36:50,510 --> 09:36:55,652
而我们通过某种方式学习如何将这些特征结合起来，从而获得我们真正想要的输出。
and us somehow learning how to combine those features together in order to get the output that we actually want.

6083
09:36:56,654 --> 09:37:03,908
现在，当我们开始审视这个模型时，自然会产生一个问题：我们如何训练一个包含隐藏层的神经网络？
Now, the natural question when we begin to look at this now is to ask the question of how do we train a neural network that has hidden layers inside of it?

6084
09:37:04,398 --> 09:37:12,580
这最初是一个有点棘手的问题，因为给定的输入数据中，我们拥有所有输入的数值，
And this turns out to initially be a bit of a tricky question, because the input data that we are given is we are given values for all of the inputs,

6085
09:37:13,070 --> 09:37:17,604
并且我们知道输出应该是多少，比如属于哪个类别。
and we're given what the value of the output should be, what the category is, for example.

6086
09:37:18,126 --> 09:37:22,720
但输入数据并没有告诉我们这些节点的所有值应该是多少。
But the input data doesn't tell us what the values for all of these nodes should be.

6087
09:37:22,926 --> 09:37:29,476
所以我们不知道每个节点到底偏离了多少，因为我们只获得了输入和输出的数据。
So we don't know how far off each of these nodes actually is, because we're only given data for the inputs and the outputs.

6088
09:37:29,760 --> 09:37:38,884
之所以称之为隐藏层，是因为提供给我们的数据并没有告诉我们这些中间节点的值究竟应该是多少。
The reason this is called a hidden layer is because the data that is made available to us doesn't tell us what the values for all of these intermediate nodes should actually be.

6089
09:37:39,694 --> 09:37:47,428
因此人们想出的策略是：如果你知道输出节点上的误差或损失是多少，
And so the strategy people came up with was to say that if you know what the error or the loss is on the output node,

6090
09:37:48,078 --> 09:37:58,144
那么根据这些权重的大小，如果其中一个权重比另一个高，你就可以估算出这个节点的误差有多少。
well, then, based on what these weights are. if one of these weights is higher than another, you can calculate an estimate for how much the error from this node was

6091
09:37:58,464 --> 09:38:04,544
由于隐藏节点、或者说隐藏层中的这部分，基于这些权重的数值。
due to this part of the hidden node, or this part of the hidden layer, or this part of the hidden layer, based on the values of these weights.

6092
09:38:04,704 --> 09:38:15,344
实际上，这意味着根据输出层的误差，我可以进行反向传播，并估算出隐藏层中每个节点的误差。
In effect, saying that based on the error from the output, I can backpropagate the error and figure out an estimate for what the error is for each of these nodes in the hidden layer as well.

6093
09:38:15,726 --> 09:38:21,636
这里还有一些微积分内容我们不会深入探讨，但这种算法被称为“反向传播”。
And there's some more calculus here that we won't get into the details of, but the idea of this algorithm is known as backpropagation.

6094
09:38:21,774 --> 09:38:25,668
它是用于训练具有多个不同隐藏层的神经网络的算法。
It's an algorithm for training a neural network with multiple different hidden layers.

6095
09:38:26,158 --> 09:38:34,532
关于这个算法的思路，也就是它的伪代码是：如果我们想用反向传播配合梯度下降，我们将像之前一样，从随机选择的权重开始。
And the idea for this, the pseudocode for it, will again be if we want to run gradient descent with backpropagation, we'll start with a random choice of weights, as we did before.

6096
09:38:35,246 --> 09:38:38,020
然后，我们将不断重复训练过程。
And now we'll go ahead and repeat the training process again and again.

6097
09:38:38,670 --> 09:38:43,824
但我们每次要做的是先计算输出层的误差。
But what we're going to do each time is now we're going to calculate the error for the output layer first.

6098
09:38:43,984 --> 09:38:48,932
我们知道输出结果以及它应该是多少，我们也知道计算出的结果，所以我们可以算出其中的误差。
We know the output and what it should be, and we know what we calculated, so we can figure out what the error there is.

6099
09:38:49,678 --> 09:38:57,860
然后我们将对每一层重复此过程：从输出层开始，向隐藏层回溯，如果有多层隐藏层，就继续往回走，
But then we're going to repeat for every layer, starting with the output layer, moving back into the hidden layer, then the hidden layer before that, if there are multiple hidden layers,

6100
09:38:58,224 --> 09:39:04,864
一直退回到第一个隐藏层。假设有多个隐藏层，我们将把误差向后传播一层。
going back all the way to the very first hidden layer, assuming there are multiple, we're going to propagate the error back one layer.

6101
09:39:05,024 --> 09:39:11,140
无论输出端的误差是多少，我们都会根据这些权重的数值，计算出前一层对应的误差应该是多少。
Whatever the error was from the output, figure out what the error should be a layer before that, based on what the values of those weights are.

6102
09:39:11,758 --> 09:39:13,828
然后我们就可以更新这些权重了。
And then we can update those weights.

6103
09:39:14,830 --> 09:39:18,544
所以从图形上来说，你可以这样理解：我们首先从输出开始。
So graphically, the way you might think about this is that we first start with the output.

6104
09:39:18,704 --> 09:39:25,124
我们知道输出应该是多少，也知道计算出的结果，基于此，我们可以确定该如何更新这些权重。
We know what the output should be, we know what output we calculated, and based on that, we can figure out, all right, how do we need to update those weights?

6105
09:39:25,424 --> 09:39:31,108
通过将误差反向传播到这些节点，并利用这些信息，我们可以推算出应该如何更新这些权重。
Backpropagating the error to these nodes, and using that, we can figure out how we should update these weights.

6106
09:39:31,534 --> 09:39:39,264
你可以想象，如果有多层，我们可以不断重复这个过程，来确定所有这些权重该如何更新。
And you might imagine if there are multiple layers, we could repeat this process again and again to begin to figure out how all of these weights should be updated.

6107
09:39:39,566 --> 09:39:44,164
而这种反向传播算法正是让神经网络成为可能的关键算法。
And this back propagation algorithm is really the key algorithm that makes neural networks possible.

6108
09:39:44,366 --> 09:39:52,464
它使得我们能够处理这些多层结构，并根据权重的数值来训练这些结构。
It makes it possible to take these multi-level structures and be able to train those structures depending on what the values of these weights are.

6109
09:39:52,544 --> 09:40:00,516
目的是找出如何更新这些权重，从而构建出一个能够最小化总损失的函数。
in order to figure out how it is that we should go about updating those weights in order to create some function that is able to minimize the total amount of loss,

6110
09:40:00,624 --> 09:40:06,788
目的是找到一组良好的权重设置，能够将输入转换为我们预期的输出。
to figure out some good setting of the weights that will take the inputs and translate it into the output that we expect.

6111
09:40:07,566 --> 09:40:15,492
正如我们所说，这不仅适用于单一隐藏层，你还可以想象多个隐藏层，在每个隐藏层中，我们可以定义任意数量的节点。
And this works, as we said, not just for a single hidden layer, but you can imagine multiple hidden layers, where each hidden layer we just define however many nodes we want,

6112
09:40:15,726 --> 09:40:25,220
其中每一层的节点都可以连接到下一层的节点，从而构建出越来越复杂的网络，能够模拟越来越复杂类型的函数。
where each of the nodes in one layer we can connect to the nodes in the next layer, defining more and more complex networks that are able to model more and more complex types of functions.

6113
09:40:26,190 --> 09:40:31,364
因此，这种类型的网络我们称之为“深度神经网络”，它是庞大家族的一部分
And so this type of network is what we might call a deep neural network, part of a larger family

6114
09:40:32,014 --> 09:40:34,464
即如果你听过这个词，它属于“深度学习”算法系列。
of deep learning algorithms, if you've ever heard that term.

6115
09:40:34,624 --> 09:40:44,944
所有深度学习的核心就是利用多层结构来预测和建模输入中更高层次的特征，从而确定输出应该是多少。
And all deep learning is about is it's using multiple layers to be able to predict and be able to model higher-level features inside of the input, to be able to figure out what the output should be.

6116
09:40:45,262 --> 09:40:52,784
所以，深度神经网络就是一个拥有多个隐藏层的神经网络，我们从输入开始，计算这一层的数值，然后是这一层，
And so a deep neural network is just a neural network that has multiple of these hidden layers, where we start at the input, calculate values for this layer, then this layer,

6117
09:40:52,864 --> 09:40:55,424
接着是这一层，最后得到输出。
then this layer, and then ultimately get an output.

6118
09:40:55,598 --> 09:41:03,620
这让我们能够建模更复杂的函数类型，因为每一层都可以计算出略有不同的内容，
And this allows us to be able to model more and more sophisticated types of functions, that each of these layers can calculate something a little bit different,

6119
09:41:03,854 --> 09:41:07,556
然后我们可以整合这些信息来确定最终的输出。
and we can combine that information to figure out what the output should be.

6120
09:41:08,494 --> 09:41:18,468
当然，正如任何机器学习的情况一样，当我们开始让模型变得越来越复杂，去建模越来越复杂的函数时，我们面临的风险就是诸如“过拟合”之类的风险。
Of course, as with any situation of machine learning, as we begin to make our models more and more complex, to model more and more complex functions, the risk we run is something like overfitting.

6121
09:41:18,894 --> 09:41:27,492
上次我们讨论过在训练模型以学习某种决策边界时的过拟合问题，
And we talked about overfitting last time in the context of overfitting based on when we were training our models to be able to learn some sort of decision boundary,

6122
09:41:27,694 --> 09:41:35,780
过拟合发生在模型过于贴合训练数据时，导致它无法很好地泛化到其他情况。
where overfitting happens when we fit too closely to the training data, and as a result, we don't generalize well to other situations as well.

6123
09:41:36,110 --> 09:41:44,384
在拥有许多不同节点的复杂神经网络中，我们面临的风险之一是可能会基于输入数据而产生过拟合。
And one of the risks we run with a far more complex neural network that has many, many different nodes, is that we might overfit based on the input data.

6124
09:41:44,464 --> 09:41:52,772
我们可能会过度依赖某些节点来仅根据输入数据进行计算，这导致我们无法很好地泛化到输出结果。
We might grow over-reliant on certain nodes to calculate things just purely based on the input data that doesn't allow us to generalize very well to the output.

6125
09:41:53,486 --> 09:41:56,292
处理过拟合问题有很多种策略。
And there are a number of strategies for dealing with overfitting.

6126
09:41:56,462 --> 09:42:00,676
但在神经网络领域，最流行的一种技术被称为“丢弃法”。
But one of the most popular in the context of neural networks is a technique known as dropout.

6127
09:42:01,102 --> 09:42:10,756
丢弃法的做法是在训练神经网络时，暂时移除一些单元，也就是从网络中临时去掉这些人工神经元，
And what dropout does is that when we're training the neural network, what we'll do in dropout is temporarily remove units, temporarily remove these artificial neurons from our network

6128
09:42:11,118 --> 09:42:12,036
这些是随机选择的。
chosen at random.

6129
09:42:12,590 --> 09:42:16,144
这里的目标就是防止过度依赖某些特定的单元。
And the goal here is to prevent over-reliance on certain units.

6130
09:42:16,270 --> 09:42:24,544
通常过拟合的现象是，我们开始过度依赖神经网络中的某些特定单元来解释输入数据。
So what generally happens in overfitting is that we begin to over rely on certain units inside the neural network to be able to tell us how to interpret the input data.

6131
09:42:24,846 --> 09:42:33,664
丢弃法会随机移除一些这些单元，从而降低过度依赖某些单元的概率，让我们的神经网络更健壮，
What dropout will do is randomly remove some of these units in order to reduce the chance that we over rely on certain units to make our neural network more robust,

6132
09:42:33,744 --> 09:42:38,500
即使在完全去掉某些特定神经元的情况下也能处理各种情况。
to be able to handle the situations even when we just drop out particular neurons entirely.

6133
09:42:39,278 --> 09:42:45,668
这种方法的运作方式是：我们有一个这样的网络，在训练过程中，当我们第一次尝试更新权重时，
So the way that might work is we have a network like this, and as we're training it, when we go about trying to update the weights the first time,

6134
09:42:45,934 --> 09:42:49,284
我们会随机选择一定比例的节点从网络中“丢弃”。
we'll just randomly pick some percentage of the nodes to drop out of the network.

6135
09:42:49,582 --> 09:42:51,216
就像这些节点根本不存在一样。
It's as if those nodes aren't there at all.

6136
09:42:51,406 --> 09:42:55,524
就像与这些节点相关的权重根本不存在一样，我们按这种方式来训练它。
It's as if the weights associated with those nodes aren't there at all, and we'll train it this way.

6137
09:42:56,078 --> 09:42:59,748
下一次更新权重时，我们会选择另一组并按这种方式继续训练。
Then the next time we update the weights, we'll pick a different set and just go ahead and train that way.

6138
09:42:59,918 --> 09:43:03,908
然后再次随机选择，并与其他被丢弃的节点一起进行训练。
And then again, randomly choose and train with other nodes that have been dropped out as well.

6139
09:43:04,558 --> 09:43:10,372
这样做的目的是，在训练过程中，如果你通过丢弃神经网络中随机的节点来训练，
