而且我们该如何训练计算机也能识别出来呢？
And how could we train a computer to be able to figure that out as well?

7056
11:06:29,070 --> 11:06:36,320
嗯，你可能会注意到一些特定的关键词，这些词往往意味着某种正面或负面的含义。
Well, you might have clued your eye in on particular key words, where those particular words tend to mean something positive or negative.

7057
11:06:36,526 --> 11:06:42,596
所以你可能已经发现像 loved、fun 和 best 这些词往往与正面的信息相关联。
So you might have identified words like loved and fun and best tend to be associated with positive messages.

7058
11:06:42,862 --> 11:06:47,428
而像 broke、cheap 和 flimsy 这些词往往与负面的信息相关联。
And words like broke and cheap and flimsy tend to be associated with negative messages.

7059
11:06:48,046 --> 11:06:54,948
所以，如果我们能让计算机学会哪些词倾向于与正面或负面信息相关联的话，
So if only we could train a computer to be able to learn what words tend to be associated with positive versus negative messages,

7060
11:06:55,120 --> 11:06:59,332
那么也许我们就能训练计算机来做这种情感分析了。
then maybe we could train a computer to do this kind of sentiment analysis as well.

7061
11:07:00,110 --> 11:07:01,476
所以我们要做的就是这件事情。
So we're going to try to do just that.

7062
11:07:01,742 --> 11:07:09,316
我们将使用一种被称为词袋模型（词袋模型）的模型，这个模型将文本表示为仅仅是一个无序的词语集合。
We're going to use a model known as the bag of words model, which is a model that represents text as just an unordered collection of words.

7063
11:07:09,742 --> 11:07:15,396
为了这个模型的目的，我们不需要考虑词语的序列和顺序，也就是哪个词在前，哪个在第二或第三位。
For the purpose of this model, we're not going to worry about the sequence and the ordering of the words, which word came first, second or third.

7064
11:07:15,600 --> 11:07:21,360
我们只是把文本当作一个无序的词语集合，这会丢失一些信息，对吧？
We're just going to treat the text as a collection of words in no particular order, and we're losing information there, right?

7065
11:07:21,440 --> 11:07:24,480
词语的顺序很重要，我们稍后会再讨论一下。
The order of words is important, and we'll come back to that a little bit later.

7066
11:07:24,782 --> 11:07:31,492
但目前为了简化模型，把文本仅仅看作一个无序的词语集合会对我们非常有帮助。
But for now to simplify our model, it'll help us tremendously just to think about text as some unordered collection of words.

7067
11:07:32,302 --> 11:07:37,796
特别是，我们将使用词袋模型来构建一个被称为朴素贝叶斯分类器（朴素贝叶斯分类器）的东西。
And in particular, we're going to use the bag of words model to build something known as a naive Bayes classifier.

7068
11:07:38,286 --> 11:07:40,000
那么，什么是朴素贝叶斯分类器？
So, what is a naive Bayes classifier?

7069
11:07:40,240 --> 11:07:42,720
嗯，它是一个能让我们对文本进行分类的工具。
Well, it's a tool that's going to allow us to classify text.

7070
11:07:43,214 --> 11:07:46,848
它是基于 Bayes' rule 的，也就是你可能在讨论概率时记得过的那个规则。
Based on Bayes' rule, again, which you might remember from when we talked about probability.

7071
11:07:47,182 --> 11:07:56,324
Bayes' rule 说，给定 A 时 B 的概率等于 B 的概率乘以 A 给定 B 的概率，
Bayes' rule says that the probability of B given A is equal to the probability of A given B multiplied by the probability of B

7072
11:07:56,558 --> 11:07:58,724
再除以 A 的概率。
divided by the probability of A.

7073
11:07:59,406 --> 11:08:02,788
那么我们打算如何利用这个规则来分析文本呢？
So how are we going to use this rule to be able to analyze text?

7074
11:08:03,534 --> 11:08:04,688
嗯，我们感兴趣的是什么？
Well, what are we interested in?

7075
11:08:04,878 --> 11:08:11,236
我们感兴趣的是一条信息具有正面情感的概率，以及它具有负面情感的概率，
We're interested in the probability that a message has a positive sentiment and the probability that a message has a negative sentiment,

7076
11:08:11,502 --> 11:08:17,668
为了简化起见，我在这里用这些表情符号来代表：笑脸和哭脸，分别代表正向和负向的情感。
which I'm here for simplicity going to represent just with these emoji, happy face and frown face, as positive and negative sentiment.

7077
11:08:18,446 --> 11:08:27,204
所以如果我有一条评论，比如“我的孙子很喜欢它”，那么我感兴趣的不仅仅是这条信息具有正面情感的概率，
And so if I had a review, something like my grandson loved it, then what I'm interested in is not just the probability that a message has positive sentiment,

7078
11:08:27,630 --> 11:08:34,340
而是在已知这条消息是“我的孙子很喜欢它”的情况下，该消息具有正面情感的条件概率。
but the conditional probability that a message has positive sentiment given that this is the message, my grandson loved it.

7079
11:08:35,118 --> 11:08:42,276
但我该如何计算这个值呢？也就是在给定评论是这一串词语时，信息为正面的概率？
But how do I go about calculating this value, the probability that the message is positive, given that the review is this sequence of words?

7080
11:08:42,830 --> 11:08:44,868
嗯，这就是词袋模型派上用武之地的地方。
Well, here's where the bag of words model comes in.

7081
11:08:45,294 --> 11:08:52,548
与其把这条评论看作按顺序排列的词语序列，不如把它看作一个无序的词汇集合。
Rather than treat this review as a string of a sequence of words in order, we're just going to treat it as an unordered collection of words.

7082
11:08:52,814 --> 11:09:02,128
我们要计算的是：在这些词——“我的孙子很喜欢它”——以任何顺序出现在评论中的情况下，该评论是正向情感的概率，
We're going to try to calculate the probability that the review is positive, given that all of these words, my grandson loved it, are in the review in no particular order,

7083
11:09:02,382 --> 11:09:04,288
仅仅是这个无序的
just this unordered collection of

7084
11:09:04,288 --> 11:09:10,852
词汇集合。这是一个条件概率，我们可以应用 Bayes' rule 来理解它。
words. And this is a conditional probability, which we can then apply Bayes' rule to try to make sense of.

7085
11:09:11,694 --> 11:09:15,968
那么根据 Bayes' rule，这个条件概率等于什么？
So according to Bayes' rule, this conditional probability is equal to what?

7086
11:09:16,128 --> 11:09:25,188
它等于：在评论是正向情感的情况下，这四个词都出现在评论中的概率，乘以评论是正向情感的概率，
It's equal to the probability that all of these four words are in the review, given that the review is positive, multiplied by the probability that the review is positive,

7087
11:09:25,488 --> 11:09:29,732
再除以这些词恰好出现在评论中的概率。
divided by the probability that all of these words happen to be in the review.

7088
11:09:30,606 --> 11:09:33,316
这就是我们现在要尝试计算的数值。
So this is the value now that we're going to try to calculate.

7089
11:09:33,870 --> 11:09:39,716
现在，你可能会注意到这里的分母，即所有这些词出现在评论中的概率，
Now, one thing you might notice is that the denominator here, the probability that all of these words appear in the review,

7090
11:09:39,982 --> 11:09:45,380
实际上并不取决于我们是在处理正向情感还是负向情感的情况。
doesn't actually depend on whether or not we're looking at the positive sentiment or negative sentiment case.

7091
11:09:45,902 --> 11:09:48,676
所以我们可以去掉这个分母，不需要去计算它。
So we can actually get rid of this denominator. We don't need to calculate it.

7092
11:09:48,928 --> 11:09:52,708
我们可以直接说这个概率与分子成比例。
We can just say that this probability is proportional to the numerator.

7093
11:09:53,230 --> 11:09:59,972
最后，我们需要对概率分布进行归一化，以确保所有数值相加等于 1。
And then at the end, we're going to need to normalize the probability distribution to make sure that all of the values sum up to the value one.

7094
11:10:00,750 --> 11:10:03,140
那么现在，我们该如何计算这个值呢？
So now, how do we calculate this value?

7095
11:10:03,470 --> 11:10:09,412
嗯，这是“所有词在正向情况下”的概率乘以“正向”的概率。
Well, this is the probability of all of these words given positive times probability of positive.

7096
11:10:09,966 --> 11:10:18,724
根据联合概率的定义，这就是一个大的联合概率，即这些情况同时成立的概率：评论是正向的，
And that, by the definition of joint probability, is just one big joint probability, the probability that all of these things are the case, that it's a positive review,

7097
11:10:18,928 --> 11:10:21,828
并且这四个词都在评论中。
and that all four of these words are in the review.

7098
11:10:22,798 --> 11:10:26,528
但即便如此，如何计算这个值仍然不是显而易见的。
But still, it's not entirely obvious how we calculate that value.

7099
11:10:26,798 --> 11:10:32,036
这里我们需要再做一个假设，这就是朴素贝叶斯中“朴素”的部分体现出来的。
And here is where we need to make one more assumption, and this is where the naive part of naive Bayes comes in.

7100
11:10:32,270 --> 11:10:36,548
我们将假设所有词之间都是相互独立的。
We're going to make the assumption that all of the words are independent of each other.

7101
11:10:36,910 --> 11:10:46,048
我的意思是，如果“孙子”这个词出现在评论中，它不会改变“喜欢”或“它”这两个词出现在评论中的概率。
And by that, I mean that if the word grandson is in the review, that doesn't change the probability that the word loved is in the review, or that the word it is in the review, for example.

7102
11:10:46,288 --> 11:10:48,608
在实践中，这个假设可能并不成立。
And in practice, this assumption might not be true.

7103
11:10:48,688 --> 11:10:56,420
几乎可以肯定地，词与词之间的概率是相互依赖的，但假设它们独立可以简化我们的分析，并仍能给出相当不错的预测结果。
It's almost certainly the case that the probability of words do depend on each other, but it's going to simplify our analysis and still give us reasonably good results,

7104
11:10:56,768 --> 11:11:03,684
只需假设这些词是独立的，且它们只取决于评论是正向还是负向。
just to assume that the words are independent of each other and they only depend on whether it's positive or negative.

7105
11:11:03,888 --> 11:11:09,636
例如，你可能会预期“喜欢”这个词在正向评论中出现的频率高于负向评论。
You might, for example, expect the word loved to appear more often in a positive review than in a negative review.

7106
11:11:10,542 --> 11:11:11,268
那这意味着什么呢？
So what does that mean?

7107
11:11:11,630 --> 11:11:21,636
如果我们做出这个假设，我们就可以说这个我们感兴趣的概率，并不是直接成比例，而是“朴素地”与这个值成比例。
Well, if we make this assumption, then we can say that this value, the probability we're interested in, is not directly proportional to, but it's naively proportional to this value.

7108
11:11:22,190 --> 11:11:24,580
评论是正向的概率
The probability that the review is positive

7109
11:11:25,294 --> 11:11:32,528
乘以“我的”在已知为正向情况下的出现概率，再乘以“孙子”在已知为正向情况下的出现概率，
times the probability that my is in the review, given that it's positive, times the probability that grandson is in the review, given that it's positive,

7110
11:11:32,718 --> 11:11:35,908
以此类推，处理这篇评论中出现的其他两个词。
and so on for the other two words that happen to be in this review.

7111
11:11:36,270 --> 11:11:41,860
现在这个看起来有点复杂的数值，实际上是一个我们可以比较容易计算出来的数值。
And now this value, which looks a little more complex, is actually a value that we can calculate pretty easily.

7112
11:11:42,670 --> 11:11:45,968
那么我们该如何估算评论是正面的概率呢？
So how are we going to estimate the probability that the review is positive?

7113
11:11:46,286 --> 11:11:52,900
嗯，如果我们有一些训练数据，一些已经被标记为正面或负面的示例评论数据的话，
Well, if we have some training data, some example data of example reviews where each one has already been labeled as positive or negative,

7114
11:11:53,198 --> 11:12:02,688
那么我们就可以通过计算正样本的数量并除以训练数据中的总样本数量，来估算评论是正面的概率。
then we can estimate the probability that a review is positive just by counting the number of positive samples and dividing by the total number of samples that we have in our training data.

7115
11:12:03,502 --> 11:12:11,012
至于条件概率，也就是在已知为正面的情况下出现 loved 的概率，那将是包含 loved 的正样本数量
And for the conditional probabilities, the probability of loved given that it's positive, well, that's going to be the number of positive samples with loved in

7116
11:12:11,758 --> 11:12:14,692
除以所有正样本的总数。
it divided by the total number of positive samples.

7117
11:12:15,374 --> 11:12:19,268
所以让我们看一个实际的例子，看看我们如何尝试计算这些数值。
So let's take a look at an actual example to see how we could try to calculate these values.

7118
11:12:19,790 --> 11:12:21,488
这里我准备了一些示例数据。
Here I've put together some sample data.

7119
11:12:21,806 --> 11:12:28,900
对这些示例数据的解读是：根据训练数据，49% 的评论是正面的，51% 是负面的。
The way to interpret the sample data is that based on the training data, 49% of the reviews are positive, 51% are negative.

7120
11:12:29,166 --> 11:12:32,516
然后在这张表格里，我们有一些条件概率。
And then over here in this table, we have some conditional probabilities.

7121
11:12:33,422 --> 11:12:38,564
如果评论是正面的，那么其中出现 my 的概率是 30%。
We have if the review is positive, then there's a 30% chance that my appears in it.

7122
11:12:38,702 --> 11:12:42,532
如果评论是负面的，那么其中出现 my 的概率是 20%。
And if the review is negative, there's a 20% chance that my appears in it.

7123
11:12:42,848 --> 11:12:48,004
而且根据我们的训练数据，在正向评论中，有 1% 的评论包含 grandson 这个词。
And based on our training data, among the positive reviews, 1% of them contain the word grandson.

7124
11:12:48,462 --> 11:12:51,620
而在负面评论中，有 2% 的评论包含 grandson 这个词。
And among the negative reviews, 2% contain the word grandson.

7125
11:12:52,398 --> 11:12:57,572
所以，利用这些数据，让我们试着计算这个我们感兴趣的数值。
So, using this data, let's try to calculate this value, the value we're interested in.

7126
11:12:57,870 --> 11:13:01,796
为了做到这一点，我们需要把所有这些数值乘在一起。
And to do that, we'll need to multiply all of these values together.

7127
11:13:02,048 --> 11:13:06,688
即正面的概率，再乘以所有这些正向条件概率。
The probability of positive, and then all of these positive conditional probabilities.

7128
11:13:06,926 --> 11:13:08,644
当我们这样做时，会得到一个数值。
And when we do that, we get some value.

7129
11:13:09,358 --> 11:13:11,908
然后我们可以对负面情况做同样的操作。
And then we can do the same thing for the negative case.

7130
11:13:12,142 --> 11:13:19,972
我们将做同样的操作：取它为负面的概率，乘以所有这些条件概率，我们就会得到另一个数值。
We're going to do the same thing, take the probability that it's negative, multiply it by all of these conditional probabilities, and we're going to get some other value.

7131
11:13:20,622 --> 11:13:27,248
现在这些数值的总和不等于 1，它们还没变成一个概率分布，但我可以对它们进行归一化并得到一些数值，
And now these values don't sum to one, they're not a probability distribution yet, but I can normalize them and get some values,

7132
11:13:27,328 --> 11:13:31,076
这能告诉我我们将预测“我的孙子很喜欢它”。
and that tells me that we're going to predict that my grandson loved it.

7133
11:13:31,328 --> 11:13:40,928
我们认为有 68% 的机会，即概率为 0.68，认为这是一条正向情感的评论，而 0.32 的概率是负面
We think there's a 68% chance, probability 0.68 that that is a positive sentiment review, and 0.32 probability that it's a negative

7134
11:13:40,928 --> 11:13:44,368
评论。那么这里可能会遇到什么问题呢？
review. So what problems might we run into here?

7135
11:13:44,528 --> 11:13:51,364
在进行这种分析以判断文本具有正向还是负向情感时，可能会出什么问题？
What could potentially go wrong when doing this kind of analysis in order to analyze whether text has a positive or negative sentiment?

7136
11:13:51,694 --> 11:13:53,348
嗯，可能会出现几个问题。
Well, a couple of problems might arise.

7137
11:13:53,774 --> 11:14:00,004
其中一个问题可能是：如果 grandson 这个词从未出现在任何正向评论中怎么办？
One problem might be: what if the word grandson never appears for any of the positive reviews?

7138
11:14:00,878 --> 11:14:08,368
如果是这种情况，当我们试图计算我们认为评论是正面的概率时，我们会把所有这些数值乘在一起，
If that were the case, then when we try to calculate the value, the probability that we think the review is positive, we're going to multiply all these values together,

7139
11:14:08,558 --> 11:14:14,116
而对于正向情况，我们最终只会得到 0，因为我们最终都会乘以那个 0 值。
and we're just going to get zero for the positive case, because we're all going to ultimately multiply by that zero value.

7140
11:14:14,382 --> 11:14:24,196
因此我们将认为评论没有可能是正面的，因为它包含了 grandson 这个词，而在我们的训练数据中，我们从未见过 grandson 出现在
And so we're going to say that we think there is no chance that the review is positive because it contains the word grandson, and in our training data, we've never seen the word grandson appear in

7141
11:14:24,846 --> 11:14:26,564
之前带有正面情感的信息。
a positive sentiment message before.

7142
11:14:26,990 --> 11:14:35,648
这可能不是正确的分析，因为在遇到罕见词时，情况可能是我们的训练数据中从未出现过“grandson”这个词
And that's probably not the right analysis, because in cases of rare words, it might be the case that in nowhere in our training data did we ever see the word grandson

7143
11:14:35,808 --> 11:14:38,084
出现在带有正面情感的信息中。
appear in a message that has positive sentiment.

7144
11:14:38,350 --> 11:14:39,940
那我们该怎么解决这个问题呢？
So what can we do to solve this problem?

7145
11:14:40,270 --> 11:14:48,196
嗯，我们通常会做一种平滑处理，即给分布中的每个值加上一个 alpha 值，只是为了让数据稍微平滑一点。
Well, one thing we'll often do is some kind of additive smoothing, where we add some value alpha to each value in our distribution just to smooth out the data a little bit.

7146
11:14:48,430 --> 11:14:53,408
其中一种常见的形式是拉普拉斯平滑，即给分布中的每个值加 1。
And a common form of this is Laplace smoothing, where we add one to each value in our distribution.

7147
11:14:53,614 --> 11:14:57,700
本质上，我们假装每个值比实际看到的还要多看到一次。
In essence, we pretend we've seen each value one more time than we actually have.

7148
11:14:57,968 --> 11:15:02,208
如果我们从未在正面评论中看到“grandson”这个词，我们就假装见过一次。
If we've never seen the word grandson for a positive review, we pretend we've seen it once.

7149
11:15:02,414 --> 11:15:11,908
如果我们见过一次，我们就假想见到了两次，只是为了避免可能出现的乘数为零的情况，从而导致分析结果不符合预期。
If we've seen it once, we pretend we've seen it twice, just to avoid the possibility that we might multiply by zero and as a result get some results we don't want in our analysis.

7150
11:15:12,782 --> 11:15:14,212
那让我们看看这在实践中是什么样子的。
So let's see what this looks like in practice.

7151
11:15:14,670 --> 11:15:21,348
让我们尝试进行一些朴素贝叶斯分类，来判断文本是属于正面还是负面。
Let's try to do some naive Bayes classification in order to classify text as either positive or negative.

7152
11:15:22,286 --> 11:15:32,100
我们将查看 sentiment.py，它会把一些示例数据加载到内存中，包括一些正面和负面的评论示例，
We'll take a look at sentiment.py, and what this is going to do is load some sample data into memory, some examples of positive reviews and negative reviews,

7153
11:15:32,398 --> 11:15:37,540
然后我们将在所有这些训练数据上训练一个朴素贝叶斯分类器。
and then we're going to train a naive Bayes classifier on all of this training data.

7154
11:15:38,414 --> 11:15:44,516
这些训练数据包含了我们在正面评论中看到的所有词汇，以及在负面评论中看到的所有词汇。
Training data that includes all of the words we see in positive reviews and all of the words we see in negative reviews.

7155
11:15:44,878 --> 11:15:47,364
然后我们将尝试对一些输入进行分类。
And then we're going to try to classify some input.

7156
11:15:48,142 --> 11:15:50,532
因此，我们将基于一个语料库来进行这项操作。
And so we're going to do this based on a corpus of data.

7157
11:15:50,798 --> 11:15:55,716
我有一些示例正面评论。这里是一些正面评论：比如“太棒了”、“很有趣”。
I have some example positive reviews. Here are some positive reviews. It was great, so much fun, for example.

7158
11:15:56,046 --> 11:15:59,008
然后是一些负面评论：不值得买、质量很差。
And then some negative reviews, not worth it, kind of cheap.

7159
11:15:59,088 --> 11:16:01,348
这些是些负面评论的例子。
These are some examples of negative reviews.

7160
11:16:02,126 --> 11:16:08,580
现在让我们试运行这个分类器，看看它如何将特定的文本分类为正面或负面。
So now let's try to run this classifier and see how it would classify particular text as either positive or negative.

7161
11:16:09,390 --> 11:16:10,788
我们将继续运行我们的
We'll go ahead and run our

7162
11:16:11,886 --> 11:16:13,508
对这个语料库的情感分析。
sentiment analysis on this corpus.

7163
11:16:14,318 --> 11:16:18,368
我们需要提供一条评论。所以我会输入类似“我很喜欢它”这样的内容。
And we need to provide it with a review. So I'll say something like I enjoyed it.

7164
11:16:19,534 --> 11:16:26,532
我们看到分类器显示，有大约 0.92 的概率认为这条特定的评论是正面的。
And we see that the classifier says there is about a 0.92 probability that we think that this particular review is positive.

7165
11:16:27,118 --> 11:16:28,288
让我们试一个负面的。
Let's try something negative.

7166
11:16:28,494 --> 11:16:30,884
我们试一下“价格过高”。
We'll try kind of overpriced.

7167
11:16:31,662 --> 11:16:36,928
我们看到现在有 0.96 的概率认为这条特定的评论是负面的。
And we see that there is a 0.96 probability now that we think that this particular review is negative.

7168
11:16:37,230 --> 11:16:45,328
因此，我们的朴素贝叶斯分类器已经学会了哪些词倾向于出现在正面评论中，以及哪些词倾向于出现在负面评论中。
And so our naive Bayes classifier has learned what kinds of words tend to appear in positive reviews and what kinds of words tend to appear in negative reviews.

7169
11:16:45,454 --> 11:16:52,708
结果就是，我们能够设计出一个可以预测特定评论是正面还是负面的分类器。
And as a result of that, we've been able to design a classifier that can predict whether a particular review is positive or negative.

7170
11:16:54,190 --> 11:17:00,548
所以这绝对是一个非常有用的工具，我们可以用它来尝试做一些预测，但为了达到这个目的，我们必须做出一些假设。
And so this definitely is a useful tool that we can use to try and make some predictions, but we had to make some assumptions in order to get there.

7171
11:17:00,910 --> 11:17:08,688
那么，如果我们现在想构建一些更复杂的模型，利用机器学习中的工具来更好地利用语言数据
So what if we want to now try to build some more sophisticated models, use some tools from machine learning to try and take better advantage of language data

7172
11:17:08,910 --> 11:17:13,060
以便得出更准确的结论，并解决新类型的任务和新类型的问题呢？
to be able to draw more accurate conclusions and solve new kinds of tasks and new kinds of problems?

7173
11:17:13,806 --> 11:17:20,688
嗯，我们已经好几次看到，当我们想要获取一些数据或输入时，最好能以一种让计算机能够理解的方式来处理它们
Well, we've seen a couple of times now that when we want to take some data and take some input, put it in a way that the computer is going to be able to make sense of,

7174
11:17:20,942 --> 11:17:24,452
将这些数据最终转化为数字会很有帮助。
it can be helpful to take that data and turn it into numbers ultimately.

7175
11:17:25,006 --> 11:17:33,248
所以，我们可能想要做的是提出一种词语表示方法，一种能把单词及其含义转化成数字的方法。
And so, what we might want to try to do is come up with some word representation, some way to take a word and translate its meaning into numbers.

7176
11:17:33,488 --> 11:17:41,764
因为，例如，如果我们想用神经网络来处理语言，把我们的语言交给一个神经网络，让它进行一些预测或分析时
Because, for example, if we wanted to use a neural network to be able to process language, give our language to a neural network and have it make some predictions or perform some analysis there,

7177
11:17:42,318 --> 11:17:48,068
神经网络接收的输入和生成的输出都是由数值组成的向量，也就是一组数字。
a neural network takes as input and produces as output a vector of values, a vector of numbers.

7178
11:17:48,462 --> 11:17:55,940
所以我们可能要做的是把我们的数据，也就是单词，转换成某种形式的数值表示。
And so what we might want to do is take our data and somehow take words and convert them into some kind of numeric representation.

7179
11:17:56,782 --> 11:17:57,668
那我们该怎么做呢？
So how might we do that?

7180
11:17:57,888 --> 11:18:00,868
我们该如何把词语变成数字呢？
How might we take words and turn them into numbers?

7181
11:18:01,518 --> 11:18:02,692
让我们看一个例子。
Let's take a look at an example.

7182
11:18:03,278 --> 11:18:09,572
这里有一个句子：he wrote a book，假设我想把这些词中的每一个都转换成由数值组成的向量。
Here's a sentence, he wrote a book, and let's say I wanted to take each of those words and turn it into a vector of values.

7183
11:18:10,190 --> 11:18:11,300
这是我可能会做的一种方法。
Here's one way I might do that.

7184
11:18:11,566 --> 11:18:17,252
我们将“he”定义为一个在第一个位置为 1，其余值均为 0 的向量。
We'll say he is going to be a vector that has a one in the first position, and the rest of the values are zero.

7185
11:18:17,742 --> 11:18:21,248
“wrote”将有第二个位置为 1，其他数值都是 0。
Rote will have a one in the second position, and the rest of the values are zero.

7186
11:18:21,568 --> 11:18:28,420
“a”在第三个位置为 1，其余值为 0；而“book”在第四个位置为 1，其余值也为 0。
A has a one in the third position with the rest of the value zero, and book has a one in the fourth position with the rest of the value zero.

7187
11:18:28,782 --> 11:18:32,612
这样，这些词现在都有了独特的向量表示。
So each of these words now has a distinct vector representation.

7188
11:18:33,294 --> 11:18:41,168
这就是我们常说的独热表示，即将词语的含义作为一个只有一个 1 的向量来表示
And this is what we often call a one hot representation, a representation of the meaning of a word as a vector with a single one

7189
11:18:41,358 --> 11:18:43,524
而其余的所有数值都是 0。
and all of the rest of the values are zero.

7190
11:18:43,886 --> 11:18:50,288
这样一来，我们现在为每个词都有了数值表示，我们可以将这些向量表示输入到
And so when doing this, we now have a numeric representation for every word, and we could pass in those vector representations into

7191
11:18:50,448 --> 11:18:55,012
神经网络或其他需要某种形式的数值数据作为输入的模型中。
a neural network or other models that require some kind of numeric data as input.

7192
11:18:55,822 --> 11:19:00,612
但这种独热表示实际上存在一些问题，由于几个原因，它并不理想。
But this one-hot representation actually has a couple of problems, and it's not ideal for a few reasons.

7193
11:19:01,230 --> 11:19:07,408
其中一个原因是，这里我们只看四个词，但如果你想象一个包含成千上万个词的词汇表的话
One reason is here we're just looking at four words, but if you imagine a vocabulary of thousands of words or more,

7194
11:19:07,694 --> 11:19:13,888
为了给词汇中每一个可能的词都分配一个独特的向量，这些向量将会变得非常长。
these vectors are going to get quite long in order to have a distinct vector for every possible word in a vocabulary.

7195
11:19:14,126 --> 11:19:20,772
结果就是，这些更长的向量将更难处理、更难训练等等，这可能就是一个问题。
And as a result of that, these longer vectors are going to be more difficult to deal with, more difficult to train, and so forth, and so that might be a problem.

7196
11:19:21,550 --> 11:19:23,748
另一个问题稍微微妙一点。
Another problem is a little bit more subtle.

7197
11:19:24,238 --> 11:19:30,608
如果我们想把一个词表示为一个向量，特别是把词的含义表示为一个向量，那么理想情况下
If we want to represent a word as a vector, and in particular the meaning of a word as a vector, then ideally

7198
11:19:30,830 --> 11:19:40,324
意思相近的词也应该有相似的向量表示，这样它们在向量空间中就会靠得很近。
it should be the case that words that have similar meanings should also have similar vector representations, so that they're close to each other together inside a vector space.

7199
11:19:41,038 --> 11:19:49,988
但在这些独热表示中情况并非如此，因为如果我们取一些意思相近的词，比如“wrote”和“authored”，它们表达的意思很像
But that's not really going to be the case with these one-hot representations, because if we take some similar words, say the word wrote and the word authored, which means similar things,

7200
11:19:50,254 --> 11:19:53,124
但它们却拥有完全不同的向量表示。
they have entirely different vector representations.

7201
11:19:54,030 --> 11:20:02,048
同样，book 和 novel 这两个词意思相近，但它们的向量表示完全不同，因为它们各自只有一个
Likewise, book and novel, those two words mean somewhat similar things, but they have entirely different vector representations because they each have a one

7202
11:20:02,288 --> 11:20:03,556
在某些不同位置上的 1。
in some different position.

7203
11:20:04,110 --> 11:20:05,540
所以这也不理想。
And so that's not ideal either.

7204
11:20:05,998 --> 11:20:10,128
因此，我们可能更感兴趣的是某种分布式表示。
So what we might be interested in instead is some kind of distributed representation.

7205
11:20:10,638 --> 11:20:19,264
分布式表示是将词义分布在多个值上，而不是仅仅在一个位置上有一个 1 的热编码。
A distributed representation is the representation of the meaning of a word distributed across multiple values instead of just being one hot with a one

7206
11:20:19,504 --> 11:20:20,356
就在一个位置上。
in one position.

7207
11:20:20,864 --> 11:20:24,932
这就是词的分布式表示可能是什么样子的。
Here is what a distributed representation of words might be.

7208
11:20:25,104 --> 11:20:36,292
每个词都关联一组数值向量，其含义分布在多个值中，理想情况下，意思相近的词会有相似的向量表示。
Each word is associated with some vector of values with the meaning distributed across multiple values, ideally in such a way that similar words have a similar vector representation.

7209
11:20:37,166 --> 11:20:38,944
但我们该如何得出这些值呢？
But how are we going to come up with those values?

7210
11:20:39,118 --> 11:20:40,452
这些值从哪里来？
Where do those values come from?

7211
11:20:40,624 --> 11:20:44,836
我们如何在这一串分布式的数字中定义一个词的含义？
How can we define the meaning of a word in this distributed sequence of numbers?

7212
11:20:45,806 --> 11:20:53,476
为了做到这一点，我们将从英国语言学家 J.R. Firth 的一句名言中汲取灵感，他说：你要通过它身边的伙伴来了解一个词。
Well, to do that, we're going to draw inspiration from a quote from British linguist J.R. Firth, who said, You shall know a word by the company it keeps.

7213
11:20:54,254 --> 11:21:00,676
换句话说，我们将根据出现在它周围的词，也就是它周围的上下文词，来定义一个词的含义。
In other words, we're going to define the meaning of a word based on the words that appear around it, the context words around it.

7214
11:21:01,230 --> 11:21:04,580
举个例子，这个语境是：他吃了（填空）。
Take, for example, this context, for blank he ate.

7215
11:21:05,262 --> 11:21:07,940
你可能会想，哪些词能合理地填补那个空白。
You might wonder what words could reasonably fill in that blank.

7216
11:21:08,782 --> 11:21:14,116
嗯，可能是 breakfast、lunch 或 dinner。这些词都可以合理地填入这个空格。
Well, it might be words like breakfast, or lunch, or dinner. All of those could reasonably fill in that blank.

7217
11:21:14,606 --> 11:21:20,292
因此我们可以说，因为 breakfast、lunch 和 dinner 出现在相似的语境中，
And so what we're going to say is because the words breakfast and lunch and dinner appear in a similar context,

7218
11:21:21,038 --> 11:21:22,660
它们一定具有相似的含义。
that they must have a similar meaning.

7219
11:21:23,342 --> 11:21:32,228
这是计算机可以理解并尝试学习的内容。计算机可以查看大量的文本语料库，观察哪些词往往出现在相似的语境中，
And that's something our computer could understand and try to learn. A computer could look at a big corpus of text, look at what words tend to appear in similar context to each other,

7220
11:21:32,464 --> 11:21:39,332
并利用这些信息来识别哪些词具有相似含义，因此在向量空间中应该彼此靠近。
and use that to identify which words have a similar meaning, and should therefore appear close to each other inside a vector space.

7221
11:21:40,206 --> 11:21:44,144
实现这一点的常用模型被称为 word2vec 模型。
And so one common model for doing this is known as the word2vec model.

7222
11:21:44,238 --> 11:21:52,388
它是一个通过查看数据和词出现的上下文来生成词向量，即为每个词提供向量表示的模型。
It's a model for generating word vectors, a vector representation for every word, by looking at data and looking at the context in which a word appears.

7223
11:21:53,006 --> 11:21:54,144
核心思路是这样的：
The idea is going to be this.

7224
11:21:54,304 --> 11:22:00,324
如果你从空间中随机位置开始排列所有词，并在一些训练数据上进行训练，
if you start out with all of the words, just in some random position in space and train it on some training data,

7225
11:22:00,974 --> 11:22:05,668
word2vec 模型就会开始学习哪些词出现在相似的语境中。
what the word2vec model will do is start to learn what words appear in similar contexts.

7226
11:22:05,934 --> 11:22:13,796
它会移动这些向量，使得具有相似含义的词，比如 breakfast、lunch 和 dinner，或者 book、memoir、novel，
and it will move these vectors around in such a way that hopefully, words with similar meanings, breakfast, lunch, and dinner, book, memoir, novel,

7227
11:22:14,382 --> 11:22:18,212
在作为向量时，也能期望出现在彼此附近。
will hopefully appear to be near to each other as vectors as well.

7228
11:22:19,054 --> 11:22:24,036
现在让我们看看在代码实现中，word2vec 在实践中是什么样子的。
So let's now take a look at what word2vec might look like in practice when implemented in code.

7229
11:22:24,910 --> 11:22:33,801
我在 words.text 文件里有一个预训练模型，其中这些词中的每一个都有由 word2vec 训练出的向量表示。
What I have here inside of words.text is a pre-trained model where each of these words has some vector representation trained by word2vec.

7230
11:22:34,064 --> 11:22:43,204
这些词中的每一个都有一组代表其含义的数值序列，理想情况下，相似的词会由相似的向量来表示。
Each of these words has some sequence of values representing its meaning, hopefully in such a way that similar words are represented by similar vectors.

7231
11:22:43,694 --> 11:22:48,704
我还有一个叫 vectors.py 的文件，它会打开这些单词并把它们组成一个字典，
I also have this file vectors.py, which is going to open up the words and form them into a dictionary,

7232
11:22:48,784 --> 11:22:57,744
我们还定义了一些有用的函数，比如 distance 来获取两个词向量之间的距离，还有 closest words 来找出哪些词在
and we also define some useful functions like distance to get the distance between two word vectors, and closest words to find which words are nearby in terms of

7233
11:22:57,984 --> 11:22:59,492
拥有彼此接近的向量这一方面是相关的。
having close vectors to each other.

7234
11:23:00,174 --> 11:23:01,316
那我们来试一下。
And so let's give this a try.

7235
11:23:02,350 --> 11:23:04,964
我们先打开 Python 解释器，
We'll go ahead and open a Python interpreter,

7236
11:23:05,904 --> 11:23:06,224
然后
and

7237
11:23:07,790 --> 11:23:09,508
我来导入这些 vectors。
I'm going to import these vectors.

7238
11:23:10,222 --> 11:23:14,180
我们可以问：好的，单词 book 的向量表示是什么？
And we might say, all right, what is the vector representation of the word book?

7239
11:23:15,630 --> 11:23:20,484
我们得到这个很长的向量，它把词 book 表示为一个值的序列。
And we get this big long vector that represents the word book as a sequence of values.

7240
11:23:21,102 --> 11:23:29,700
这个值序列本身并没有太多意义，但在与其他词的向量进行比较时，它就有意义了。
And this sequence of values by itself is not all that meaningful, but it is meaningful in the context of comparing it to other vectors for other words.

7241
11:23:30,318 --> 11:23:35,300
所以我们可以使用这个 distance 函数，它能帮我们获取两个词向量之间的距离。
So we could use this distance function, which is going to get us the distance between two word vectors.

7242
11:23:35,758 --> 11:23:41,604
我们可以问：词 book 的向量表示与词
And we might say what is the distance between the vector representation for the word book and the vector representation

7243
11:23:42,254 --> 11:23:43,172
对于单词「novel」的？
for the word novel?

7244
11:23:44,302 --> 11:23:46,020
我们看到结果是 0.34。
And we see that it's 0.34.

7245
11:23:46,304 --> 11:23:50,436
你可以把 0 理解为非常接近，而 1 理解为非常遥远。
You can kind of interpret zero as being really close together and one being very far apart.

7246
11:23:51,022 --> 11:23:55,204
那么现在 book 和比如 breakfast 之间的距离是多少？
And so now what is the distance between book and let's say breakfast?

7247
11:23:55,822 --> 11:24:02,116
嗯，book 和 breakfast 的差异比 book 和 novel 大，所以我预期这个距离会更大。
Well, book and breakfast are more different from each other than book and novel are, so I would hopefully expect the distance to be larger.

7248
11:24:02,574 --> 11:24:05,424
事实上，它大约是 0.64。
And in fact, it is 0.64 approximately.

7249
11:24:05,584 --> 11:24:07,620
这两个词离得更远一些。
These two words are further away from each other.

7250
11:24:08,302 --> 11:24:13,060
那现在 lunch 和 breakfast 之间的距离呢？
And what about now the distance between, let's say, lunch and breakfast?

7251
11:24:13,582 --> 11:24:14,784
嗯，那是大约 0.2。
Well, that's about 0.2.

7252
11:24:15,104 --> 11:24:19,076
这两个词甚至更接近。它们的含义更接近。
Those are even closer together. They have a meaning that is closer to each other.

7253
11:24:19,886 --> 11:24:21,444
我们还可以做另一件有趣的
Another interesting thing we might

7254
11:24:22,094 --> 11:24:23,844
事情，就是计算最接近的词。
do is calculate the closest words.

7255
11:24:24,398 --> 11:24:31,984
我们可以问：根据 Word2Vec，离词 book 最近的词是什么？让我们找出最接近的 10 个词。
We might say, what are the closest words, according to WordDevek, to the word book? And let's say let's get the ten closest words.

7256
11:24:32,144 --> 11:24:36,740
有哪些向量与词 book 的向量表示最接近？
What are the ten closest vectors to the vector representation for the word book?

7257
11:24:37,614 --> 11:24:40,624
当我们进行这项分析时，我们得到这个词列表。
And when we perform that analysis, we get this list of words.

7258
11:24:40,910 --> 11:24:48,544
最接近的一个是 book 本身，但我们还有它的复数形式，还有 essay、memoir、essays、novella、anthology 等等。
The closest one is book itself, but we also have book's plural, and then essay, memoir, essays, novella, anthology, and so on.

7259
11:24:48,784 --> 11:24:56,384
至少根据 Word2Vec，所有这些词的意思都和词 book 相似，因为它们有相似的向量表示。
All of these words mean something similar to the word book, according to word to vec at least, because they have a similar vector representation.

7260
11:24:56,590 --> 11:25:02,948
所以看起来我们在尝试捕捉这种词义的向量表示方面做得相当不错。
So it seems like we've done a pretty good job of trying to capture this kind of vector representation of word meaning.

7261
11:25:03,854 --> 11:25:11,504
Word2Vec 的另一个有趣的副作用是，它也能捕捉到词与词之间的关系。
One other interesting side effect of Word2Vec is that it's also able to capture something about the relationships between words as well.

7262
11:25:11,918 --> 11:25:13,124
让我们来看一个例子。
Let's take a look at an example.

7263
11:25:13,518 --> 11:25:19,908
这里有两个词，man 和 king，它们在 Word2Vec 中分别被表示为向量。
Here, for instance, are two words, man and king, and these are each represented by Word2Vec as vectors.

7264
11:25:20,430 --> 11:25:26,500
那么如果我用一个减去另一个，计算 king 减去 man 的值会发生什么？
So what might happen if I subtracted one from the other, calculated the value king minus man?

7265
11:25:27,310 --> 11:25:38,564
这个结果将是一个从 man 到 king 的向量，在某种程度上体现了词 man 的向量表示与词 king 的向量表示之间的关系。
Well, that will be the vector that will take us from man to king, somehow represent this relationship between the vector representation of the word man and the vector representation of the word king.

7266
11:25:38,926 --> 11:25:41,668
这就是这个值，即 king 减去 man 所代表的内容。
And that's what this value, king minus man, represents.

7267
11:25:42,574 --> 11:25:50,756
那么如果我取词 woman 的向量表示，并加上同样的值，也就是 king 减去 man，会发生什么？
So what would happen if I took the vector representation of the word woman and added that same value, king minus man, to it?

7268
11:25:51,182 --> 11:25:54,500
比如，我们得到的最接近的词是什么？
What would we get as the closest word to that, for example?

7269
11:25:54,958 --> 11:25:55,664
好，我们可以试一下。
Well, we could try it.

7270
11:25:55,744 --> 11:25:59,172
让我们回到 Python 解释器去尝试一下。
Let's go ahead and go back to our Python interpreter and give this a try.

7271
11:25:59,822 --> 11:26:07,908
我可以问：最接近“词 king 的向量表示减去词 man 的向量表示加上
I could say what is the closest word to the vector representation of the word king minus the representation of the word man plus

7272
11:26:08,270 --> 11:26:10,628
词 woman 的向量表示”的词是什么？
the representation of the word woman.

7273
11:26:11,374 --> 11:26:13,984
我们看到，最接近的词是 queen。
And we see that the closest word is the word queen.

7274
11:26:14,286 --> 11:26:22,144
我们设法捕捉到了 king 和 man 之间的关系，然后当我们把它应用到词 woman 上时，得到的结果就是
We've somehow been able to capture the relationship between king and man, and then when we apply it to the word woman, we get as the result the word

7275
11:26:22,574 --> 11:26:22,852
queen。
queen.

7276
11:26:24,174 --> 11:26:33,924
所以 Word2Vec 不仅能捕捉到词语以及它们之间的相似性，还能捕捉到词与词之间的关系以及这些词是如何相互关联的。
So word2vec has been able to capture not just the words and how they're similar to each other, but also something about the relationships between words and how those words are connected to each other.

7277
11:26:34,702 --> 11:26:38,304
既然我们现在有了词的向量表示，我们可以用它做什么呢？
So now that we have this vector representation of words, what can we now do with it?

7278
11:26:38,574 --> 11:26:44,676
现在我们可以把词表示为数字，因此我们可以尝试将这些词作为输入传递给，比如，一个神经网络。
Now we can represent words as numbers, and so we might try to pass those words as input to, say, a neural network.

7279
11:26:45,070 --> 11:26:50,304
我们见过的神经网络是识别模式和进行预测的强大工具。
Neural networks we've seen are very powerful tools for identifying patterns and making predictions.

7280
11:26:50,638 --> 11:27:00,004
记住，你可以把神经网络看作是由这些单元组成的，但实际上神经网络做的是接收某些输入，将其传入网络，然后产生一些输出。
Recall that a neural network you can think of as all of these units, but really what the neural network is doing is taking some input, passing it into the network, and then producing some output.

7281
11:27:00,334 --> 11:27:08,132
通过为神经网络提供训练数据，我们能够更新网络内部的权重，从而让神经网络能够更准确地
And by providing the neural network with training data, we're able to update the weights inside of the network so that the neural network can do a more accurate job

7282
11:27:08,398 --> 11:27:10,884
将这些输入转换成相应的输出。
of translating those inputs into those outputs.

7283
11:27:11,726 --> 11:27:21,124
既然现在我们可以把词表示为可能作为输入或输出的数字，你可以想象将一个词作为输入传给神经网络，并得到一个词作为输出。
And now that we can represent words as numbers that could be the input or output, you could imagine passing a word in as input to a neural network and getting a word as output.

7284
11:27:21,678 --> 11:27:23,024
那么这种情况什么时候会有用呢？
And so when might that be useful?

7285
11:27:23,310 --> 11:27:29,664
神经网络的一个常见用途是机器翻译，即当我们想把文本从一种语言翻译成另一种语言时。
One common use for neural networks is in machine translation, when we want to translate text from one language into another.

7286
11:27:29,998 --> 11:27:35,780
比如将英语翻译成法语，通过将英文输入到神经网络中并获得一些法语输出。
Say translate English into French by passing English into the neural network and getting some French output.

7287
11:27:36,174 --> 11:27:42,916
例如，你可以想象我们将 LAMP 这个英文单词输入到神经网络中，得到 LAMP 的法语单词作为输出。
You might imagine, for instance, that we could take the English word for LAMP, pass it into the neural network, get the French word for LAMP as output.

7288
11:27:43,790 --> 11:27:52,704
但在实践中，当我们把文本从一种语言翻译成另一种语言时，我们通常不只是对将单个词从一种语言翻译到另一种语言感兴趣，
But in practice, when we're translating text from one language to another, we're usually not just interested in translating a single word from one language to another,

7289
11:27:52,910 --> 11:27:55,812
而是针对一个序列，比如一段话或一个段落。
but a sequence, say a sentence or a paragraph of words.

7290
11:27:56,270 --> 11:28:00,228
这里是另一个段落，同样取自《福尔摩斯探案》，是用英语写的。
Here, for example, is another paragraph, again taken from Sherlock Holmes, written in English.

7291
11:28:00,622 --> 11:28:09,060
我可能想做的是把整句内容输入到神经网络中，并让它输出同一句的法语翻译。
And what I might want to do is take that entire sentence, pass it into the neural network, and get as output a French translation of the same sentence.

7292
11:28:10,094 --> 11:28:14,500
但请记住，神经网络的输入和输出需要是固定大小的。
But recall that a neural network's input and output needs to be of some fixed size.

7293
11:28:14,862 --> 11:28:20,352
而句子并不是固定长度的，它是可变的。你可能会遇到短句，也可能遇到长句。
And a sentence is not a fixed size, it's variable. You might have shorter sentences and you might have longer sentences.

7294
11:28:20,686 --> 11:28:27,364
所以我们必须想办法通过神经网络解决将一个序列翻译成另一个序列的问题。
So somehow we need to solve the problem of translating a sequence into another sequence by means of a neural network.

7295
11:28:27,632 --> 11:28:31,748
这不仅适用于机器翻译，也适用于其他问题。
And that's going to be true not only for machine translation, but also for other problems.

7296
11:28:32,112 --> 11:28:33,700
比如问答系统。
Problems like question answering.

7297
11:28:33,934 --> 11:28:38,532
如果我想输入一个问题，比如“马萨诸塞州的首都是哪里？”
If I want to pass as input a question, something like, what is the capital of Massachusetts?

7298
11:28:38,990 --> 11:28:45,508
将它作为输入喂给神经网络，我希望得到的输出是像“首都是波士顿”这样的句子。
Feed that as input into the neural network, I would hope that what I would get as output is a sentence like, the capital is Boston.

7299
11:28:45,792 --> 11:28:49,284
同样，这是在将一个序列转换成另一个序列。
Again, translating some sequence into some other sequence.

7300
11:28:49,998 --> 11:28:57,232
如果你曾与 AI 聊天机器人交流过，或者向手机提问过，它就需要执行类似的操作。
And if you've ever had a conversation with an AI chatbot or have ever asked your phone a question, it needs to do something like this.

7301
11:28:57,392 --> 11:29:05,572
它需要理解你作为人类提供的输入词序列，然后计算机需要生成相应的输出词序列。
It needs to understand the sequence of words that you, the human, provided as input, and then the computer needs to generate some sequence of words as output.

7302
11:29:06,190 --> 11:29:07,108
那么我们该如何实现这一点呢？
So how can we do this?

7303
11:29:07,502 --> 11:29:15,232
我们可以使用一个工具，就是我们上次看过的循环神经网络，它是一种让我们向
Well, one tool that we can use is the recurrent neural network, which we took a look at last time, which is a way for us to provide a sequence of values to a

7304
11:29:15,232 --> 11:29:18,116
神经网络提供一系列数值的方法，通过多次运行神经网络来实现。
neural network by running the neural network multiple times.

7305
11:29:18,574 --> 11:29:24,644
每次运行神经网络时，我们要做的就是记录一些隐藏状态。
And each time we run the neural network, what we're going to do is we're going to keep track of some hidden state.

7306
11:29:25,006 --> 11:29:32,228
这个隐藏状态会从一次神经网络运行传递到下一次，从而保留所有相关的关键信息。
And that hidden state is going to be passed from one run of the neural network to the next run of the neural network, keeping track of all of the relevant information.

7307
11:29:33,198 --> 11:29:36,192
那么让我们看看如何将它应用到类似的情况中。
And so let's take a look at how we could apply that to something like this.

7308
11:29:36,398 --> 11:29:45,828
特别是，我们将研究一种被称为“编码器-解码器”架构，我们将把这个问题编码成某种隐藏状态，
And in particular, we're going to look at an architecture known as an encoder-decoder architecture, where we're going to encode this question into some kind of hidden state,

7309
11:29:46,286 --> 11:29:51,076
然后使用解码器将该隐藏状态解码为我们感兴趣的输出。
and then use a decoder to decode that hidden state into the output that we're interested in.

7310
11:29:51,982 --> 11:29:53,060
那具体是什么样的过程呢？
So what's that going to look like?

7311
11:29:53,454 --> 11:30:00,292
我们从第一个词“what”开始，它进入我们的神经网络，并产生某种隐藏状态。
We'll start with the first word, the word what, that goes into our neural network, and it's going to produce some hidden state.

7312
11:30:00,686 --> 11:30:05,796
这是关于“what”这个词的一些信息，我们的神经网络需要记录这些信息。
This is some information about the word what that our neural network is going to need to keep track of.

7313
11:30:06,798 --> 11:30:08,452
接着当第二个词出现时，
Then when the second word comes along,

7314
11:30:09,134 --> 11:30:15,460
我们会把它喂给同一个编码器神经网络，但它同时也会接收到那个隐藏状态作为输入。
we're going to feed it into that same encoder neural network, but it's going to get as input that hidden state as well.

7315
11:30:15,982 --> 11:30:23,140
所以我们输入第二个词的同时，也获取了关于隐藏状态的信息，这个过程会持续到输入的其他单词为止。
So we pass in the second word, we also get the information about the hidden state, and that's going to continue for the other words in the input.

7316
11:30:23,392 --> 11:30:25,316
这将会产生一个新的隐藏状态。
This is going to produce a new hidden state.

7317
11:30:25,582 --> 11:30:27,872
因此当我们处理到第三个词时，
And so then when we get to the third word, the,

7318
11:30:28,814 --> 11:30:32,068
它进入编码器时，也能获取到隐藏状态。
that goes into the encoder, it also gets access to the hidden state.

7319
11:30:32,462 --> 11:30:36,912
然后它会产生一个新的隐藏状态，并在我们使用“capital”这个词时传递到下一次运行中。
And then it produces a new hidden state that gets passed into the next run when we use the word capital.

7320
11:30:37,134 --> 11:30:41,380
同样的情况也会在输入中出现的其他单词上重复发生。
And the same thing is going to repeat for the other words that appear in the input.

7321
11:30:41,582 --> 11:30:46,404
所以马萨诸塞州，这产生了一个最终的隐藏状态。
So of Massachusetts, that produces one final piece of hidden state.

7322
11:30:47,278 --> 11:30:49,872
现在我们得以某种方式发出信号，表明我们已经结束了。
Now somehow we need to signal the fact that we're done.

7323
11:30:50,032 --> 11:30:51,364
输入中已经没有任何内容了。
There's nothing left in the input.

7324
11:30:51,630 --> 11:31:00,068
我们通常的做法是向神经网络传递某种特殊标记，比如一个结束标记，现在解码过程就要开始了。
And we typically do this by passing some kind of special token, say an end token, into the neural network, and now the decoding process is going to start.

7325
11:31:00,462 --> 11:31:02,432
我们要生成单词 the，
We're going to generate the word the,

7326
11:31:03,310 --> 11:31:05,152
但除了生成单词 the 之外，
but in addition to generating the word the,

7327
11:31:06,030 --> 11:31:10,436
这个解码器网络还会生成某种隐藏状态。
this decoder network is also going to generate some kind of hidden state.

7328
11:31:11,118 --> 11:31:12,772
那么下一次会发生什么呢？
And so what happens the next time?

7329
11:31:13,134 --> 11:31:17,956
嗯，为了生成下一个词，知道第一个词是什么可能会很有帮助。
Well, to generate the next word, it might be helpful to know what the first word was.

7330
11:31:18,542 --> 11:31:21,956
所以我们可能会把第一个词 the 再传回解码器网络中。
So we might pass the first word the back into the decoder network.

7331
11:31:22,766 --> 11:31:26,980
它会把这个隐藏状态作为输入，并生成下一个词 capital。
It's going to get as input this hidden state, and it's going to generate the next word capital.

7332
11:31:27,566 --> 11:31:29,636
而这也会产生一些隐藏状态。
And that's also going to generate some hidden state.

7333
11:31:29,998 --> 11:31:36,964
我们将重复这个过程，把 capital 输入网络以生成第三个词 is，然后再进行一次以获取第四个词 Boston。
And we'll repeat that, passing capital into the network to generate the third word is, and then one more time in order to get the fourth word Boston.

7334
11:31:37,966 --> 11:31:39,152
到那时我们就完成了。
And at that point we're done.

7335
11:31:39,406 --> 11:31:40,592
但我们怎么知道已经完成了呢？
But how do we know we're done?

7336
11:31:40,782 --> 11:31:50,148
通常我们会再做最后一次，把 Boston 输入解码器网络，并得到一个输出为某种结束标记，以表明这是我们输入的终点。
Usually we'll do this one more time, pass Boston into the decoder network, and get an output some end token to indicate that that is the end of our input.

7337
11:31:50,670 --> 11:32:00,804
这就是我们如何利用循环神经网络来获取一些输入，将其编码成隐藏状态，然后利用该隐藏状态将其解码为我们感兴趣的输出。
And so this then is how we could use a recurrent neural network to take some input, encode it into some hidden state, and then use that hidden state to decode it into the output we're interested in.

7338
11:32:01,166 --> 11:32:04,512
换一种稍微不同的方式来可视化它：我们有一些输入序列。
To visualize it in a slightly different way, we have some input sequence.

7339
11:32:04,592 --> 11:32:06,372
这只是一个词语序列。
This is just some sequence of words.

7340
11:32:06,734 --> 11:32:16,032
该输入序列进入编码器（在这种情况下是一个循环神经网络），在过程中生成这些隐藏状态，直到我们生成最终的隐藏
That input sequence goes into the encoder, which in this case is a recurrent neural network, generating these hidden states along the way, until we generate some final hidden

7341
11:32:16,032 --> 11:32:23,524
状态，此时我们开始解码过程，同样使用一个循环神经网络，它也将生成输出序列。
state, at which point we start the decoding process, again using a recurrent neural network, that's going to generate the output sequence as well.

7342
11:32:23,886 --> 11:32:30,564
所以我们有一个编码器，它将输入序列的信息编码到这个隐藏状态中，然后是解码器
So we've got the encoder, which is encoding the information about the input sequence into this hidden state, and then the decoder,

7343
11:32:30,798 --> 11:32:35,108
它接收该隐藏状态并利用它来生成输出序列。
which takes that hidden state and uses it in order to generate the output sequence.

7344
11:32:36,334 --> 11:32:37,472
但这里存在一些问题。
But there are some problems.

7345
11:32:37,552 --> 11:32:46,692
多年来，这就是最先进的技术。循环神经网络基于这种方法的特性是当时我们已知处理自然语言处理任务的最佳方法之一。
And for many years, this was the state of the art. The recurrent neural network invariants on this approach were some of the best ways we knew in order to perform tasks in natural language processing.

7346
11:32:47,022 --> 11:32:53,828
但有一些问题是我们想要尝试解决的，而且这些问题在过去几年中为了改进此类模型已被逐步解决。
But there are some problems that we might want to try to deal with and that have been dealt with over the years to try and improve upon this kind of model.

7347
11:32:54,414 --> 11:32:57,796
你可能会注意到一个问题发生在这个编码阶段。
And one problem you might notice happens in this encoder stage.

7348
11:32:58,222 --> 11:33:05,060
我们获取了这个输入序列，即词语序列，并将其全部编码到这个最终的隐藏状态中。
We've taken this input sequence, the sequence of words, and encoded it all into this final piece of hidden state.

7349
11:33:05,422 --> 11:33:13,700
而这个最终的隐藏状态需要包含从输入序列中获取的所有信息，以便生成输出序列。
And that final piece of hidden state needs to contain all of the information from the input sequence that we need in order to generate the output sequence.

7350
11:33:14,734 --> 11:33:20,032
虽然这是可行的，但随着序列变得越来越长，这就会变得越来越困难。
And while that's possible, it becomes increasingly difficult as the sequence gets larger and larger.

7351
11:33:20,270 --> 11:33:28,912
对于越来越长的输入序列，要将我们需要的全部信息都存储在这个单一的隐藏状态中会变得越来越困难。
For larger and larger input sequences, it's going to become more and more difficult to store all of the information we need about the input inside this single hidden

7352
11:33:29,134 --> 11:33:30,084
这个上下文片段。
state piece of context.

7353
11:33:30,606 --> 11:33:33,472
要把这么多信息塞进一个单一的值里，压力太大了。
That's a lot of information to pack into just a single value.

7354
11:33:33,712 --> 11:33:44,324
在生成输出时，如果我们不只参考这一个值，而是参考编码器产生的所有之前的隐藏值，可能会很有用。
It might be useful for us when generating output to not just refer to this one value, but to all of the previous hidden values that have been generated by the encoder.

7355
11:33:45,070 --> 11:33:49,732
这样做可能有用，但我们该怎么做呢？我们有很多不同的值，需要某种方式把它们结合起来。
And so that might be useful, but how could we do that? We've got a lot of different values, we need to combine them somehow.

7356
11:33:50,126 --> 11:33:59,140
你可以想象把它们相加，或者取平均值，但这样做会默认这些隐藏状态片段的重要性是相同的。
So you could imagine adding them together, taking the average of them, for example, but doing that would assume that all of these pieces of hidden state are equally important.

7357
11:33:59,694 --> 11:34:01,232
但这并不一定成立。
But that's not necessarily true either.

7358
11:34:01,392 --> 11:34:08,196
某些隐藏状态片段会比其他的更重要，这取决于它们最接近哪个词。
Some of these pieces of hidden state are going to be more important than others, depending on what word they most closely correspond to.

7359
11:34:08,494 --> 11:34:17,252
例如，这个隐藏状态非常对应输入序列的第一个词，而那个则非常对应第二个词。
This piece of hidden state very closely corresponds to the first word of the input sequence, this one very closely corresponds to the second word of the input sequence, for example,

7360
11:34:17,742 --> 11:34:20,612
其中一些会比其他的更重要。
and some of those are going to be more important than others.

7361
11:34:21,262 --> 11:34:29,348
情况变得更复杂的是，根据我们正在生成输出序列中的哪一个词，不同的输入词可能具有不同程度的重要性。
To make matters more complicated, depending on which word of the output sequence we're generating, different input words might be more or less important.

7362
11:34:29,966 --> 11:34:37,988
所以我们真正想要的是一种方法，能让我们决定在特定时间点，哪些输入值值得关注。
And so what we really want is some way to decide for ourselves which of the input values are worth paying attention to at what point in time.

7363
11:34:38,510 --> 11:34:41,764
这就是被称为「注意力」机制的核心思想。
And this is the key idea behind a mechanism known as attention.

7364
11:34:42,126 --> 11:34:50,724
注意力的核心就在于让我们在生成——在这种情况下是序列中的下一个词时——决定哪些值是需要关注的。
Attention is all about letting us decide which values are important to pay attention to when generating, in this case, the next word in our sequence.

7365
11:34:51,822 --> 11:34:53,764
那我们来看看一个例子。
So let's take a look at an example of that.

7366
11:34:54,222 --> 11:34:54,980
这是一个句子。
Here's a sentence.

7367
11:34:55,312 --> 11:34:57,552
马萨诸塞大学的首都是哪里？
What is the capital of Massachusetts?

7368
11:34:57,712 --> 11:34:58,820
还是之前的那个句子。
Same sentence as before.

7369
11:34:59,086 --> 11:35:03,940
假设我们正试图通过生成输出标记来回答这个问题。
And let's imagine that we were trying to answer that question by generating tokens of output.

7370
11:35:04,270 --> 11:35:05,604
那么输出看起来会是什么样？
So what would the output look like?

7371
11:35:05,838 --> 11:35:12,164
它看起来会像「首都是」，假设我们现在正试图生成这里的最后一个词。
Well, it's going to look like something like the capital is, and let's say we're now trying to generate this last word here.

7372
11:35:12,558 --> 11:35:13,712
那个最后一个词是什么？
What is that last word?

7373
11:35:13,872 --> 11:35:16,068
计算机将如何推断出它？
How is the computer going to figure it out?

7374
11:35:16,654 --> 11:35:21,796
嗯，它需要做的是决定它要关注哪些值。
Well, what it's going to need to do is decide which values it's going to pay attention to.

7375
11:35:22,286 --> 11:35:30,592
因此，注意力机制将允许我们为每个词计算一些注意力分数，即对应每个词的某个数值。
And so the attention mechanism will allow us to calculate some attention scores for each word, some value corresponding to each word,

7376
11:35:30,832 --> 11:35:35,524
从而确定在当前时刻，关注那个词对我们有多重要。
determining how relevant is it for us to pay attention to that word right now.

7377
11:35:36,238 --> 11:35:45,444
在这种情况下，当生成输出序列的第四个词时，最值得关注的词可能是「capital」和「Massachusetts」。
And in this case, when generating the fourth word of the output sequence, the most important words to pay attention to might be capital and Massachusetts, for example.

7378
11:35:46,158 --> 11:35:48,804
也就是说，那些词将变得特别相关。
That those words are going to be particularly relevant.

7379
11:35:49,166 --> 11:35:53,472
为了计算这些注意力分数，有多种不同的机制可以使用。
And there are a number of different mechanisms that have been used in order to calculate these attention scores.

7380
11:35:53,712 --> 11:36:01,792
它可以是简单到用点积来查看两个向量的相似度，或者我们可以训练整个神经网络来计算这些注意力分数。
It could be something as simple as a dot product to see how similar two vectors are, or we could train an entire neural network to calculate these attention scores.

7381
11:36:01,998 --> 11:36:09,124
但核心思想是，在神经网络的训练过程中，我们将学会如何计算这些注意力分数。
But the key idea is that during the training process for our neural network, we're going to learn how to calculate these attention scores.

7382
11:36:09,392 --> 11:36:16,196
我们的模型将学会哪些内容是需要重点关注的，从而决定下一个词应该是什。
Our model is going to learn what is important to pay attention to in order to decide what the next word should be.

7383
11:36:17,166 --> 11:36:24,320
所以，计算这些注意力分数的结果是，我们可以为每个输入词计算出一个值，
So the result of all of this, calculating these attention scores, is that we can calculate some value, some value for each input word,

7384
11:36:24,526 --> 11:36:29,188
来确定我们对那个特定值的关注程度有多重要。
determining how important is it for us to pay attention to that particular value.

7385
11:36:29,838 --> 11:36:39,428
别忘了，每一个输入词都与一个隐藏状态上下文向量相关联，它捕捉了到该点为止的句子信息，
And recall that each of these input words is also associated with one of these hidden state context vectors, capturing information about the sentence up to that point,

7386
11:36:39,600 --> 11:36:42,820
但主要集中在那个特定的词上。
but primarily focused on that word in particular.

7387
11:36:43,502 --> 11:36:51,972
因此，如果我们拥有所有这些向量，并且有代表我们对这些特定向量关注程度的值，
And so what we can now do is if we have all of these vectors and we have values representing how important is it for us to pay attention to those particular vectors,

7388
11:36:52,302 --> 11:36:53,828
我们就可以进行加权平均。
is we can take a weighted average.

7389
11:36:54,286 --> 11:37:03,908
我们可以把这些向量乘以它们的注意力分数并相加，从而得到一个新的向量值，它将代表来自输入的上下文，
We can take all of these vectors, multiply them by their attention scores, and add them up to get some new vector value, which is going to represent the context from the input,

7390
11:37:04,160 --> 11:37:08,772
但特别侧重于我们认为最重要的那些词。
but specifically paying attention to the words that we think are most important.

7391
11:37:09,486 --> 11:37:17,668
完成这一步后，这个上下文向量就可以输入到我们的解码器中，从而确定该词应该是什么，在这种情况下是 Boston。
And once we've done that, that context vector can be fed into our decoder in order to say that the word should be, in this case, Boston.

7392
11:37:18,670 --> 11:37:27,844
所以注意力是一个非常强大的工具，它允许我们在尝试解码时决定应该关注输入的哪些词，
So attention is this very powerful tool that allows any word when we're trying to decode it to decide which words from the input should we pay attention to

7393
11:37:28,046 --> 11:37:32,644
以便确定生成下一个输出词时哪些内容是重要的。
in order to determine what's important for generating the next word of the output.

7394
11:37:33,358 --> 11:37:37,600
这个技术最早被广泛应用在机器翻译领域。
And one of the first places this was really used was in the field of machine translation.

7395
11:37:37,902 --> 11:37:45,572
这是介绍这一概念的论文中的一个图表示例，它专注于尝试将英语句子翻译成法语句子。
Here's an example of a diagram from the paper that introduced this idea, which was focused on trying to translate English sentences into French sentences.

7396
11:37:45,774 --> 11:37:52,196
我们在顶部有一个输入的英文句子，然后在左侧有对应的输出法语句子。
So we have an input English sentence up along the top, and then along the left side, the output French equivalent of that same sentence.

7397
11:37:52,622 --> 11:38:00,580
在所有这些方格中，你看到的是可视化的注意力分数，颜色越浅的方块表示注意力分数越高。
And what you see in all of these squares are the attention scores visualized, where a lighter square indicates a higher attention score.

7398
11:38:01,262 --> 11:38:07,280
你会注意到，法语单词与对应的英语单词之间有很强的对应关系，
And what you'll notice is that there's a strong correspondence between the French word and the equivalent English word,

7399
11:38:07,440 --> 11:38:16,800
法语中的“同意”一词确实在关注英语中的“同意”，以便决定在那个时间点应该生成哪个法语词。
that the French word for agreement is really paying attention to the English word for agreement in order to decide what French word should be generated at that point in time.

7400
11:38:17,038 --> 11:38:19,140
有时你可能会关注多个词。
And sometimes you might pay attention to multiple words.

7401
11:38:19,360 --> 11:38:29,380
如果你看法语里的“经济”这个词，它主要关注英语中的“经济”，但在这种情况下也关注了英语中的“欧洲”这个词，
If you look at the French word for economic, that's primarily paying attention to the English word for economic, but also paying attention to the English word for European in this case,

7402
11:38:29,600 --> 11:38:29,920
同样也是。
too.

7403
11:38:30,382 --> 11:38:37,920
因此，注意力分数非常容易可视化，从而让我们了解机器学习模型究竟在关注什么？
And so attention scores are very easy to visualize to get a sense for what is our machine learning model really paying attention to?

7404
11:38:38,080 --> 11:38:45,860
它正在利用哪些信息来判断什么是重要的、什么不是重要的，从而确定最终的输出标记应该是什么。
What information is it using in order to determine what's important and what's not in order to determine what the ultimate output token should be.

7405
11:38:46,734 --> 11:38:52,720
因此，当我们把注意力机制与循环神经网络结合时，我们可以获得非常强大且有用的结果，
And so when we combine the attention mechanism with a recurrent neural network, we can get very powerful and useful results

7406
11:38:52,880 --> 11:38:57,796
我们能够通过关注输入序列来生成输出序列。
where we're able to generate an output sequence by paying attention to the input sequence too.

7407
11:38:58,094 --> 11:39:02,052
但是使用循环神经网络这种方法也存在其他问题。
But there are other problems with this approach of using a recurrent neural network as well.

7408
11:39:02,286 --> 11:39:07,588
特别是，注意神经网络的每一次运行都依赖于前一步的输出。
In particular, notice that every run of the neural network depends on the output of the previous step.

7409
11:39:07,886 --> 11:39:12,548
这对于理解词语的序列以及这些特定词的顺序很重要，
And that was important for getting a sense for the sequence of words and the ordering of those particular words,

7410
11:39:12,814 --> 11:39:21,124
但在计算出上一个输入标记产生的隐藏状态之前，我们无法运行神经网络的这个单元。
but we can't run this unit of the neural network until after we've calculated the hidden state from the run before it from the previous input token.

7411
11:39:21,678 --> 11:39:25,508
这意味着这个过程很难并行化。
And what that means is that it's very difficult to parallelize this process.

7412
11:39:25,838 --> 11:39:35,360
随着输入序列变得越来越长，我们可能想利用并行化来加速训练神经网络并理解所有这些语言数据的过程，
That as the input sequence get longer and longer, we might want to use parallelism to try and speed up this process of training the neural network and making sense of all of this language data,

7413
11:39:35,598 --> 11:39:41,860
但这样做很难，而且在循环神经网络中执行起来很慢，因为所有步骤都必须按顺序进行。
but it's difficult to do that, and it's slow to do that with a recurrent neural network because all of it needs to be performed in sequence.

7414
11:39:42,446 --> 11:39:47,524
随着我们开始使用越来越大的语言模型，这成了一个日益严峻的挑战。
And that's become an increasing challenge as we've started to get larger and larger language models.

7415
11:39:47,822 --> 11:39:56,080
我们能获得的用于训练机器学习模型的语言数据越多，模型就越准确，对语言的表征就越好，
The more language data that we have available to us to use to train our machine learning models, the more accurate it can be, the better representation of language it can have,

7416
11:39:56,160 --> 11:39:59,840
它就能有更好的理解，我们也能看到更好的结果。
the better understanding it can have, and the better results that we can see.

7417
11:40:00,110 --> 11:40:07,748
因此我们看到了大语言模型的增长，它们使用越来越大的数据集，但结果就是它们的训练时间越来越长。
And so we've seen this growth of large language models that are using larger and larger data sets, but as a result, they take longer and longer to train.

7418
11:40:08,046 --> 11:40:14,564
因此，循环神经网络难以并行化这一问题变得越来越严重。
And so this problem that recurrent neural networks are not easy to parallelize has become an increasing problem.

7419
11:40:15,182 --> 11:40:24,900
因此，这成为了采用不同架构来思考如何处理自然语言的主要动力，这就是所谓的 Transformer 架构。
And as a result of that, that was one of the main motivations for a different architecture for thinking about how to deal with natural language, and that's known as the transformer architecture.

7420
11:40:25,184 --> 11:40:34,020
这是自然语言处理领域的一个重要里程碑，它极大地提高了我们执行此类自然语言处理任务的能力，
And this has been a significant milestone in the world of natural language processing for really increasing how well we can perform these kinds of natural language processing tasks,

7421
11:40:34,350 --> 11:40:39,428
同时也加快了训练机器学习模型以产生有效结果的速度。
as well as how quickly we can train a machine learning model to be able to produce effective results.

7422
11:40:39,982 --> 11:40:48,612
从工作原理来看，有多种不同类型的 Transformer，但我们在这里要看的是一种 Transformer 可能运作的基本架构，
There are a number of different types of transformers in terms of how they work, but what we're going to take a look at here is the basic architecture for how one might work with a transformer

7423
11:40:48,782 --> 11:40:51,104
以便了解其中涉及的内容以及我们的做法。
to get a sense for what's involved and what we're

7424
11:40:51,104 --> 11:40:58,784
所以让我们从之前看的模型开始，具体是到我们编码器-解码器架构中的这个编码器部分，
doing. So let's start with the model we were looking at before, specifically at this encoder part of our encoder-decoder architecture,

7425
11:40:59,022 --> 11:41:08,772
在那里我们使用循环神经网络来处理这个输入序列，并获取关于隐藏状态以及我们需要了解的关于该输入序列的信息。
where we used a recurrent neural network to take this input sequence and capture all of this information about the hidden state and the information we need to know about that input sequence.

7426
11:41:09,486 --> 11:41:19,904
现在，所有内容都需要按线性顺序进行，但 Transformer 将允许我们独立处理每个单词，这种方式很容易并行化。
Right now, it all needs to happen in this linear progression, but what the transformer is going to allow us to do is process each of the words independently in a way that's easy to parallelize.

7427
11:41:20,064 --> 11:41:30,852
不再让每个词等待其他词，而是让每个词都通过同一个神经网络，并产生该特定输入词的某种编码表示。
Rather than have each word wait for some other word, each word is going to go through the same neural network and produce some kind of encoded representation of that particular input word.

7428
11:41:31,118 --> 11:41:33,156
而所有这些都将并行发生。
And all of this is going to happen in parallel.

7429
11:41:33,806 --> 11:41:39,024
现在所有单词都在同时处理，但为了清晰起见，我们只关注一个词的处理过程。
Now it's happening for all of the words at once, but we're really just going to focus on what's happening for one word to make it clear.

7430
11:41:39,246 --> 11:41:44,868
但你要知道，你看到这个词发生的任何情况，对于所有其他输入词也是一样的。
But know that whatever you're seeing happen for this one word is going to happen for all of the other input words too.

7431
11:41:45,710 --> 11:41:46,948
那么这里发生了什么？
So what's going on here?

7432
11:41:47,278 --> 11:41:49,412
好的，我们从一些输入词开始。
Well, we start with some input word.

7433
11:41:49,774 --> 11:41:57,024
这个输入词进入神经网络，输出是希望得到某种关于输入词的编码表示，
That input word goes into the neural network, and the output is hopefully some encoded representation of the input word,

7434
11:41:57,230 --> 11:42:02,628
即我们在生成输出时需要了解的、与输入词相关的相关信息。
the information we need to know about the input word that's going to be relevant to us as we're generating the output.

7435
11:42:03,278 --> 11:42:07,140
因为我们独立处理每个词，所以很容易并行化。
And because we're doing this each word independently, it's easy to parallelize.

7436
11:42:07,264 --> 11:42:11,748
在将这个词通过神经网络之前，我们不需要等待前一个词。
We don't have to wait for the previous word before we run this word through the neural network.

7437
11:42:12,782 --> 11:42:16,544
但是尝试并行化整个过程时，我们失去了什么？
But what did we lose in this process by trying to parallelize this whole thing?

7438
11:42:16,782 --> 11:42:19,264
嗯，我们失去了对词语顺序的所有概念。
Well, we've lost all notion of word ordering.

7439
11:42:19,664 --> 11:42:21,184
词语的顺序很重要。
The order of words is important.

7440
11:42:21,390 --> 11:42:27,172
“福尔摩斯把书给华生”这句话的意思与“华生把书给福尔摩斯”完全不同。
The sentence Sherlock Holmes gave the book to Watson has a different meaning than Watson gave the book to Sherlock Holmes.

7441
11:42:27,504 --> 11:42:30,692
所以我们想要记录关于词语位置的信息。
And so we want to keep track of that information about word position.

7442
11:42:31,406 --> 11:42:38,660
在循环神经网络中，这会自动发生，因为我们可以让每个词一个接一个地通过神经网络，获取隐藏状态，
In the recurrent neural network, that happened for us automatically, because we could run each word one at a time through the neural network, get the hidden state,

7443
11:42:38,864 --> 11:42:41,348
并将其传递到下一次神经网络运行中。
pass it on to the next run of the neural network.

7444
11:42:41,646 --> 11:42:48,100
但在 Transformer 中情况并非如此，因为每个词都是独立处理的。
But that's not the case here with the transformer, where each word is being processed independent of all of the other ones.

7445
11:42:49,070 --> 11:42:51,104
那么我们要怎么做才能解决这个问题呢？
So what are we going to do to try to solve that problem?

7446
11:42:51,470 --> 11:42:56,644
我们可以采取的方法之一是给输入词添加某种位置编码。
One thing we can do is add some kind of positional encoding to the input word.

7447
11:42:57,038 --> 11:43:02,144
位置编码是一个表示词在句子中位置的向量。
The positional encoding is some vector that represents the position of the word in the sentence.

7448
11:43:02,702 --> 11:43:04,868
这就是第一个词，第二个词，第三个词，以此类推。
This is the first word, the second word, the third word, and so forth.

7449
11:43:05,230 --> 11:43:07,396
我们要把这个加到输入词上，
We're going to add that to the input word,

7450
11:43:08,078 --> 11:43:12,544
这样得到的结果就是一个包含多个信息片段的向量。
and the result of that is going to be a vector that captures multiple pieces of information.

7451
11:43:12,814 --> 11:43:16,708
它既包含了输入词本身，也包含了它在句子中出现的位置。
It captures the input word itself as well as where in the sentence it appears.

7452
11:43:17,422 --> 11:43:24,704
这样我们就可以把这个相加的结果，也就是输入词和位置编码的相加结果，传给神经网络。
The result of that is we can pass the output of that addition, the addition of the input word and the positional encoding into the neural network.

7453
11:43:24,942 --> 11:43:32,864
这样神经网络就知道这个词以及它在句子中的位置，并能利用这两个信息来决定如何最好地
That way the neural network knows the word and where it appears in the sentence and can use both of those pieces of information to determine how best to

7454
11:43:32,864 --> 11:43:37,092
在最后的编码表示中体现出这个词的含义。
represent the meaning of that word in the encoded representation at the end of it.

7455
11:43:38,222 --> 11:43:46,660
除了我们目前有的这些内容，即位置编码和这个前馈神经网络，我们还要增加一个额外的组件，
In addition to what we have here, in addition to the positional encoding and this feed-forward neural network, we're also going to add one additional component,

7456
11:43:47,054 --> 11:43:49,348
那就是自注意力步骤。
which is going to be a self-attention step.

7457
11:43:49,934 --> 11:43:57,664
这将是注意力机制，让我们去关注其他的输入词，因为一个输入词的含义或解释可能会
This is going to be attention where we're paying attention to the other input words, because the meaning or interpretation of an input word might

7458
11:43:57,664 --> 11:44:00,544
也取决于输入中的其他词。
vary depending on the other words in the input as well.

7459
11:44:00,814 --> 11:44:10,180
因此，我们将允许输入的每个词决定它应该关注哪些其他输入词，从而决定其编码表示。
And so we're going to allow each word in the input to decide what other words in the input it should pay attention to in order to decide on its encoded representation.

7460
11:44:10,766 --> 11:44:20,836
这将让我们能为每个词获得更好的编码表示，因为词是由它们的上下文、周围的词以及它们在特定语境中的用法来定义的。
And that's going to allow us to get a better encoded representation for each word, because words are defined by their context, by the words around them and how they're used in that particular context.

7461
11:44:21,422 --> 11:44:30,212
事实上，这种自注意力非常有价值，以至于 Transformer 经常会同时使用多个不同的自注意力层，
This kind of self-attention is so valuable, in fact, that oftentimes the transformer will use multiple different self-attention layers at the same time

7462
11:44:30,510 --> 11:44:35,716
让这个模型能够同时关注输入的多个方面。
to allow for this model to be able to pay attention to multiple facets of the input at the same time.

7463
11:44:36,398 --> 11:44:41,540
我们称之为多头注意力，其中每个注意力头可以关注不同的内容。
And we call this multi-headed attention, where each attention head can pay attention to something different.

7464
